\c 3
\s1 The Sons of Aaron
\r \ref Leviticus 10:1–7|LEV 10:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb This|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb is the account|תּוֹלְדֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and Moses|וּמֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb at the time|בְּי֗וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb Sinai.|סִינָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb These|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּֽנֵי־\rb* \rb of Aaron:|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb Nadab|נָדָ֑ב\rb* \rb the firstborn,|הַבְּכ֣וֹר׀\rb* \rb then Abihu,|וַאֲבִיה֕וּא\rb* \rb Eleazar,|אֶלְעָזָ֖ר\rb* \rb and Ithamar.|וְאִיתָמָֽר׃\rb* \v 3 \rb These|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb were Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |שְׁמוֹת֙\rb* \rb sons,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the anointed|הַמְּשֻׁחִ֑ים\rb* \rb priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were ordained|מִלֵּ֥א\rb*\rb |יָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb to serve as priests.|לְכַהֵֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Nadab|נָדָ֣ב\rb* \rb and Abihu, however,|וַאֲבִיה֣וּא\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb in the presence of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb when they offered|בְּֽהַקְרִבָם֩\rb* \rb unauthorized|זָרָ֜ה\rb*\f + \fr 3:4 \ft Or \fqa strange\f* \rb fire|אֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Sinai.|סִינַ֔י\rb* \rb And since they had|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb sons,|וּבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb only Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָר֙\rb* \rb and Ithamar|וְאִ֣יתָמָ֔ר\rb* \rb served as priests|וַיְכַהֵ֤ן\rb* \rb during|עַל־\rb* \rb the lifetime|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of their father|אֲבִיהֶֽם׃פ\rb* \rb Aaron.|אַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb*
\s1 The Duties of the Levites
\p \v 5 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 6 \rb “Bring|הַקְרֵב֙\rb* \rb the tribe|מַטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and present|וְֽהַעֲמַדְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb to assist him.|וְשֵׁרְת֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb They are to perform|וְשָׁמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb duties for him|מִשְׁמַרְתּ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |מִשְׁמֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb and for the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb attending|לַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the service|עֲבֹדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the tabernacle.|הַמִּשְׁכָּֽן׃\rb* \v 8 \rb They shall take care of|וְשָׁמְר֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the furnishings|כְּלֵי֙\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb fulfill obligations|מִשְׁמֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb for the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb by attending|לַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the service|עֲבֹדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the tabernacle.|הַמִּשְׁכָּֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Assign|וְנָתַתָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb to Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and his sons;|וּלְבָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb they|הֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb have been given exclusively|נְתוּנִ֨ם\rb*\rb |נְתוּנִ֥ם\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 3:9 \ft Most MT manuscripts; some MT manuscripts, SP, and LXX (see also \ref Numbers 8:16|NUM 8:16\ref*) \fqa to Me\f* \rb from among|מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 10 \rb So|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb you shall appoint|תִּפְקֹ֔ד\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָיו֙\rb* \rb to carry out|וְשָׁמְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the duties of the priesthood;|כְּהֻנָּתָ֑ם\rb* \rb but any outsider|וְהַזָּ֥ר\rb* \rb who approaches the tabernacle|הַקָּרֵ֖ב\rb* \rb must be put to death.”|יוּמָֽת׃פ\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Again the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 12 \rb “Behold,|הִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb I|וַאֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb have taken|לָקַ֣חְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb from among|מִתּוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb the children|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֧חַת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb*\rb |בְּכ֛וֹר\rb* \rb firstborn|פֶּ֥טֶר\rb* \rb Israelite|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb from the womb.|רֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb The Levites|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \rb belong|וְהָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb to Me,|לִ֖י\rb* \v 13 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכוֹר֒\rb* \rb are Mine.|לִי֮\rb* \rb On the day|בְּיוֹם֩\rb* \rb I struck down|הַכֹּתִ֨י\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb firstborn|בְּכ֜וֹר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb I consecrated|הִקְדַּ֨שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb to Myself|לִ֤י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכוֹר֙\rb* \rb in Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb both man|מֵאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|עַד־\rb* \rb beast.|בְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb They are|יִהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb Mine;|לִ֥י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Numbering of the Levites
\p \v 14 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of Sinai,|סִינַ֖י\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 15 \rb “Number|פְּקֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |לֵוִ֔י\rb* \rb by their families|אֲבֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb and clans.|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb You are to count|תִּפְקְדֵֽם׃\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֛ר\rb* \rb a month|חֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb old|מִבֶּן־\rb* \rb or more.”|וָמַ֖עְלָה\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb numbered|וַיִּפְקֹ֥ד\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb according to|עַל־\rb* \rb the word|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb he had been commanded.|צֻוָּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb These|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb were|וַיִּֽהְיוּ־\rb* \rb the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִ֖י\rb* \rb by name:|בִּשְׁמֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb Gershon,|גֵּרְשׁ֕וֹן\rb* \rb Kohath,|וּקְהָ֖ת\rb* \rb and Merari.|וּמְרָרִֽי׃\rb* \v 18 \rb These|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb were the names|שְׁמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּֽנֵי־\rb* \rb of Gershon|גֵרְשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb by their clans:|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb Libni|לִבְנִ֖י\rb* \rb and Shimei.|וְשִׁמְעִֽי׃\rb* \v 19 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Kohath|קְהָ֖ת\rb* \rb by their clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb were Amram,|עַמְרָ֣ם\rb* \rb Izhar,|וְיִצְהָ֔ר\rb* \rb Hebron,|חֶבְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb and Uzziel.|וְעֻזִּיאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 20 \rb And the sons|וּבְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Merari|מְרָרִ֛י\rb* \rb by their clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb were Mahli|מַחְלִ֣י\rb* \rb and Mushi.|וּמוּשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb These|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb were|הֵ֛ם\rb* \rb the clans|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Levites,|הַלֵּוִ֖י\rb* \rb according to their families.|אֲבֹתָֽם׃\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֥ית\rb*
\s1 The Gershonites
\r \ref Numbers 4:21–28|NUM 4:21-28\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 23:7–11|1CH 23:7-11\ref*)
\p \v 21 \rb From Gershon came|לְגֵ֣רְשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb the Libnite|הַלִּבְנִ֔י\rb* \rb clan|מִשְׁפַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb and the Shimeite|הַשִּׁמְעִ֑י\rb* \rb clan;|וּמִשְׁפַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb these|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb*\rb |הֵ֔ם\rb* \rb were the Gershonite|הַגֵּרְשֻׁנִּֽי׃\rb* \rb clans.|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֖ת\rb* \v 22 \rb The number|פְּקֻדֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |בְּמִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the males|זָכָ֔ר\rb* \rb a month|חֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb old|מִבֶּן־\rb* \rb or more|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb was|פְּקֻ֣דֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb 7,500.|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֽוֹת׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb The Gershonite|הַגֵּרְשֻׁנִּ֑י\rb* \rb clans|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֖ת\rb* \rb were to camp|יַחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb on the west,|יָֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb behind|אַחֲרֵ֧י\rb* \rb the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ן\rb* \v 24 \rb and the leader|וּנְשִׂ֥יא\rb* \rb of the families|בֵֽית־\rb*\rb |אָ֖ב\rb* \rb of the Gershonites|לַגֵּרְשֻׁנִּ֑י\rb* \rb was Eliasaph|אֶלְיָסָ֖ף\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Lael.|לָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb The duties|וּמִשְׁמֶ֤רֶת\rb* \rb of the Gershonites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |גֵרְשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb at the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb were the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb and tent,|וְהָאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb its covering,|מִכְסֵ֕הוּ\rb* \rb the curtain|וּמָסַ֕ךְ\rb* \rb for the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 26 \rb the curtains|וְקַלְעֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the courtyard,|הֶֽחָצֵ֗ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the curtain|מָסַךְ֙\rb* \rb for the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the courtyard|הֶֽחָצֵ֔ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb surrounds|עַל־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ן\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and altar,|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*\rb |סָבִ֑יב\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and the cords—|מֵֽיתָרָ֔יו\rb* \rb all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the service for these items.|עֲבֹדָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\s1 The Kohathites
\r \ref Numbers 4:1–20|NUM 4:1-20\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 23:12–20|1CH 23:12-20\ref*)
\p \v 27 \rb From Kohath came|וְלִקְהָ֗ת\rb* \rb the clans|מִשְׁפַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb of the Amramites,|הַֽעַמְרָמִי֙\rb* \rb the Izharites,|הַיִּצְהָרִ֔י\rb* \rb the Hebronites,|הַֽחֶבְרֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb and the Uzzielites;|הָֽעָזִּיאֵלִ֑י\rb* \rb these|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb*\rb |הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb were the clans|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Kohathites.|הַקְּהָתִֽי׃\rb* \v 28 \rb The number|בְּמִסְפַּר֙\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the males|זָכָ֔ר\rb* \rb a month|חֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb old|מִבֶּן־\rb* \rb or more|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb was 8,600.|שְׁמֹנַ֤ת\rb*\f + \fr 3:28 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa 8,300\ft ; see the total in verse 39.\f*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb They were responsible for|שֹׁמְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the duties|מִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb of the sanctuary.|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb The clans|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Kohathites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |קְהָ֖ת\rb* \rb were to camp|יַחֲנ֑וּ\rb* \rb on|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb the south|תֵּימָֽנָה׃\rb* \rb side|יֶ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \v 30 \rb and the leader|וּנְשִׂ֥יא\rb* \rb of the families|בֵֽית־\rb*\rb |אָ֖ב\rb* \rb of the Kohathites|הַקְּהָתִ֑י\rb* \rb was Elizaphan|אֶלִיצָפָ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 3:30 \fqa Elizaphan \ft is a variant of \fqa Elzaphan\ft ; see \ref Exodus 6:22|EXO 6:22\ref* and Leviticus 10:4.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Uzziel.|עֻזִּיאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb Their duties|וּמִשְׁמַרְתָּ֗ם\rb* \rb were the ark,|הָאָרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb the table,|וְהַשֻּׁלְחָן֙\rb* \rb the lampstand,|וְהַמְּנֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb the altars,|וְהַֽמִּזְבְּחֹ֔ת\rb* \rb the articles|וּכְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb used|יְשָׁרְת֖וּ\rb* \rb with them,|בָּהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and the curtain—|וְהַ֨מָּסָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the service for these items.|עֲבֹדָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb The chief|וּנְשִׂיא֙\rb* \rb of the leaders|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלֵּוִ֔י\rb* \rb was Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֖ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb the priest;|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb he oversaw|פְּקֻדַּ֕ת\rb* \rb those responsible for|שֹׁמְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the duties|מִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb of the sanctuary.|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*
\s1 The Merarites
\r \ref Numbers 4:29–33|NUM 4:29-33\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 23:21–23|1CH 23:21-23\ref*)
\p \v 33 \rb From Merari came|לִמְרָרִ֕י\rb* \rb the clans|מִשְׁפַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb of the Mahlites|הַמַּחְלִ֔י\rb* \rb and Mushites;|הַמּוּשִׁ֑י\rb*\rb |וּמִשְׁפַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb these|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb*\rb |הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb were the Merarite|מְרָרִֽי׃\rb* \rb clans.|מִשְׁפְּחֹ֥ת\rb* \v 34 \rb The number|וּפְקֻדֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |בְּמִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the males|זָכָ֔ר\rb* \rb a month|חֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb old|מִבֶּן־\rb* \rb or more|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb was 6,200.|שֵׁ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb The leader|וּנְשִׂ֤יא\rb* \rb of the families|בֵֽית־\rb*\rb |אָב֙\rb* \rb of the Merarites|מְרָרִ֔י\rb*\rb |לְמִשְׁפְּחֹ֣ת\rb* \rb was Zuriel|צוּרִיאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abihail;|אֲבִיחָ֑יִל\rb* \rb they were to camp|יַחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb on|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the north|צָפֹֽנָה׃\rb* \rb side|יֶ֧רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the tabernacle.|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ן\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb The duties|מִשְׁמֶרֶת֮\rb* \rb assigned|וּפְקֻדַּ֣ת\rb* \rb to the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Merari|מְרָרִי֒\rb* \rb were the tabernacle’s|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֔ן\rb* \rb frames,|קַרְשֵׁי֙\rb* \rb crossbars,|וּבְרִיחָ֖יו\rb* \rb posts,|וְעַמֻּדָ֣יו\rb* \rb bases,|וַאֲדָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb its equipment—|כֵּלָ֔יו\rb* \rb all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the service for these items,|עֲבֹדָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 37 \rb as well as the posts|וְעַמֻּדֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the surrounding|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb courtyard|הֶחָצֵ֛ר\rb* \rb with their bases,|וְאַדְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb tent pegs,|וִיתֵדֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and ropes.|וּמֵֽיתְרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\s1 Moses and Aaron
\p \v 38 \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֣ה׀\rb* \rb Aaron,|וְאַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and Aaron’s sons|וּבָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb were to camp|וְהַחֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb to the east|קֵ֣דְמָה\rb* \rb of the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֡ן\rb* \rb toward the sunrise,|מִזְרָ֜חָה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֩\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹֽהֶל־\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵ֨ד׀\rb* \rb They were to perform|שֹֽׁמְרִים֙\rb* \rb the duties|מִשְׁמֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּ֔שׁ\rb* \rb as a service|לְמִשְׁמֶ֖רֶת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb on behalf of the Israelites;|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb but any outsider|וְהַזָּ֥ר\rb* \rb who approached the sanctuary|הַקָּרֵ֖ב\rb* \rb was to be put to death.|יוּמָֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb The total|כָּל־\rb* \rb number|פְּקוּדֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְׄאַׄהֲׄרֹ֛ׄןׄ\rb* \rb counted|פָּקַ֨ד\rb* \rb by their clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb command,|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb including all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the males|זָכָר֙\rb* \rb a month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb old|מִבֶּן־\rb* \rb or more,|וָמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb was 22,000.|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Redemption of the Firstborn
\p \v 40 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Number|פְּקֹ֨ד\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb firstborn|בְּכֹ֤ר\rb* \rb male|זָכָר֙\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb a month|חֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb old|מִבֶּן־\rb* \rb or more,|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb and list|וְשָׂ֕א\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |מִסְפַּ֥ר\rb* \rb their names.|שְׁמֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 41 \rb You are to take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֨\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֥ם\rb* \rb for Me—|לִי֙\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD—|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and the livestock|בֶּהֱמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֔וֹר\rb* \rb of the livestock|בְּבֶהֱמַ֖ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites.”|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 42 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb numbered|וַיִּפְקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |בִּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb him.|אֹת֑וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \v 43 \rb The total|כָל־\rb* \rb number|לִפְקֻדֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb of the firstborn|בְּכ֨וֹר\rb* \rb males|זָכָ֜ר\rb* \rb a month|חֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb old|מִבֶּן־\rb* \rb or more,|וָמַ֖עְלָה\rb* \rb listed|בְּמִסְפַּ֥ר\rb* \rb by name,|שֵׁמ֛וֹת\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb 22,273.|שְׁנַ֤יִם\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתָֽיִם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 44 \rb Again the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 45 \rb “Take|קַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb in place|תַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכוֹר֙\rb*\rb |בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the livestock|בֶּהֱמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb in place|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb of their livestock.|בְּהֶמְתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb The Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb belong|וְהָיוּ־\rb* \rb to Me;|לִ֥י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 46 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb To redeem|פְּדוּיֵ֣י\rb* \rb the 273|הַשְּׁלֹשָׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְהַשִּׁבְעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְהַמָּאתָ֑יִם\rb* \rb firstborn|מִבְּכ֖וֹר\rb* \rb Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb who outnumber|הָעֹֽדְפִים֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the Levites,|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \v 47 \rb you are to collect|וְלָקַחְתָּ֗\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֧שֶׁת\rb*\rb |חֲמֵ֛שֶׁת\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 3:47 \fqa 5 shekels \ft is approximately 2 ounces or 57 grams.\f* \rb for each one,|לַגֻּלְגֹּ֑לֶת\rb* \rb according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*\rb |תִּקָּ֔ח\rb* \rb shekel|בְּשֶׁ֤קֶל\rb* \rb of twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb gerahs.|גֵּרָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 3:47 \fqa 20 gerahs \ft is equivalent to one shekel (approximately 0.4 ounces or 11.4 grams).\f* \rb |הַשָּֽׁקֶל׃\rb*\v 48 \rb Give|וְנָתַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb to Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb as the redemption price|פְּדוּיֵ֕י\rb* \rb for the excess|הָעֹדְפִ֖ים\rb* \rb among the Israelites.”|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 49 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb collected|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the redemption|הַפִּדְי֑וֹם\rb*\rb |מֵאֵת֙\rb* \rb money|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb from those in excess|הָעֹ֣דְפִ֔ים\rb* \rb of|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the number redeemed|פְּדוּיֵ֥י\rb* \rb by the Levites.|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \v 50 \rb |מֵאֵ֗ת\rb* \rb He collected|לָקַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the money|הַכָּ֑סֶף\rb* \rb from the firstborn|בְּכ֛וֹר\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites:|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb 1,365|חֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |וְשִׁשִּׁ֜ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֛וֹת\rb*\rb |וָאֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb shekels,|בְּשֶׁ֥קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 3:50 \fqa 1,365 shekels \ft is approximately 34.3 pounds or 15.6 kilograms.\f* \rb according to the sanctuary shekel.|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \v 51 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb the redemption|הַפְּדֻיִ֛ם\rb* \rb money|כֶּ֧סֶף\rb* \rb to Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּלְבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb in obedience to|עַל־\rb* \rb the word|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb him.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*
\c 4
\s1 The Duties of the Kohathites
\r \ref Numbers 3:27–32|NUM 3:27-32\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 23:12–20|1CH 23:12-20\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Take|נָשֹׂ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a census|רֹאשׁ֙\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Kohathites|קְהָ֔ת\rb* \rb among|מִתּ֖וֹךְ\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Levites|לֵוִ֑י\rb* \rb by their clans|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and families,|אֲבֹתָֽם׃\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \v 3 \rb men from thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |מִבֶּ֨ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb*\rb |וָמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb to|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb years old—|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who is qualified|בָּא֙\rb* \rb to serve|לַצָּבָ֔א\rb*\rb |לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb in the work|מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb* \rb at the Tent|בְּאֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb This|זֹ֛את\rb* \rb service|עֲבֹדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Kohathites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |קְהָ֖ת\rb* \rb at the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb regards the most|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb holy things.|הַקֳּדָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Whenever the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb sets out,|בִּנְסֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָיו֙\rb* \rb are to go in,|וּבָ֨א\rb* \rb take down|וְהוֹרִ֕דוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the veil|פָּרֹ֣כֶת\rb* \rb of the curtain,|הַמָּסָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb and cover|וְכִ֨סּוּ־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָעֵדֻֽת׃\rb*\f + \fr 4:5 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\f* \rb with it.|בָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \v 6 \rb They are to place|וְנָתְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb over|עָלָ֗יו\rb* \rb this a covering|כְּסוּי֙\rb*\rb |ע֣וֹר\rb* \rb of fine leather,|תַּ֔חַשׁ\rb*\f + \fr 4:6 \ft Possibly the hides of large aquatic mammals; also in verses 8, 10, 11, 12, 14, and 25; see \ref Exodus 25:5|EXO 25:5\ref*.\f* \rb spread|וּפָרְשׂ֧וּ\rb* \rb a solid|כְּלִ֛יל\rb* \rb blue|תְּכֵ֖לֶת\rb* \rb cloth|בֶֽגֶד־\rb* \rb over it,|מִלְמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb and insert|וְשָׂמ֖וּ\rb* \rb its poles.|בַּדָּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Over|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the table|שֻׁלְחַ֣ן\rb* \rb of the Presence|הַפָּנִ֗ים\rb* \rb they are to spread|יִפְרְשׂוּ֮\rb* \rb a blue|תְּכֵלֶת֒\rb* \rb cloth|בֶּ֣גֶד\rb* \rb and place|וְנָתְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb the plates|הַקְּעָרֹ֤ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and cups|הַכַּפֹּת֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb on it,|עָ֠לָיו\rb* \rb along with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the bowls|הַמְּנַקִּיֹּ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and pitchers|קְשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb for the drink offering.|הַנָּ֑סֶךְ\rb* \rb The regular|הַתָּמִ֖יד\rb* \rb bread|וְלֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb offering is to remain|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb on it.|עָלָ֥יו\rb* \v 8 \rb And they shall spread|וּפָרְשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb a scarlet|תּוֹלַ֣עַת\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb cloth|בֶּ֚גֶד\rb* \rb over them,|עֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb cover|וְכִסּ֣וּ\rb* \rb them|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb with|בְּמִכְסֵ֖ה\rb* \rb fine leather,|תָּ֑חַשׁ\rb*\rb |ע֣וֹר\rb* \rb and insert|וְשָׂמ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the poles.|בַּדָּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb They are to take|וְלָקְח֣וּ׀\rb* \rb a blue|תְּכֵ֗לֶת\rb* \rb cloth|בֶּ֣גֶד\rb* \rb and cover|וְכִסּ֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lampstand|מְנֹרַ֤ת\rb* \rb used for light,|הַמָּאוֹר֙\rb* \rb together|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with its lamps,|נֵ֣רֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb wick trimmers,|מַלְקָחֶ֖יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and trays,|מַחְתֹּתֶ֑יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb as well as the jars|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of oil|שַׁמְנָ֔הּ\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to supply|יְשָׁרְתוּ־\rb* \rb it.|לָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |בָּהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Then they shall wrap|וְנָתְנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb it|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils|כֵּלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb inside|אֶל־\rb* \rb a covering|מִכְסֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of fine leather|תָּ֑חַשׁ\rb*\rb |ע֣וֹר\rb* \rb and put|וְנָתְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the carrying frame.|הַמּֽוֹט׃\rb*
