\p \v 23 \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb shall write|וְ֠כָתַב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb curses|הָאָלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb on a scroll|בַּסֵּ֑פֶר\rb* \rb and wash them off|וּמָחָ֖ה\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the bitter|הַמָּרִֽים׃\rb* \rb water.|מֵ֥י\rb* \v 24 \rb He is to have the woman|הָ֣אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb drink|וְהִשְׁקָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bitter|הַמָּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb water|מֵ֥י\rb* \rb that brings a curse,|הַמְאָֽרֲרִ֑ים\rb* \rb and it|הַמַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb will enter|וּבָ֥אוּ\rb* \rb her|בָ֛הּ\rb* \rb and may cause her bitter|לְמָרִֽים׃\rb* \rb suffering.|הַֽמְאָרֲרִ֖ים\rb* \v 25 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb shall take|וְלָקַ֤ח\rb* \rb from her|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb the grain offering|מִנְחַ֣ת\rb* \rb for jealousy,|הַקְּנָאֹ֑ת\rb* \rb wave|וְהֵנִ֤יף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַמִּנְחָה֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and bring|וְהִקְרִ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \v 26 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֤ן\rb* \rb is to take a handful|וְקָמַ֨ץ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as a memorial portion|אַזְכָּ֣רָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and burn|וְהִקְטִ֖יר\rb* \rb it on the altar;|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חָה\rb* \rb after that|וְאַחַ֛ר\rb* \rb he is to have the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb drink|יַשְׁקֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the water.|הַמָּֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb When he has made her drink|וְהִשְׁקָ֣הּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the water,|הַמַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb if|אִֽם־\rb* \rb she has defiled herself|נִטְמְאָה֮\rb* \rb and been unfaithful|וַתִּמְעֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |מַ֣עַל\rb* \rb to her husband,|בְּאִישָׁהּ֒\rb* \rb then the water|הַמַּ֤יִם\rb* \rb that brings a curse|הַמְאָֽרֲרִים֙\rb* \rb will enter|וּבָ֨אוּ\rb* \rb her|בָ֜הּ\rb* \rb and cause bitter suffering;|לְמָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb her belly|בִטְנָ֔הּ\rb* \rb will swell,|וְצָבְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb her thigh|יְרֵכָ֑הּ\rb* \rb will shrivel,|וְנָפְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and she will become|וְהָיְתָ֧ה\rb*\rb |הָאִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb accursed|לְאָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb among|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb her people.|עַמָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 28 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb defiled herself|נִטְמְאָה֙\rb* \rb and is clean,|וּטְהֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb she|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb will be unaffected|וְנִקְּתָ֖ה\rb* \rb and able to conceive|וְנִזְרְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb children.|זָֽרַע׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of jealousy|הַקְּנָאֹ֑ת\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb goes astray|תִּשְׂטֶ֥ה\rb* \rb and defiles herself|וְנִטְמָֽאָה׃\rb* \rb while under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb her husband’s authority,|אִישָׁ֖הּ\rb* \v 30 \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb a feeling|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of jealousy|קִנְאָ֖ה\rb* \rb comes over|תַּעֲבֹ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָלָ֛יו\rb* \rb a husband|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb and he suspects|וְקִנֵּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his wife.|אִשְׁתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb He is to have the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb stand|וְהֶעֱמִ֤יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb is to apply|וְעָ֤שָׂה\rb* \rb to her|לָהּ֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb law.|הַתּוֹרָ֖ה\rb* \v 31 \rb The husband|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb will be free|וְנִקָּ֥ה\rb* \rb from guilt,|מֵעָוֺ֑ן\rb* \rb but the|הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb woman|וְהָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb shall bear|תִּשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb her|אֶת־\rb* \rb iniquity.”|עֲוֺנָֽהּ׃פ\rb*
\c 6
\s1 The Nazirite Vow
\r \ref Judges 13:1–25|JDG 13:1-25\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Speak|דַּבֵּר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb them that|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb if|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb makes a special|יַפְלִא֙\rb* \rb vow,|לִנְדֹּר֙\rb* \rb the vow|נֶ֣דֶר\rb* \rb of a Nazirite,|נָזִ֔יר\rb*\f + \fr 6:2 \fqa Nazirite \ft means \fqa one separated \ft or \fqa one consecrated\ft .\f* \rb to separate himself|לְהַזִּ֖יר\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb he is to abstain|יַזִּ֔יר\rb* \rb from wine|מִיַּ֤יִן\rb* \rb and strong drink.|וְשֵׁכָר֙\rb* \rb He must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb drink|יִשְׁתֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb vinegar|חֹ֥מֶץ\rb* \rb made from wine|יַ֛יִן\rb*\rb |וְחֹ֥מֶץ\rb* \rb or strong drink,|שֵׁכָ֖ר\rb* \rb and he must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb drink|יִשְׁתֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb grape|עֲנָבִים֙\rb* \rb juice|מִשְׁרַ֤ת\rb* \rb or eat|יֹאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb fresh|לַחִ֥ים\rb* \rb grapes|וַעֲנָבִ֛ים\rb* \rb or raisins.|וִיבֵשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \v 4 \rb All|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his separation,|נִזְר֑וֹ\rb* \rb he is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to eat|יֹאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb anything that comes from|יֵעָשֶׂ֜ה\rb* \rb the grapevine,|מִגֶּ֣פֶן\rb*\rb |הַיַּ֗יִן\rb* \rb not even the seeds|מֵחַרְצַנִּ֛ים\rb* \rb or|וְעַד־\rb* \rb skins.|זָ֖ג\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb For the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb period|יְמֵי֙\rb* \rb of his vow|נֶ֣דֶר\rb* \rb of separation,|נִזְר֔וֹ\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb razor|תַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb shall touch|יַעֲבֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb his head.|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb He must be|יִהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb holy|קָדֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the time|הַיָּמִ֜ם\rb* \rb of|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his separation|יַזִּ֤יר\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָה֙\rb* \rb is complete;|מְלֹ֨את\rb* \rb he must let the hair|שְׂעַ֥ר\rb* \rb of his head|רֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb* \rb grow|גַּדֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb long.|פֶּ֖רַע\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his separation|הַזִּיר֖וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb he must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go|יָבֹֽא׃\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb a dead|מֵ֖ת\rb* \rb body.|נֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \v 7 \rb Even if his father|לְאָבִ֣יו\rb* \rb or mother|וּלְאִמּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb or brother|לְאָחִיו֙\rb* \rb or sister|וּלְאַ֣חֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb should die,|בְּמֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb he is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to defile himself,|יִטַּמָּ֥א\rb* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the symbol of consecration|נֵ֥זֶר\rb* \rb to his God|אֱלֹהָ֖יו\rb* \rb is upon|עַל־\rb* \rb his head.|רֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Throughout the time|כֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his separation,|נִזְר֑וֹ\rb* \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is holy|קָדֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb someone suddenly|בְּפֶ֣תַע\rb*\rb |פִּתְאֹ֔ם\rb* \rb dies|יָמ֨וּת\rb*\rb |מֵ֤ת\rb* \rb in his presence|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and defiles|וְטִמֵּ֖א\rb* \rb his consecrated head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of hair,|נִזְר֑וֹ\rb* \rb he must shave|וְגִלַּ֤ח\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁוֹ֙\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of his cleansing—|טָהֳרָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb |יְגַלְּחֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb day.|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \v 10 \rb On the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֗י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb he must bring|יָבִא֙\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb turtledoves|תֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb young|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb pigeons|יוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 11 \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb is to offer|וְעָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּאת֙\rb*\f + \fr 6:11 \ft Or \fqa purification offering\ft ; here and throughout Numbers\f* \rb and the other|וְאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|לְעֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb to make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb for him,|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb because|מֵאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he has sinned|חָטָ֖א\rb* \rb by being in the presence|עַל־\rb* \rb of the dead body.|הַנָּ֑פֶשׁ\rb* \rb On that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb he must consecrate|וְקִדַּ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his head again.|רֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \v 12 \rb He must rededicate|וְהִזִּ֤יר\rb* \rb his time|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of separation|נִזְר֔וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and bring|וְהֵבִ֛יא\rb* \rb a year-old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שְׁנָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb male lamb|כֶּ֥בֶשׂ\rb* \rb as a guilt offering.|לְאָשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb But the preceding|הָרִאשֹׁנִים֙\rb* \rb days|וְהַיָּמִ֤ים\rb* \rb shall not be counted,|יִפְּל֔וּ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb his separation|נִזְרֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb was defiled.|טָמֵ֖א\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Now this|וְזֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the Nazirite|הַנָּזִ֑יר\rb* \rb when|בְּי֗וֹם\rb* \rb his time|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of separation|נִזְר֔וֹ\rb* \rb is complete:|מְלֹאת֙\rb* \rb He must be brought|יָבִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 14 \rb and he is to present|וְהִקְרִ֣יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an offering|קָרְבָּנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb of an|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb unblemished|תָמִ֤ים\rb* \rb year-old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שְׁנָת֨וֹ\rb* \rb male lamb|כֶּבֶשׂ֩\rb* \rb as a burnt offering,|לְעֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb an|אַחַ֧ת\rb* \rb unblemished|תְּמִימָ֖ה\rb* \rb year-old|בַּת־\rb*\rb |שְׁנָתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb female lamb|וְכַבְשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb as a sin offering,|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb* \rb and an|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb unblemished|תָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb ram|וְאַֽיִל־\rb* \rb as a peace offering—|לִשְׁלָמִֽים׃\rb*  \v 15 \rb together with their grain offerings|וּמִנְחָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and drink offerings—|וְנִסְכֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb*  \rb and a basket|וְסַ֣ל\rb* \rb of unleavened|מַצּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb cakes|חַלֹּת֙\rb* \rb made from fine flour|סֹ֤לֶת\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלֹ֣ת\rb* \rb with oil|בַּשֶּׁ֔מֶן\rb* \rb and unleavened|מַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb wafers|וּרְקִיקֵ֥י\rb* \rb coated|מְשֻׁחִ֣ים\rb* \rb with oil.|בַּשָּׁ֑מֶן\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb is to present all these|וְהִקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and make|וְעָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sin offering|חַטָּאת֖וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the burnt offering.|עֹלָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 17 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He shall also offer|יַעֲשֶׂ֨ה\rb* \rb the ram|הָאַ֜יִל\rb*\rb |זֶ֤בַח\rb* \rb as a peace offering|שְׁלָמִים֙\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb along with|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the basket|סַ֣ל\rb* \rb of unleavened bread.|הַמַּצּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to offer|וְעָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb the accompanying grain offering|מִנְחָת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and drink offering.|נִסְכּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then at the entrance|פֶּ֛תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb the Nazirite|הַנָּזִ֗יר\rb* \rb is to shave|וְגִלַּ֣ח\rb* \rb his consecrated|נִזְר֑וֹ\rb* \rb head,|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb take|וְלָקַ֗ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the hair,|שְׂעַר֙\rb*\rb |רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*\rb |נִזְר֔וֹ\rb* \rb and put|וְנָתַן֙\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb*\rb |זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb the peace offering.|הַשְּׁלָמִֽים׃\rb* \v 19 \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֨ח\rb* \rb the boiled|בְּשֵׁלָה֮\rb* \rb shoulder|הַזְּרֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the ram,|הָאַיִל֒\rb* \rb one|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb unleavened|מַצָּ֤ה\rb* \rb cake|וְֽחַלַּ֨ת\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the basket,|הַסַּ֔ל\rb* \rb and one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb unleavened|מַצָּ֖ה\rb* \rb wafer,|וּרְקִ֥יק\rb* \rb and put them|וְנָתַן֙\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the hands|כַּפֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the Nazirite|הַנָּזִ֔יר\rb* \rb who has just|אַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb shaved|הִֽתְגַּלְּח֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the hair of his consecration.|נִזְרֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 20 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֥ן׀\rb* \rb shall then wave|וְהֵנִיף֩\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֨ם\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָה֮\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb This|הוּא֙\rb* \rb is a holy|קֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb* \rb portion for the priest,|לַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb in addition to|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the breast|חֲזֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the wave offering|הַתְּנוּפָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb and the thigh|שׁ֣וֹק\rb* \rb that was presented.|הַתְּרוּמָ֑ה\rb* \rb After that,|וְאַחַ֛ר\rb* \rb the Nazirite|הַנָּזִ֖יר\rb* \rb may drink|יִשְׁתֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb wine.|יָֽיִן׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb This|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Nazirite|הַנָּזִיר֮\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb vows|יִדֹּר֒\rb* \rb his offering|קָרְבָּנ֤וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb his separation,|נִזְר֔וֹ\rb* \rb in addition to|מִלְּבַ֖ד\rb* \rb whatever else|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he can afford;|תַּשִּׂ֣יג\rb*\rb |יָד֑וֹ\rb*\rb |כְּפִ֤י\rb* \rb he must fulfill|יַעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb vow|נִדְרוֹ֙\rb* \rb he makes,|יִדֹּ֔ר\rb*\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb according to|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the law|תּוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of his separation.”|נִזְרֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\s1 Aaron’s Blessing
\p \v 22 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 23 \rb “Tell|דַּבֵּ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his sons:|בָּנָ֣יו\rb*\rb This is how you are to bless|תְבָרֲכ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Say|אָמ֖וֹר\rb* \rb to them:|לָהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 24 \rb ‘May the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb bless you|יְבָרֶכְךָ֥\rb*
\q2 \rb and keep you;|וְיִשְׁמְרֶֽךָ׃ס\rb*
\q1 \v 25 \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה׀\rb* \rb cause His face|פָּנָ֛יו\rb* \rb to shine|יָאֵ֨ר\rb* \rb upon you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and be gracious to you;|וִֽיחֻנֶּֽךָּ׃ס\rb*
\q1 \v 26 \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb lift up|יִשָּׂ֨א\rb* \rb His countenance|פָּנָיו֙\rb* \rb toward you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and give|וְיָשֵׂ֥ם\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb peace.’|שָׁלֽוֹם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb So they shall put|וְשָׂמ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will bless them.”|אֲבָרֲכֵֽם׃פ\rb*
\c 7
\s1 Offerings of Dedication
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb On the day|בְּיוֹם֩\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb finished|כַּלּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb setting up|לְהָקִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֗ן\rb* \rb he anointed|וַיִּמְשַׁ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb and consecrated|וַיְקַדֵּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb it|אֹתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its furnishings,|כֵּלָ֔יו\rb* \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its utensils.|כֵּלָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וַיִּמְשָׁחֵ֖ם\rb*\rb |וַיְקַדֵּ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And the leaders|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of their families,|אֲבֹתָ֑ם\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb presented an offering.|וַיַּקְרִ֙יבוּ֙\rb* \rb These men|הֵ֚ם\rb* \rb were the tribal|הַמַּטֹּ֔ת\rb*\rb |הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb leaders|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb who had supervised|הָעֹמְדִ֖ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the registration.|הַפְּקֻדִֽים׃\rb* \v 3 \rb They brought|וַיָּבִ֨יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as their offering|קָרְבָּנָ֜ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb covered|צָב֙\rb* \rb carts|עֶגְלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb and twelve|וּשְׁנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb oxen—|בָּקָ֔ר\rb*  \rb an ox|וְשׁ֣וֹר\rb* \rb from each leader|לְאֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb and a cart|עֲגָלָ֛ה\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb every two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb leaders—|הַנְּשִׂאִ֖ים\rb*  \rb and presented|וַיַּקְרִ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the tabernacle.|הַמִּשְׁכָּֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 5 \rb “Accept these gifts|קַ֚ח\rb* \rb from them,|מֵֽאִתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb that they may be|וְהָי֕וּ\rb* \rb used|לַעֲבֹ֕ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the work|עֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb And give|וְנָתַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Levites,|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb to each man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb according to|כְּפִ֥י\rb* \rb his service.”|עֲבֹדָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb the carts|הָעֲגָלֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and oxen|הַבָּקָ֑ר\rb* \rb and gave|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Levites.|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb |אֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb He gave|נָתַ֖ן\rb* \rb the Gershonites|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |גֵרְשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb carts|הָעֲגָלֹ֗ת\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and four|אַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb* \rb oxen,|הַבָּקָ֔ר\rb* \rb as their service|עֲבֹדָתָֽם׃\rb* \rb required,|כְּפִ֖י\rb* \v 8 \rb and|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb he gave|נָתַ֖ן\rb* \rb the Merarites|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |מְרָרִ֑י\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb carts|הָעֲגָלֹ֗ת\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and eight|שְׁמֹנַ֣ת\rb* \rb oxen,|הַבָּקָ֔ר\rb* \rb as their service|עֲבֹ֣דָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb required,|כְּפִי֙\rb* \rb all under the direction|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb of Ithamar|אִֽיתָמָ֔ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb the priest.|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \v 9 \rb But he did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb give any|נָתָ֑ן\rb* \rb to the Kohathites,|וְלִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |קְהָ֖ת\rb* \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they were to carry|יִשָּֽׂאוּ׃\rb* \rb on their|עֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb shoulders|בַּכָּתֵ֖ף\rb* \rb the holy objects|הַקֹּ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb for which they were responsible.|עֲבֹדַ֤ת\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb When|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb the altar was anointed,|הִמָּשַׁ֣ח\rb* \rb the leaders|הַנְּשִׂאִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb approached|וַיַּקְרִ֣יבוּ\rb* \rb with their offerings|קָרְבָּנָ֖ם\rb* \rb for its dedication|חֲנֻכַּ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb and|הַנְּשִׂיאִ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb presented them|וַיַּקְרִ֧יבוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb “Each day|לַיּ֗וֹם\rb*\rb |נָשִׂ֤יא\rb*\rb |אֶחָד֙\rb*\rb |לַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb leader|נָשִׂ֨יא\rb* \rb is to present|יַקְרִ֙יבוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his offering|קָרְבָּנָ֔ם\rb* \rb for the dedication|לַחֲנֻכַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of the altar.”|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb On the first|הָרִאשׁ֖וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb Nahshon|נַחְשׁ֥וֹן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Amminadab|עַמִּינָדָ֖ב\rb* \rb from the tribe|לְמַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb drew near|הַמַּקְרִ֛יב\rb* \rb with his offering.|קָרְבָּנ֑וֹ\rb* \v 13 \rb His offering|וְקָרְבָּנ֞וֹ\rb* \rb was one|אַחַ֗ת\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb platter|קַֽעֲרַת־\rb* \rb weighing|מִשְׁקָלָהּ֒\rb* \rb a hundred and thirty shekels,|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 7:13 \fqa 130 shekels \ft is approximately 3.3 pounds or 1.48 kilograms; here and throughout this chapter.\f* \rb |וּמֵאָה֮\rb*\rb and one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb bowl|מִזְרָ֤ק\rb* \rb weighing seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb shekels,|שֶׁ֖קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 7:13 \fqa 70 shekels \ft is approximately 1.76 pounds or 797.8 grams; here and throughout this chapter.\f* \rb both according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb shekel|בְּשֶׁ֣קֶל\rb* \rb and|שְׁנֵיהֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb filled with|מְלֵאִ֗ים\rb* \rb fine flour|סֹ֛לֶת\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלָ֥ה\rb* \rb with oil|בַשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb for a grain offering;|לְמִנְחָֽה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb one|אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb dish|כַּ֥ף\rb* \rb weighing ten shekels,|עֲשָׂרָ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 7:14 \fqa 10 shekels \ft is approximately 4 ounces or 114 grams; here and throughout this chapter.\f* \rb filled with|מְלֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb incense;|קְטֹֽרֶת׃\rb* \v 15 \rb one|אֶחָ֞ד\rb* \rb young|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֗ר\rb* \rb bull,|פַּ֣ר\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb ram,|אַ֧יִל\rb* \rb and one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb male lamb|כֶּֽבֶשׂ־\rb* \rb a year old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שְׁנָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb for a burnt offering;|לְעֹלָֽה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb male goat|שְׂעִיר־\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֥ים\rb* \rb for a sin offering;|לְחַטָּֽאת׃\rb* \v 17 \rb and a peace offering|הַשְּׁלָמִים֮\rb*\rb |וּלְזֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb of two|שְׁנַיִם֒\rb* \rb oxen,|בָּקָ֣ר\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb rams,|אֵילִ֤ם\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb male goats,|עַתּוּדִ֣ים\rb* \rb and five|חֲמִשָּׁ