\p \v 89 \rb When Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb entered|וּבְבֹ֨א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵד֮\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with the LORD,|אִתּוֹ֒\rb* \rb he heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֨ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the voice|הַקּ֜וֹל\rb* \rb speaking|מִדַּבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb from between|מִבֵּ֖ין\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִ֑ים\rb* \rb above|מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb the mercy seat|הַכַּפֹּ֙רֶת֙\rb*\f + \fr 7:89 \ft Or \fqa atonement cover\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb of the Testimony.|הָעֵדֻ֔ת\rb*\f + \fr 7:89 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\f* \rb Thus the LORD spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to him.|אֵלָֽיו׃פ\rb*
\c 8
\s1 The Lampstand
\r \ref Exodus 25:31–40|EXO 25:31-40\ref*; \ref Exodus 37:17–24|EXO 37:17-24\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Speak|דַּבֵּר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb him:|אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb ‘When you set up|בְּהַעֲלֹֽתְךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַנֵּרֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb lamps,|הַנֵּרֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb they are to light the area|יָאִ֖ירוּ\rb* \rb in front|מוּל֙\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the lampstand.’”|הַמְּנוֹרָ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb And Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb so;|כֵּן֙\rb* \rb he set up|הֶעֱלָ֖ה\rb* \rb the lamps|נֵרֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb facing|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front|מוּל֙\rb* \rb of the lampstand,|הַמְּנוֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb just as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb This is how|וְזֶ֨ה\rb* \rb the lampstand|הַמְּנֹרָה֙\rb* \rb was constructed:|מַעֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb* \rb it was made of hammered|מִקְשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb from|עַד־\rb* \rb its base|יְרֵכָ֥הּ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb its blossoms,|פִּרְחָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |הַמְּנֹרָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb fashioned|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִקְשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |הִ֑וא\rb* \rb according to the pattern|כַּמַּרְאֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had shown|הֶרְאָ֤ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb*
\s1 Cleansing the Levites
\p \v 5 \rb Again the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 6 \rb “Take|קַ֚ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb from among|מִתּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and make them ceremonially clean.|וְטִהַרְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb This is what|וְכֹֽה־\rb* \rb you must do|תַעֲשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb to cleanse them:|לְטַֽהֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb Sprinkle|הַזֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb with the water|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb of purification.|חַטָּ֑את\rb* \rb Have them shave|וְהֶעֱבִ֤ירוּ\rb*\rb |תַ֙עַר֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb their whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb bodies|בְּשָׂרָ֔ם\rb* \rb and wash|וְכִבְּס֥וּ\rb* \rb their clothes,|בִגְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and so purify themselves.|וְהִטֶּהָֽרוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then have them take|וְלָֽקְחוּ֙\rb* \rb a young bull|פַּ֣ר\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֔ר\rb* \rb with its grain offering|וּמִנְחָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֖לֶת\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלָ֣ה\rb* \rb with oil,|בַשָּׁ֑מֶן\rb* \rb and you are to take|תִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a second|שֵׁנִ֥י\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb young bull|וּפַר־\rb* \rb for a sin offering.|לְחַטָּֽאת׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Bring|וְהִקְרַבְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb and assemble|וְהִ֨קְהַלְתָּ֔\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֖ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 10 \rb You are to present|וְהִקְרַבְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and have the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lay|וְסָמְכ֧וּ\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb them.|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \v 11 \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb is to present|וְהֵנִיף֩\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֤ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָה֙\rb* \rb from the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְהָי֕וּ\rb* \rb so that they may perform|לַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the service|עֲבֹדַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּם֙\rb* \rb are to lay|יִסְמְכ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the heads|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the bulls,|הַפָּרִ֑ים\rb* \rb and offer|וַ֠עֲשֵׂה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֨ד\rb* \rb as a sin offering|חַטָּ֜את\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the other|הָאֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb as a burnt offering,|עֹלָה֙\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the Levites.|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb You are to have the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb stand|וְהַֽעֲמַדְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְלִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and his sons|בָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb and then present|וְהֵנַפְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb before the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb as a wave offering.|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \v 14 \rb In this way you shall separate|וְהִבְדַּלְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֖וֹךְ\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the rest of the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and the Levites|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \rb will belong|וְהָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb to Me.|לִ֖י\rb* \v 15 \rb After|וְאַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵן֙\rb* \rb you have cleansed|וְטִֽהַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and presented|וְהֵנַפְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb as a wave offering,|תְּנוּפָֽה׃\rb* \rb they|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb may come|יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to serve|לַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb at the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the Levites|הֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb have been wholly given|נְתֻנִ֨ים\rb*\rb |נְתֻנִ֥ים\rb* \rb to Me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb from among|מִתּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb I have taken|לָקַ֥חְתִּי\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb for Myself|לִֽי׃\rb* \rb in place of|תַּחַת֩\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who come first|פִּטְרַ֨ת\rb* \rb from the womb,|רֶ֜חֶם\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of all|כֹּל֙\rb* \rb the sons|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \v 17 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb firstborn|בְּכוֹר֙\rb* \rb male|בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb in Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb is Mine,|לִ֤י\rb* \rb both man|בָּאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and beast.|וּבַבְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb I set them apart|הִקְדַּ֥שְׁתִּי\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb for Myself|לִֽי׃\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֗וֹם\rb* \rb I struck down|הַכֹּתִ֤י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכוֹר֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \v 18 \rb But I have taken|וָאֶקַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֖וֹר\rb* \rb among the sons|בִּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 19 \rb And I have given|וָאֶתְּנָ֨ה\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb* \rb as a gift|נְתֻנִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb to Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and his sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb from among|מִתּוֹךְ֮\rb*\rb |וּלְבָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb to perform|לַעֲבֹ֞ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the service|עֲבֹדַ֤ת\rb* \rb for the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb at the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb and to make atonement|וּלְכַפֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb on their|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb behalf,|עַל־\rb* \rb so that no|וְלֹ֨א\rb* \rb plague|נֶ֔גֶף\rb* \rb will come|יִהְיֶ֜ה\rb* \rb against the Israelites|בִּבְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb when they|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb approach|בְּגֶ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb the sanctuary.”|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb So Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb* \rb Aaron,|וְאַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb* \rb and the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֥ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb with the Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* \rb everything|כְּ֠כֹל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֨ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |כֵּן־\rb* \rb they|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb should do.|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \v 21 \rb The Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb purified|וַיִּֽתְחַטְּא֣וּ\rb* \rb themselves and washed|וַֽיְכַבְּסוּ֙\rb* \rb their clothes,|בִּגְדֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb presented|וַיָּ֨נֶף\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb as a wave offering|תְּנוּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb also made atonement|וַיְכַפֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb for them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to cleanse them.|לְטַהֲרָֽם׃\rb* \v 22 \rb After|וְאַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb that,|כֵ֞ן\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to perform|לַעֲבֹ֤ד\rb* \rb their service|עֲבֹֽדָתָם֙\rb* \rb at the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְלִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and his sons.|בָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb Thus|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb they did|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb with the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֨ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*
\s1 Retirement for Levites
\p \v 23 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 24 \rb “This|זֹ֖את\rb* \rb applies|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to the Levites:|לַלְוִיִּ֑ם\rb* \rb Men twenty-five|חָמֵ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּן֩\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb or older|וָמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb shall enter|יָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb to perform|לִצְבֹ֣א\rb* \rb the service|צָבָ֔א\rb* \rb in the work|בַּעֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb at the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 25 \rb But at the age|וּמִבֶּן֙\rb* \rb of fifty,|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb they must retire|יָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb from performing|מִצְּבָ֣א\rb* \rb the work|הָעֲבֹדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb longer|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb serve.|יַעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb After that, they may assist|וְשֵׁרֵ֨ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their brothers|אֶחָ֜יו\rb* \rb in fulfilling|לִשְׁמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb their duties|מִשְׁמֶ֔רֶת\rb* \rb at the Tent|בְּאֹ֤הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵד֙\rb* \rb but they themselves are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to do|יַעֲבֹ֑ד\rb* \rb the work.|וַעֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb* \rb This is how|כָּ֛כָה\rb* \rb you are to assign|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb responsibilities|בְּמִשְׁמְרֹתָֽם׃פ\rb* \rb to the Levites.”|לַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb*
\c 9
\s1 The Second Passover
\r \ref Exodus 12:1–13|EXO 12:1-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the first|הָרִאשׁ֖וֹן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֜ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֨ה\rb* \rb after Israel had come out|לְצֵאתָ֨ם\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְמִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Sinai:|סִ֠ינַי\rb* \v 2 \rb “The Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to observe|וְיַעֲשׂ֧וּ\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפָּ֖סַח\rb* \rb at its appointed time.|בְּמוֹעֲדֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb You are to observe|תַּעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb at the appointed time,|בְּמוֹעֲד֑וֹ\rb* \rb at|בֵּ֧ין\rb* \rb twilight|הָֽעֲרְבַּ֛יִם\rb* \rb on the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבָּעָ֣ה\rb*\f + \fr 9:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa between the two evenings of the fourteenth\ft ; also in verses 5 and 11\f* \rb |עָשָֽׂר־\rb*\rb day|י֠וֹם\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֨דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb in accordance with|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb its statutes|חֻקֹּתָ֥יו\rb*\rb |וּכְכָל־\rb* \rb and ordinances.”|מִשְׁפָּטָ֖יו\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to observe|לַעֲשֹׂ֥ת\rb* \rb the Passover,|הַפָּֽסַח׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and they did so|וַיַּעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַפֶּ֡סַח\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Sinai,|סִינָ֑י\rb* \rb at|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb twilight|הָעַרְבַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb on the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבָּעָה֩\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֨ר\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the first|בָּרִאשׁ֡וֹן\rb* \rb month.|לַחֹ֛דֶשׁ\rb* \rb The Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb did|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb everything|כְּ֠כֹל\rb* \rb just as|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֤ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb But there were|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb some men|אֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb were|הָי֤וּ\rb* \rb unclean|טְמֵאִים֙\rb* \rb due to a dead body,|אָדָ֔ם\rb*\rb |לְנֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb so they could|יָכְל֥וּ\rb* \rb not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb observe|לַעֲשֹׂת־\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפֶּ֖סַח\rb* \rb on that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day.|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb And they came|וַֽיִּקְרְב֞וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |וְלִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb that same|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \v 7 \rb and said|וַ֠יֹּאמְרוּ\rb*\rb |הָאֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |הָהֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb to Moses,|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb “We|אֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb are unclean|טְמֵאִ֖ים\rb* \rb because of a dead body,|אָדָ֑ם\rb*\rb |לְנֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb but why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb should we be excluded|נִגָּרַ֗ע\rb* \rb from|לְבִלְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb presenting|הַקְרִ֜ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb offering|קָרְבַּ֤ן\rb* \rb with|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the other Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb at the appointed time?”|בְּמֹ֣עֲד֔וֹ\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb “Wait here|עִמְד֣וּ\rb* \rb until I find out|וְאֶשְׁמְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb commands|יְצַוֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb concerning you,”|לָכֶֽם׃פ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 10 \rb “Tell|דַּבֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites:|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb ‘When|כִּי־\rb* \rb any one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of you or|אוֹ֩\rb* \rb your descendants|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb is|יִהְיֶֽה־\rb* \rb unclean|טָמֵ֣א׀\rb* \rb because of a dead body,|לָנֶ֡פֶשׁ\rb* \rb or|א֚וֹ\rb* \rb is away|רְחֹקָ֜הׄ\rb* \rb on a journey,|בְדֶ֨רֶךְ\rb* \rb he may still observe|וְעָ֥שָׂה\rb* \rb the Passover|פֶ֖סַח\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb Such people are to observe|יַעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb at|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb twilight|הָעַרְבַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb on the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבָּעָ֨ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb day|י֛וֹם\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֜י\rb* \rb month.|בַּחֹ֨דֶשׁ\rb* \rb They are to eat the lamb,|יֹאכְלֻֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb together with|עַל־\rb* \rb unleavened bread|מַצּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb and bitter herbs;|וּמְרֹרִ֖ים\rb* \v 12 \rb they may not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb leave|יַשְׁאִ֤ירוּ\rb* \rb any of|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb it until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|בֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb or break|יִשְׁבְּרוּ־\rb* \rb any of its|ב֑וֹ\rb* \rb bones.|וְעֶ֖צֶם\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb They must observe|יַעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפֶּ֖סַח\rb* \rb according to all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb its statutes.|חֻקַּ֥ת\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb But if a man|וְהָאִישׁ֩\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is|ה֨וּא\rb* \rb ceremonially clean|טָה֜וֹר\rb* \rb and is|הָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb on a journey|וּבְדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb still fails|וְחָדַל֙\rb* \rb to observe|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the Passover,|הַפֶּ֔סַח\rb* \rb he must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb from his people,|מֵֽעַמֶּ֑יהָ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb he did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb present|הִקְרִיב֙\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb offering|קָרְבַּ֣ן\rb* \rb at its appointed time.|בְּמֹ֣עֲד֔וֹ\rb* \rb That|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb will bear|יִשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb the consequences of his sin.|חֶטְא֥וֹ\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a foreigner|גֵּ֗ר\rb* \rb dwelling|יָג֨וּר\rb* \rb among you|אִתְּכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb wants to observe|וְעָ֤שָֽׂה\rb* \rb the Passover|פֶ֙סַח֙\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb he is to do|יַעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb according to the Passover|הַפֶּ֛סַח\rb* \rb statute|כְּחֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb and its ordinances.|וּכְמִשְׁפָּט֖וֹ\rb* \rb You are to apply|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the same|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb statute|חֻקָּ֤ה\rb* \rb to both the foreigner|וְלַגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb and the native|וּלְאֶזְרַ֥ח\rb* \rb of the land.’”|הָאָֽרֶץ׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Cloud above the Tabernacle
\r \ref Exodus 40:34–38|EXO 40:34-38\ref*)
\p \v 15 \rb On the day that|וּבְיוֹם֙\rb* \rb the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֔ן\rb* \rb the Tent|לְאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb of the Testimony,|הָעֵדֻ֑ת\rb* \rb was set up,|הָקִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶֽעָנָן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb covered|כִּסָּ֤ה\rb* \rb it|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֔ן\rb* \rb and appeared|כְּמַרְאֵה־\rb* \rb like fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb above|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֛ן\rb* \rb from evening|וּבָעֶ֜רֶב\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֧ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning.|בֹּֽקֶר׃\rb* \v 16 \rb It remained|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb that way|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb continually;|תָמִ֔יד\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶעָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb would cover the tabernacle by day,|יְכַסֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*\f + \fr 9:16 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew does not include \fqa by day\f* \rb and at night|לָֽיְלָה׃\rb* \rb it would appear|וּמַרְאֵה־\rb* \rb like fire.|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \v 17 \rb Whenever|וּלְפִ֞י\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶֽעָנָן֙\rb* \rb was lifted|הֵעָלֹ֤ת\rb* \rb from above|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the Tent,|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb*\rb |וְאַ֣חֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb would set out,|יִסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb and wherever|וּבִמְק֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶֽעָנָ֔ן\rb*\rb |שָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb settled,|יִשְׁכָּן־\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb would camp.|יַחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \v 18 \rb At|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb command|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb set out,|יִסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb and at|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb command|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb they camped.|יַחֲנ֑וּ\rb* \rb As long as|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֗י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶעָנָ֛ן\rb* \rb remained|יִשְׁכֹּ֧ן\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the tabernacle,|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb they remained encamped.|יַחֲנֽוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Even when the cloud|הֶֽעָנָ֛ן\rb* \rb lingered|וּבְהַאֲרִ֧יךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb for many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb days,|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb kept|וְשָׁמְר֧וּ\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb charge|מִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb set out.|יִסָּֽעוּ׃\rb* \v 20 \rb Sometimes|וְיֵ֞שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶֽעָנָ֛ן\rb* \rb remained|יִהְיֶ֧ה\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \rb for only a few|מִסְפָּ֖ר\rb* \rb days,|יָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb and they would camp|יַחֲנ֔וּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb command|פִּ֤י\rb* \rb and set out|יִסָּֽעוּ׃\rb* \rb at|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb command.|פִּ֥י\rb* \v 21 \rb Sometimes|וְיֵ֞שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶֽעָנָן֙\rb* \rb remained|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb only from evening|מֵעֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning,|בֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb and when it|הֶֽעָנָ֛ן\rb* \rb lifted|וְנַעֲלָ֧ה\rb* \rb in the morning,|בַּבֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb they would set out.|וְנָסָ֑עוּ\rb* \rb Whether|א֚וֹ\rb* \rb it was by day|יוֹמָ֣ם\rb* \rb or by night,|וָלַ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb when the cloud|הֶעָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb was taken up,|וְנַעֲלָ֥ה\rb* \rb they would set out.|וְנָסָֽעוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Whether|אֽוֹ־\rb*\rb |אוֹ־\rb*\rb |יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb the cloud lingered|בְּהַאֲרִ֨יךְ\rb* \rb for two days,|יֹמַ֜יִם\rb* \rb a month,|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb or longer,|אוֹ־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb camped|יַחֲנ֥וּ\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb set out|יִסָּ֑עוּ\rb* \rb as long as the cloud|הֶעָנָ֤ן\rb* \rb remained|לִשְׁכֹּ֣ן\rb*\rb |עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the tabernacle;|הַמִּשְׁכָּן֙\rb* \rb but when it was lifted,|וּבְהֵעָלֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb they would set out.|יִסָּֽעוּ׃\rb* \v 23 \rb They camped|יַחֲנ֔וּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb command,|פִּ֤י\rb* \rb and they set out|יִסָּ֑עוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb at|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb command;|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb they carried out|שָׁמָ֔רוּ\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb charge|מִשְׁמֶ֤רֶת\rb* \rb according to|עַל־\rb* \rb His|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb command|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*
\c 10
\s1 The Two Silver Trumpets
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Make|עֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּי֙\rb* \rb trumpets|חֲצֽוֹצְרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of hammered|מִקְשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb to be used|וְהָי֤וּ\rb* \rb for calling|לְמִקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the congregation|הָֽעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and for having the camps|הַֽמַּחֲנֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb set out.|וּלְמַסַּ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 3 \rb When both are sounded,|וְתָקְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb is to assemble|וְנֽוֹעֲד֤וּ\rb* \rb before|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb you at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 4 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb only one|בְּאַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb is sounded,|יִתְקָ֑עוּ\rb* \rb then the leaders,|הַנְּשִׂיאִ֔ים\rb* \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of the clans|אַלְפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb are to gather|וְנוֹעֲד֤וּ\rb* \rb before you.|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb When you sound|וּתְקַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb short blasts,|תְּרוּעָ֑ה\rb* \rb the camps|הַֽמַּחֲנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb that lie|הַחֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the east side|קֵֽדְמָה׃\rb* \rb are to set out.|וְנָֽסְעוּ֙\rb* \v 6 \rb When you sound|וּתְקַעְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb the short blasts|תְּרוּעָה֙\rb* \rb a second time,|שֵׁנִ֔ית\rb* \rb the camps|הַֽמַּחֲנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb that lie|הַחֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the south side|תֵּימָ֑נָה\rb* \rb are to set out.|וְנָֽסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb The blasts|תְּרוּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb are to signal them|יִתְקְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to set out.|לְמַסְעֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb To convene|וּבְהַקְהִ֖יל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the assembly,|הַקָּהָ֑ל\rb* \rb you are to sound long blasts,|תִּתְקְע֖וּ\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb short ones.|תָרִֽיעוּ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb The sons|וּבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Aaron,|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb the priests,|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb are to sound|יִתְקְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the trumpets.|בַּֽחֲצֹצְר֑וֹת\rb* \rb This shall be|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb a permanent|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb statute|לְחֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and the generations to come.|לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb When|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹ֨אוּ\rb* \rb into battle|מִלְחָמָ֜ה\rb* \rb in your land|בְּאַרְצְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb an adversary|הַצַּר֙\rb* \rb who attacks|הַצֹּרֵ֣ר\rb* \rb you,|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb sound short blasts|וַהֲרֵעֹתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on the trumpets,|בַּחֲצֹצְר֑וֹת\rb* \rb and you will be remembered|וֲנִזְכַּרְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and saved|וְנוֹשַׁעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb from your enemies.|מֵאֹיְבֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb And on your joyous|שִׂמְחַתְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb occasions,|וּבְי֨וֹם\rb* \rb your appointed feasts,|וּֽבְמוֹעֲדֵיכֶם֮\rb* \rb and the beginning|וּבְרָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of each month,|חָדְשֵׁיכֶם֒\rb* \rb you are to blow|וּתְקַעְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb the trumpets|בַּחֲצֹֽצְרֹ֗ת\rb* \rb over|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb your burnt offerings|עֹלֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb and peace|שַׁלְמֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb offerings|זִבְחֵ֣י\rb* \rb to serve|וְהָי֨וּ\rb* \rb as a reminder|לְזִכָּרוֹן֙\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.”|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\s1 From Sinai to Paran
\p \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb On the twentieth|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb day|בַּחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֛ית\rb* \rb year,|בַּשָּׁנָ֧ה\rb* \rb the cloud|הֶֽעָנָ֔ן\rb* \rb was lifted|נַעֲלָה֙\rb* \rb from above|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the tabernacle|מִשְׁכַּ֥ן\rb* \rb of the Testimony,|הָעֵדֻֽת׃\rb* \v 12 \rb and the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb set out|וַיִּסְע֧וּ\rb* \rb from the Wilderness|מִמִּדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Sinai,|סִינָ֑י\rb* \rb traveling from place to place|לְמַסְעֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb until the cloud|הֶעָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb settled|וַיִּשְׁכֹּ֥ן\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of Paran.|פָּארָֽן׃\rb* \v 13 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb this first time|בָּרִאשֹׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb according to|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb command|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb First,|בָּרִאשֹׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb the divisions|לְצִבְאֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the camp|מַחֲנֵ֧ה\rb* \rb of Judah|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb set out|וַיִּסַּ֞ע\rb* \rb under their standard,|דֶּ֣גֶל\rb* \rb with Nahshon|נַחְשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Amminadab|עַמִּינָדָֽב׃\rb* \rb in command.|וְעַל־\rb*\rb |צְבָא֔וֹ\rb* \v 15 \rb Nethanel|נְתַנְאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zuar|צוּעָֽר׃\rb* \rb was over|וְעַ֨ל־\rb* \rb the division|צְבָ֔א\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֖ה\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Issachar,|יִשָׂשכָ֑ר\rb* \v 16 \rb and Eliab|אֱלִיאָ֖ב\rb* \rb son|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Helon|חֵלֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb was over|וְעַ֨ל־\rb* \rb the division|צְבָ֔א\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֖ה\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zebulun.|זְבוּלֻ֑ן\rb* \v 17 \rb Then the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֑ן\rb* \rb was taken down,|וְהוּרַ֖ד\rb* \rb and the Gershonites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |גֵרְשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb and the Merarites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |מְרָרִ֔י\rb* \rb set out,|וְנָסְע֤וּ\rb* \rb transporting|נֹשְׂאֵ֖י\rb* \rb it.|הַמִּשְׁכָּֽן׃ס\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then the divisions|לְצִבְאֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the camp|מַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֖ן\rb* \rb set out|וְנָסַ֗ע\rb* \rb under their standard,|דֶּ֛גֶל\rb* \rb with Elizur|אֱלִיצ֖וּר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shedeur|שְׁדֵיאֽוּר׃\rb* \rb in command.|וְעַל־\rb*\rb |צְבָא֔וֹ\rb* \v 19 \rb Shelumiel|שְׁלֻֽמִיאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zurishaddai|שַׁדָּֽי׃\rb* \rb was over|וְעַ֨ל־\rb* \rb the division|צְבָ֔א\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֖ה\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |צוּרִֽי\rb* \rb of Simeon,|שִׁמְע֑וֹן\rb* \v 20 \rb and Eliasaph|אֶלְיָסָ֖ף\rb* \rb son|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Deuel|דְּעוּאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb was over|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the division|צְבָ֖א\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Gad.|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |גָ֑ד\rb* \v 21 \rb Then the Kohathites|הַקְּהָתִ֔ים\rb* \rb set out,|וְנָסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb transporting|נֹשְׂאֵ֖י\rb* \rb the holy objects;|הַמִּקְדָּ֑שׁ\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הַמִּשְׁכָּ֖ן\rb* \rb was to be set up|וְהֵקִ֥ימוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|עַד־\rb* \rb their arrival.|בֹּאָֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Next, the divisions|לְצִבְאֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the camp|מַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of Ephraim|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb set out|וְנָסַ֗ע\rb* \rb under their standard,|דֶּ֛גֶל\rb* \rb with Elishama|אֱלִישָׁמָ֖ע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ammihud|עַמִּיהֽוּד׃\rb* \rb in command.|וְעַל־\rb*\rb |צְבָא֔וֹ\rb* \v 23 \rb Gamaliel|גַּמְלִיאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Pedahzur|פְּדָה־\rb*\rb |צֽוּר׃\rb* \rb was over|וְעַ֨ל־\rb* \rb the division|צְבָ֔א\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb of Manasseh,|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb* \v 24 \rb and Abidan|אֲבִידָ֖ן\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb son|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gideoni|גִּדְעוֹנִֽי׃ס\rb* \rb was over|וְעַ֨ל־\rb* \rb the division|צְבָ֔א\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb of Benjamin.|בִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Finally, the divisions|לְצִבְאֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb of the camp|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Dan|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |דָ֔ן\rb* \rb set out|וְנָסַ֗ע\rb* \rb under their standard,|דֶּ֚גֶל\rb* \rb serving as the rear guard|מְאַסֵּ֥ף\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb units,|הַֽמַּחֲנֹ֖ת\rb* \rb with Ahiezer|אֲחִיעֶ֖זֶר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ammishaddai|עַמִּישַׁדָּֽי׃\rb* \rb in command.|וְעַל־\rb*\rb |צְבָא֔וֹ\rb* \v 26 \rb Pagiel|פַּגְעִיאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Ocran|עָכְרָֽן׃\rb* \rb was over|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the division|צְבָ֔א\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb of Asher,|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |אָשֵׁ֑ר\rb* \v 27 \rb and Ahira|אֲחִירַ֖ע\rb* \rb son|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Enan|עֵינָֽן׃\rb* \rb was over|וְעַ֨ל־\rb* \rb the division|צְבָ֔א\rb* \rb of the tribe|מַטֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb of Naphtali.|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |נַפְתָּלִ֑י\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb This|אֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb was the order of march|מַסְעֵ֥י\rb* \rb for the Israelite|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb divisions|לְצִבְאֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb as they set out.|וַיִּסָּֽעוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to Hobab,|לְ֠חֹבָב\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Moses’|מֹשֶׁה֒\rb* \rb father-in-law|חֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb Reuel|רְעוּאֵ֣ל\rb*\f + \fr 10:29 \fqa Reuel \ft was also called \fqa Jethro\ft ; see \ref Exodus 3:1|EXO 3:1\ref*.\f* \rb the Midianite,|הַמִּדְיָנִי֮\rb* \rb “We are|אֲנַ֗חְנוּ\rb* \rb setting out|נֹסְעִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb of which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb said:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘I will give it|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb to you.’|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Come|לְכָ֤ה\rb* \rb with us,|אִתָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb and we will treat you well,|וְהֵטַ֣בְנוּ\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb has promised|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb good|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb things to|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel.”|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb “I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go,”|אֵלֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb Hobab replied.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb “Instead,|כִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb I am going back|אֵלֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my own land|אַרְצִ֛י\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and my own people.”|מוֹלַדְתִּ֖י\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb “Please|נָ֖א\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb leave us,”|תַּעֲזֹ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb Moses said,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “since|כִּ֣י׀\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb you know|יָדַ֗עְתָּ\rb* \rb where we should camp|חֲנֹתֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb in the wilderness,|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb and you can serve|וְהָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb as our|לָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb eyes.|לְעֵינָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 32 \rb |וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb If|כִּי־\rb* \rb you come|תֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb with us,|עִמָּ֑נוּ\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb we will share|וְהֵטַ֥בְנוּ\rb* \rb with you|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |יֵיטִ֧יב\rb* \rb good things|הַטּ֣וֹב\rb*\rb |הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb gives us.”|עִמָּ֖נוּ\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb So they set out|וַיִּסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb on a three-day|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb journey|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb from the mountain|מֵהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb with the ark|וַאֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb traveling|נֹסֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb ahead of them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |דֶּ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb for those three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb to seek|לָת֥וּר\rb* \rb a resting place|מְנוּחָֽה׃\rb* \rb for them.|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 34 \rb And the cloud|וַעֲנַ֧ן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb was over them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb by day|יוֹמָ֑ם\rb* \rb when they set out|בְּנָסְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the camp.|הַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃׆ס\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb Whenever|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb set out,|בִּנְסֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb would say,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Rise up,|קוּמָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb O LORD!|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb May Your enemies|אֹֽיְבֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb be scattered;|וְיָפֻ֙צוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb may those who hate You|מְשַׂנְאֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb flee|וְיָנֻ֥סוּ\rb* \rb before You.”|מִפָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb And when it came to rest,|וּבְנֻחֹ֖ה\rb* \rb he would say:|יֹאמַ֑ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Return,|שׁוּבָ֣ה\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb to the countless|רִֽבְב֖וֹת\rb* \rb thousands|אַלְפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.”|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃׆ס\rb*
\c 11
\s1 The Complaints of the People
\p \v 1 \rb Soon|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb began to complain|כְּמִתְאֹ֣נְנִ֔ים\rb* \rb about their hardship|רַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and when He|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb heard them,|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb His anger|אַפּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb was kindled,|וַיִּ֣חַר\rb* \rb and fire|אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb blazed|וַתִּבְעַר־\rb* \rb among them|בָּם֙\rb* \rb and consumed|וַתֹּ֖אכַל\rb* \rb the outskirts|בִּקְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the camp.|הַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּצְעַ֥ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb and he|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֤ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and the fire|הָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb died down.|וַתִּשְׁקַ֖ע\rb* \v 3 \rb So that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb was called|וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb Taberah,|תַּבְעֵרָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 11:3 \fqa Taberah \ft means \fqa burning\ft .\f* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the fire|אֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had burned|בָעֲרָ֥ה\rb* \rb among them.|בָ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Meanwhile, the rabble|וְהָֽאסַפְסֻף֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb among them|בְּקִרְבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb had a strong craving for other food,|הִתְאַוּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |תַּאֲוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and|גַּ֚ם\rb* \rb again|וַיָּשֻׁ֣בוּ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb wept|וַיִּבְכּ֗וּ\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb will feed us|יַאֲכִלֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb meat?|בָּשָֽׂר׃\rb* \v 5 \rb We remember|זָכַ֙רְנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fish|הַדָּגָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb we ate|נֹאכַ֥ל\rb* \rb freely|חִנָּ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb in Egypt,|בְּמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb along with the cucumbers,|הַקִּשֻּׁאִ֗ים\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb melons,|הָֽאֲבַטִּחִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb leeks,|הֶחָצִ֥יר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb onions,|הַבְּצָלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and garlic.|הַשּׁוּמִֽים׃\rb* \v 6 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb our appetite|נַפְשֵׁ֥נוּ\rb* \rb is gone;|יְבֵשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb there is nothing|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |כֹּ֑ל\rb* \rb to see|עֵינֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb but|בִּלְתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb this manna!”|הַמָּ֥ן\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Now the manna|וְהַמָּ֕ן\rb* \rb resembled coriander|גַּ֖ד\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb* \rb seed,|כִּזְרַע־\rb* \rb and its appearance|וְעֵינ֖וֹ\rb* \rb was like that|כְּעֵ֥ין\rb* \rb of gum resin.|הַבְּדֹֽלַח׃\rb* \v 8 \rb The people|הָעָ֨ם\rb* \rb walked around|שָׁטוּ֩\rb* \rb and gathered it,|וְלָֽקְט֜וּ\rb* \rb ground it|וְטָחֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb on a handmill|בָרֵחַ֗יִם\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb crushed it|דָכוּ֙\rb* \rb in a mortar,|בַּמְּדֹכָ֔ה\rb* \rb then boiled|וּבִשְּׁלוּ֙\rb* \rb it in a cooking pot|בַּפָּר֔וּר\rb* \rb or shaped it into|וְעָשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb cakes.|עֻג֑וֹת\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb It tasted|טַעְמ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |כְּטַ֖עַם\rb* \rb like pastry|לְשַׁ֥ד\rb* \rb baked with fine oil.|הַשָּֽׁמֶן׃\rb* \v 9 \rb When the dew|הַטַּ֛ל\rb* \rb fell|וּבְרֶ֧דֶת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb at night,|לָ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb the manna|הַמָּ֖ן\rb* \rb would fall|יֵרֵ֥ד\rb* \rb with it.|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*
\s1 The Complaint of Moses
\p \v 10 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֨ע\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb of family|לְמִשְׁפְּחֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb after family|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb weeping|בֹּכֶה֙\rb* \rb at the entrances|לְפֶ֣תַח\rb* \rb to their tents,|אָהֳל֑וֹ\rb* \rb and the anger|אַ֤ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was kindled|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb greatly,|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb and Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb was also displeased.|וּבְעֵינֵ֥י\rb*\rb |רָֽע׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb “Why|לָמָ֤ה\rb* \rb have You brought this trouble|הֲרֵעֹ֙תָ֙\rb* \rb on Your servant?|לְעַבְדֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb Why|וְלָ֛מָּה\rb* \rb have I not|לֹא־\rb* \rb found|מָצָ֥תִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in Your sight,|בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb that You have laid|לָשׂ֗וּם\rb* \rb upon me|עָלָֽי׃\rb* \rb the burden|מַשָּׂ֛א\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people?|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \v 12 \rb Did I|הֶאָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb conceive|הָרִ֗יתִי\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb people?|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb Did I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb give them birth,|יְלִדְתִּ֑יהוּ\rb* \rb so that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You should tell|תֹאמַ֨ר\rb* \rb me,|אֵלַ֜י\rb* \rb ‘Carry them|שָׂאֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb in your bosom,|בְחֵיקֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb a nurse|הָאֹמֵן֙\rb* \rb carries|יִשָּׂ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an infant,’|הַיֹּנֵ֔ק\rb* \rb to|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the land|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You swore to give|נִשְׁבַּ֖עְתָּ\rb* \rb their fathers?|לַאֲבֹתָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Where|מֵאַ֤יִן\rb* \rb can I get meat|בָּשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb for|לָתֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb people?|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they keep crying out|יִבְכּ֤וּ\rb* \rb to me,|עָלַי֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Give|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb us|לָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb meat|בָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb to eat!’|וְנֹאכֵֽלָה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb I|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb cannot|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |אוּכַ֤ל\rb* \rb carry|לָשֵׂ֖את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb by myself;|לְבַדִּ֔י\rb* \rb it is|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb too burdensome|כָבֵ֖ד\rb* \rb for me.|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb* \v 15 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb this is how|כָּ֣כָה׀\rb* \rb You|אַתְּ־\rb* \rb are going to treat|עֹ֣שֶׂה\rb* \rb me,|לִּ֗י\rb* \rb please|נָא֙\rb* \rb kill me right now—|הָרֹ֔ג\rb*  \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in Your eyes—|בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb*  \rb and let me not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb see|אֶרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb my own wretchedness.”|בְּרָעָתִֽי׃פ\rb*
\s1 Seventy Elders Anointed
\p \v 16 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Bring|אֶסְפָה־\rb* \rb Me|לִּ֞י\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֮\rb* \rb of the elders|מִזִּקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb known to you|יָדַ֔עְתָּ\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb*\rb |הֵ֛ם\rb* \rb as leaders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb and officers|וְשֹׁטְרָ֑יו\rb* \rb of the people.|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb Bring|וְלָקַחְתָּ֤\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb and have them stand|וְהִֽתְיַצְּב֥וּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb with you.|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb And I will come down|וְיָרַדְתִּ֗י\rb* \rb and speak|וְדִבַּרְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֮\rb* \rb there,|שָׁם֒\rb* \rb and I will take|וְאָצַלְתִּ֗י\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the Spirit|הָר֛וּחַ\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on you|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and put|וְשַׂמְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb that Spirit on them.|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb They will help you bear|וְנָשְׂא֤וּ\rb*\rb |אִתְּךָ֙\rb* \rb the burden|בְּמַשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb of the people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb so that you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb do not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb have to bear it|תִשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb by yourself.|לְבַדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb And|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb say|תֹּאמַ֜ר\rb* \rb to the people:|הָעָ֨ם\rb* \rb Consecrate yourselves|הִתְקַדְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb for tomorrow,|לְמָחָר֮\rb* \rb and you will eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb meat,|בָּשָׂר֒\rb* \rb because|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb you have cried out|בְּכִיתֶם֩\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb will feed us|יַאֲכִלֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb meat?|בָּשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb we were better off|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb in Egypt!’|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb Therefore the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb will give|וְנָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb meat,|בָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb and you will eat.|וַאֲכַלְתֶּֽם׃\rb* \v 19 \rb You will eat it|תֹּאכְל֖וּן\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb for one|אֶחָ֛ד\rb*\rb |י֥וֹם\rb* \rb or two days,|יוֹמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א׀\rb* \rb for five|חֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |יָמִ֗ים\rb*\rb |וְלֹא֙\rb* \rb or ten|עֲשָׂרָ֣ה\rb*\rb |יָמִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb or twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb days,|יֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 20 \rb but for|עַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb a whole month—|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb until|עַ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb it comes out|יֵצֵא֙\rb* \rb of your nostrils|מֵֽאַפְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and makes|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb nauseous—|לְזָרָ֑א\rb* \rb because|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have rejected|מְאַסְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is among you,|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and have cried out|וַתִּבְכּ֤וּ\rb* \rb before Him,|לְפָנָיו֙\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb did we ever|זֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb leave|יָצָ֥אנוּ\rb* \rb Egypt?’”|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁה֒\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb* \rb “Here I am|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb among|בְּקִרְבּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb 600,000|שֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb men|הָעָ֕ם\rb* \rb on foot,|רַגְלִ֔י\rb* \rb yet You|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb say,|אָמַ֗רְתָּ\rb* \rb ‘I will give|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb meat,|בָּשָׂר֙\rb* \rb and they will eat|וְאָכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb for a month.’|חֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |יָמִֽים׃\rb* \v 22 \rb If all our flocks|הֲצֹ֧אן\rb* \rb and herds|וּבָקָ֛ר\rb* \rb were slaughtered|יִשָּׁחֵ֥ט\rb* \rb for them,|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb would they have enough?|וּמָצָ֣א\rb* \rb Or if|אִ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fish|דְּגֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the sea|הַיָּ֛ם\rb* \rb were caught|יֵאָסֵ֥ף\rb* \rb for them,|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb would they have enough?”|וּמָצָ֥א\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Is the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb arm|הֲיַ֥ד\rb* \rb too short?|תִּקְצָ֑ר\rb* \rb Now|עַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb you will see|תִרְאֶ֛ה\rb* \rb whether or|אִם־\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא׃\rb* \rb My word|דְבָרִ֖י\rb* \rb will come to pass.”|הֲיִקְרְךָ֥\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb and relayed|וַיְדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and he gathered|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֞ף\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb of the elders|מִזִּקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and had them stand|וַֽיַּעֲמֵ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb around|סְבִיבֹ֥ת\rb* \rb the tent.|הָאֹֽהֶל׃\rb* \v 25 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb came down|וַיֵּ֨רֶד\rb* \rb in the cloud|בֶּעָנָן֮\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָיו֒\rb* \rb and He took|וַיָּ֗אצֶל\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the Spirit|הָר֙וּחַ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was on Moses|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and placed|וַיִּתֵּ֕ן\rb* \rb that Spirit on|עַל־\rb* \rb the seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb elders.|הַזְּקֵנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb As the Spirit|הָר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb rested|כְּנ֤וֹחַ\rb* \rb on them,|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb they prophesied—|וַיִּֽתְנַבְּא֖וּ\rb*  \rb but they never|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb did so again.|יָסָֽפוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb men,|אֲנָשִׁ֣ים׀\rb* \rb however, had remained|וַיִּשָּׁאֲר֣וּ\rb* \rb in the camp—|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶ֡ה\rb*  \rb one|הָאֶחָ֣ד׀\rb* \rb named|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb Eldad|אֶלְדָּ֡ד\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁם֩\rb* \rb and the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֨י\rb* \rb Medad—|מֵידָ֜ד\rb*  \rb and the Spirit|הָר֗וּחַ\rb* \rb rested|וַתָּ֧נַח\rb* \rb on them.|עֲלֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb They|וְהֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb were among those listed,|בַּכְּתֻבִ֔ים\rb* \rb but they had not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb gone out|יָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb to the tent,|הָאֹ֑הֱלָה\rb* \rb and they prophesied|וַיִּֽתְנַבְּא֖וּ\rb* \rb in the camp.|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \v 27 \rb A young man|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb* \rb ran|וַיָּ֣רָץ\rb* \rb and reported|וַיַּגֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb to Moses,|לְמֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “Eldad|אֶלְדָּ֣ד\rb* \rb and Medad|וּמֵידָ֔ד\rb* \rb are prophesying|מִֽתְנַבְּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the camp.”|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun,|נ֗וּן\rb* \rb the attendant|מְשָׁרֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb since youth,|מִבְּחֻרָ֖יו\rb* \rb spoke up|וַיַּ֜עַן\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb my lord,|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb stop them!”|כְּלָאֵֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “Are you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb jealous|הַֽמְקַנֵּ֥א\rb* \rb on my|לִ֑י\rb* \rb account?|וּמִ֨י\rb* \rb I wish that|יִתֵּ֜ן\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb people|עַ֤ם\rb* \rb were prophets|נְבִיאִ֔ים\rb* \rb and that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb would place|יִתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb His Spirit|רוּח֖וֹ\rb* \rb on them!”|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb returned|וַיֵּאָסֵ֥ף\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp,|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb along with the elders|וְזִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\s1 The Quail and the Plague
\p \v 31 \rb Now a wind|וְר֜וּחַ\rb* \rb sent by|מִן־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb came up,|נָסַ֣ע׀\rb* \rb drove in|וַיָּ֣גָז\rb* \rb quail|שַׂלְוִים֮\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the sea,|הַיָּם֒\rb* \rb and brought them|וַיִּטֹּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the camp,|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֜ה\rb* \rb about two cubits|וּכְאַמָּתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the surface|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the ground,|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*\f + \fr 11:31 \ft Or \fqa up to two cubits deep\ft ; that is, approximately 3 feet or 91.4 centimeters\f* \rb for a day’s|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb journey|כְּדֶ֧רֶךְ\rb* \rb in every direction|כֹּ֗ה\rb*\rb |וּכְדֶ֤רֶךְ\rb*\rb |יוֹם֙\rb*\rb |כֹּ֔ה\rb* \rb around|סְבִיב֖וֹת\rb* \rb the camp.|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \v 32 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|הַה֨וּא\rb* \rb day|הַיּוֹם֩\rb* \rb and night,|הַלַּ֜יְלָה\rb*\rb |וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the next|הַֽמָּחֳרָ֗ת\rb* \rb day,|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֡ם\rb* \rb stayed up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb gathering|וַיַּֽאַסְפוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the quail.|הַשְּׂלָ֔ו\rb* \rb No one gathered|אָסַ֖ף\rb* \rb less than|הַמַּמְעִ֕יט\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb homers,|חֳמָרִ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 11:32 \fqa 10 homers \ft is approximately 62.4 bushels or 2,200 liters.\f* \rb and they spread them out|וַיִּשְׁטְח֤וּ\rb*\rb |שָׁט֔וֹחַ\rb* \rb all around|סְבִיב֖וֹת\rb* \rb the camp.|הַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb But while|עוֹדֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂ֗ר\rb* \rb was still between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb their teeth,|שִׁנֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb before|טֶ֖רֶם\rb* \rb it was chewed,|יִכָּרֵ֑ת\rb* \rb the anger|וְאַ֤ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb burned|חָרָ֣ה\rb* \rb against the people,|בָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb struck|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb them|בָּעָ֔ם\rb* \rb with a severe|רַבָּ֥ה\rb* \rb plague.|מַכָּ֖ה\rb* \v 34 \rb So they called|וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb*\rb |קִבְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb Kibroth-hattaavah,|הַֽתַּאֲוָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 11:34 \fqa Kibroth-hattaavah \ft means \fqa graves of craving\ft .\f* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb they buried|קָֽבְר֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb who had craved other food.|הַמִּתְאַוִּֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb From|מִקִּבְר֧וֹת\rb* \rb Kibroth-hattaavah|הַֽתַּאֲוָ֛ה\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb moved on|נָסְע֥וּ\rb* \rb to Hazeroth,|חֲצֵר֑וֹת\rb* \rb where they remained for some time.|וַיִּהְי֖וּ\rb*\rb |בַּחֲצֵרֽוֹת׃פ\rb*
\c 12
\s1 The Complaint of Miriam and Aaron
\p \v 1 \rb Then Miriam|מִרְיָ֤ם\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb criticized|וַתְּדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb Moses|בְּמֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb*\rb |אֹד֛וֹת\rb* \rb the Cushite|הַכֻּשִׁ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb woman|הָאִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb he had married,|לָקָ֑ח\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he had taken|לָקָֽח׃\rb* \rb a Cushite|כֻשִׁ֖ית\rb* \rb wife.|אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \v 2 \rb “Does the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb speak|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb only|הֲרַ֤ק\rb*\rb |אַךְ־\rb* \rb through Moses?”|בְּמֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb they said.|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “Does He not|הֲלֹ֖א\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb speak|דִבֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb through us?”|בָּ֣נוּ\rb* \rb And the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb heard this.|וַיִּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Now Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb was a very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb humble|עָנָו\rb* \rb man,|וְהָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb more so than any|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And suddenly|פִּתְאֹ֗ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Miriam,|מִרְיָ֔ם\rb* \rb “You three,|שְׁלָשְׁתְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb come out|צְא֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.”|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb So the three|שְׁלָשְׁתָּֽם׃\rb* \rb went out,|וַיֵּצְא֖וּ\rb* \v 5 \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb came down|וַיֵּ֤רֶד\rb* \rb in a pillar|בְּעַמּ֣וּד\rb* \rb of cloud,|עָנָ֔ן\rb* \rb stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent,|הָאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb and summoned|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and Miriam.|וּמִרְיָ֔ם\rb* \rb When both|שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb of them had stepped forward,|וַיֵּצְא֖וּ\rb* \v 6 \rb He said,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “Hear|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb* \rb now|נָ֣א\rb* \rb My words:|דְבָרָ֑י\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb there is|יִֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb a prophet among you,|נְבִ֣יאֲכֶ֔ם\rb*
