\p \rb Why then|וּמַדּ֙וּעַ֙\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb were you unafraid|יְרֵאתֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb against My servant|בְּעַבְדִּ֥י\rb* \rb Moses?”|בְמֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \v 9 \rb So the anger|אַ֧ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר\rb* \rb against them,|בָּ֖ם\rb* \rb and He departed.|וַיֵּלַֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb As the cloud|וְהֶעָנָ֗ן\rb* \rb lifted|סָ֚ר\rb* \rb from above|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the Tent,|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb Miriam|מִרְיָ֖ם\rb* \rb became leprous,|מְצֹרַ֣עַת\rb*\f + \fr 12:10 \ft The Hebrew word traditionally translated as \fqa leprous \ft was used for various skin diseases; see Leviticus 13.\f* \rb white as snow.|כַּשָּׁ֑לֶג\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּ֧פֶן\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb her,|מִרְיָ֖ם\rb* \rb saw that|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb she was leprous,|מְצֹרָֽעַת׃\rb* \v 11 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*\rb |בִּ֣י\rb* \rb “My lord,|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb please|נָ֨א\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb hold|תָשֵׁ֤ת\rb* \rb against us|עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb this sin|חַטָּ֔את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb we have so foolishly|נוֹאַ֖לְנוּ\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb committed.|חָטָֽאנוּ׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let her be|תְהִ֖י\rb* \rb like a stillborn infant|כַּמֵּ֑ת\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb flesh|בְשָׂרֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb is half|חֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb consumed|וַיֵּאָכֵ֖ל\rb* \rb when he comes out|בְּצֵאתוֹ֙\rb* \rb of his mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb womb.”|מֵרֶ֣חֶם\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּצְעַ֣ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “O God,|אֵ֕ל\rb* \rb please|נָ֛א\rb* \rb heal|רְפָ֥א\rb*\rb |נָ֖א\rb* \rb her!”|לָֽהּ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “If her father|וְאָבִ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb had but spit|יָרֹ֤ק\rb*\rb |יָרַק֙\rb* \rb in her face,|בְּפָנֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb would she not|הֲלֹ֥א\rb* \rb have been in disgrace|תִכָּלֵ֖ם\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days?|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb Let her be confined|תִּסָּגֵ֞ר\rb* \rb outside|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb days;|יָמִים֙\rb* \rb after that|וְאַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb she may be brought back in.”|תֵּאָסֵֽף׃\rb*
