\c 14
\s1 Israel’s Rebellion
\r \ref Deuteronomy 1:26–33|DEU 1:26-33\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb lifted up|וַתִּשָּׂא֙\rb* \rb their voices|קוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb and cried out,|וַֽיִּתְּנ֖וּ\rb* \rb and that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb wept.|וַיִּבְכּ֥וּ\rb* \v 2 \rb All|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb grumbled|וַיִּלֹּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb and the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָעֵדָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַֽיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb “If only|לוּ־\rb* \rb we had died|מַ֙תְנוּ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb or|א֛וֹ\rb* \rb if only|לוּ־\rb* \rb we had died|מָֽתְנוּ׃\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb wilderness!|בַּמִּדְבָּ֥ר\rb* \v 3 \rb Why|וְלָמָ֣ה\rb* \rb is the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb* \rb bringing|מֵבִ֨יא\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֜נוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb to fall|לִנְפֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb by the sword?|בַּחֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb Our wives|נָשֵׁ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb and children|וְטַפֵּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb will become|יִהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb plunder.|לָבַ֑ז\rb* \rb Would it not|הֲל֧וֹא\rb* \rb be better|ט֦וֹב\rb* \rb for us|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to go back|שׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb to Egypt?”|מִצְרָֽיְמָה׃\rb*
