\p \v 25 \rb Now since the Amalekites|וְהָֽעֲמָלֵקִ֥י\rb* \rb and Canaanites|וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb are living|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in the valleys,|בָּעֵ֑מֶק\rb* \rb turn back|פְּנ֨וּ\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֗ר\rb* \rb and head for|וּסְע֥וּ\rb* \rb the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb* \rb along the route to|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb the Red|סֽוּף׃פ\rb* \rb Sea.|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 14:25 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f*”
\p \v 26 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 27 \rb “How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַ֗י\rb* \rb will this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb wicked|הָֽרָעָה֙\rb* \rb congregation|לָעֵדָ֤ה\rb*\rb |הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb grumble|מַלִּינִ֖ים\rb* \rb against|עָלָ֑י\rb* \rb Me?|אֶת־\rb* \rb I have heard|שָׁמָֽעְתִּי׃\rb* \rb the complaints|תְּלֻנּ֞וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |הֵ֧מָּה\rb*\rb |מַלִּינִ֛ים\rb* \rb are making against Me.|עָלַ֖י\rb* \v 28 \rb So tell them:|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb As surely as I|אָ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb live,|חַי־\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb I will do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb exactly|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֕א\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I heard|בְּאָזְנָ֑י\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb you say.|דִּבַּרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \v 29 \rb Your bodies|פִגְרֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb will fall|יִפְּל֨וּ\rb* \rb in this|הַ֠זֶּה\rb* \rb wilderness—|בַּמִּדְבָּ֣ר\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb who were numbered|פְּקֻדֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb in the census,|מִסְפַּרְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb everyone|לְכָל־\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb or older—|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have grumbled|הֲלִֽינֹתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb against Me.|עָלָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Surely none|אִם־\rb* \rb of you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb will enter|תָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I swore|נָשָׂ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb to settle you,|לְשַׁכֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb except|כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb Caleb|כָּלֵ֣ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jephunneh|יְפֻנֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb and Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun.|נֽוּן׃\rb* \v 31 \rb But I will bring your children,|וְטַ֨פְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you said|אֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb would become|יִהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb plunder,|לָבַ֣ז\rb* \rb into|וְהֵבֵיאתִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have rejected—|מְאַסְתֶּ֖ם\rb*  \rb and they will enjoy it.|וְיָֽדְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 32 \rb As for you,|אַתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb however, your bodies|וּפִגְרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will fall|יִפְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb wilderness.|בַּמִּדְבָּ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb Your children|וּ֠בְנֵיכֶם\rb* \rb will be|יִהְי֨וּ\rb* \rb shepherds|רֹעִ֤ים\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּר֙\rb* \rb for forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb and they will suffer|וְנָשְׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb for your unfaithfulness|זְנוּתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb until the last|עַד־\rb* \rb of your bodies|פִּגְרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb lies|תֹּ֥ם\rb* \rb in the wilderness.|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb* \v 34 \rb In keeping with the|בְּמִסְפַּ֨ר\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you spied|תַּרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb out the land,|הָאָרֶץ֮\rb* \rb you shall bear|תִּשְׂאוּ֙\rb* \rb your guilt|עֲוֺנֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb years—|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*  \rb a year|לַשָּׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb for each day—|לַשָּׁנָ֞ה\rb*\rb |י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |יוֹם֒\rb*\rb |י֣וֹם\rb*  \rb and you will experience|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My alienation.|תְּנוּאָתִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb I,|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb have spoken,|דִּבַּרְתִּי֒\rb* \rb and I will surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א׀\rb* \rb do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֗ה\rb* \rb these things|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb to this entire|לְכָל־\rb* \rb wicked|הָֽרָעָה֙\rb*\rb |הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb congregation,|הָעֵדָ֤ה\rb* \rb which has conspired|הַנּוֹעָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb against Me.|עָלָ֑י\rb* \rb They will meet their end|יִתַּ֖מּוּ\rb* \rb in the wilderness,|בַּמִּדְבָּ֥ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb and there|וְשָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb they will die.”|יָמֻֽתוּ׃\rb*
\s1 The Plague on the Ten Spies
\p \v 36 \rb So the men|וְהָ֣אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb had sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb to spy out|לָת֣וּר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֗בוּ\rb* \rb and made the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb grumble|וַיִּלּוֹנוּ\rb* \rb against him|עָלָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb by bringing out|לְהוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb a bad report|דִבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb the land—|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 37 \rb those men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb who had brought out|מוֹצִאֵ֥י\rb* \rb the bad|רָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb report|דִבַּת־\rb* \rb about the land—|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb were struck down|וַיָּמֻ֙תוּ֙\rb* \rb by a plague|בַּמַּגֵּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 38 \rb Of|מִן־\rb* \rb those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb who had gone|הַֽהֹלְכִ֖ים\rb* \rb to spy out|לָת֥וּר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land,|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb only Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֔וּן\rb* \rb and Caleb|וְכָלֵ֖ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jephunneh|יְפֻנֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb remained alive.|חָיוּ֙\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb And when Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb relayed|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb mourned|וַיִּֽתְאַבְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb bitterly.|מְאֹֽד׃\rb*
\s1 The Defeat at Hormah
\r \ref Deuteronomy 1:41–46|DEU 1:41-46\ref*)
\p \v 40 \rb Early the next morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb they got up|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֣מוּ\rb* \rb and went up|וַיַּֽעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ridge|רֹאשׁ־\rb* \rb of the hill country.|הָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb “We have indeed|הִנֶּ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb sinned,”|חָטָֽאנוּ׃\rb* \rb they said,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “but we will go|וְעָלִ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֛וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has promised.”|אָמַ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 41 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb are you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb transgressing|עֹבְרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandment|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD?|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb This|וְהִ֖וא\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb succeed!|תִצְלָֽח׃\rb* \v 42 \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb go up,|תַּעֲל֔וּ\rb* \rb lest|וְלֹא֙\rb* \rb you be struck down|תִּנָּ֣גְפ֔וּ\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your enemies,|אֹיְבֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is not|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb among you.|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \v 43 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb the Amalekites|הָעֲמָלֵקִ֨י\rb* \rb and Canaanites|וְהַכְּנַעֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will face you,|לִפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and you will fall|וּנְפַלְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb by the sword.|בֶּחָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb you have turned|שַׁבְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb away|מֵאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb from the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb with you.”|עִמָּכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 44 \rb But they dared|וַיַּעְפִּ֕לוּ\rb* \rb to go up|לַעֲל֖וֹת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ridge|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the hill country,|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb though neither|לֹא־\rb* \rb Moses|וּמֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb nor the ark|וַאֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb moved|מָ֖שׁוּ\rb* \rb from|מִקֶּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb the camp.|הַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \v 45 \rb Then the Amalekites|הָעֲמָלֵקִי֙\rb* \rb and Canaanites|וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb who lived|הַיֹּשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb part of the hill country|בָּהָ֣ר\rb* \rb came down,|וַיֵּ֤רֶד\rb* \rb attacked them,|וַיַּכּ֥וּם\rb* \rb and routed them|וַֽיַּכְּת֖וּם\rb* \rb all the way|עַד־\rb* \rb to Hormah.|הַֽחָרְמָֽה׃פ\rb*
\c 15
\s1 Laws about Offerings
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Speak|דַּבֵּר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and tell them:|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb After|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹ֗אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb as a home|מוֹשְׁבֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \v 3 \rb and you present|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֨ם\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the herd|הַבָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb flock|הַצֹּֽאן׃\rb* \rb to produce|לַעֲשׂ֞וֹת\rb* \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb aroma|רֵ֤יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD—|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*  \rb either a burnt offering|עֹלָ֣ה\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb a sacrifice,|זֶ֔בַח\rb* \rb for a special|לְפַלֵּא־\rb* \rb vow|נֶ֙דֶר֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb freewill offering|בִנְדָבָ֔ה\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb appointed feast—|בְּמֹעֲדֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \v 4 \rb then the one presenting|וְהִקְרִ֛יב\rb* \rb his offering|קָרְבָּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb shall also present|הַמַּקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb a grain offering|מִנְחָה֙\rb* \rb of a tenth of an ephah|עִשָּׂר֔וֹן\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֣לֶת\rb*\f + \fr 15:4 \fqa A tenth of an ephah \ft is approximately 2 dry quarts or 2.2 liters (probably about 2.6 pounds or 1.2 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb mixed|בָּל֕וּל\rb* \rb with a quarter|בִּרְבִעִ֥ית\rb* \rb hin|הַהִ֖ין\rb* \rb of olive oil.|שָֽׁמֶן׃\rb*\f + \fr 15:4 \ft Or \fqa a quarter hin of oil\ft ; that is, approximately 0.97 quarts or 0.92 liters; similarly in verse 5\f* \v 5 \rb With|עַל־\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb sacrifice|לַזָּ֑בַח\rb* \rb of each|הָאֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb lamb,|לַכֶּ֖בֶשׂ\rb* \rb you are to prepare|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb a quarter|רְבִיעִ֣ית\rb* \rb hin|הַהִ֔ין\rb* \rb of wine|וְיַ֤יִן\rb* \rb as a drink offering.|לַנֶּ֙סֶךְ֙\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb |א֤וֹ\rb* \rb With a ram|לָאַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb you are to prepare|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb a grain offering|מִנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb of two-tenths of an ephah|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 15:6 \fqa Two-tenths of an ephah \ft is approximately 4 dry quarts or 4.4 liters (probably about 5.1 pounds or 2.3 kilograms of flour).\f*\rb |עֶשְׂרֹנִ֑ים\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֖לֶת\rb* \rb mixed|בְּלוּלָ֥ה\rb* \rb with a third|שְׁלִשִׁ֥ית\rb* \rb of a hin|הַהִֽין׃\rb* \rb of olive oil,|בַשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb*\f + \fr 15:6 \ft Or \fqa a third of a hin of oil\ft ; that is, approximately 1.3 quarts or 1.2 liters; similarly in verse 7\f* \v 7 \rb and|תַּקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb a third|שְׁלִשִׁ֣ית\rb* \rb of a hin|הַהִ֑ין\rb* \rb of wine|וְיַ֥יִן\rb* \rb as a drink offering,|לַנֶּ֖סֶךְ\rb* \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵֽיחַ־\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb When|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb you prepare|תַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb a young|בֶן־\rb* \rb bull|בָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עֹלָ֣ה\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb sacrifice|זָ֑בַח\rb* \rb to fulfill|לְפַלֵּא־\rb* \rb a vow|נֶ֥דֶר\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb as a peace offering|שְׁלָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 9 \rb present|וְהִקְרִ֤יב\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb the bull|הַבָּקָר֙\rb* \rb a grain offering|מִנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb of three-tenths of an ephah|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֹנִ֑ים\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֖לֶת\rb*\f + \fr 15:9 \fqa Three-tenths of an ephah \ft is approximately 6 dry quarts or 6.6 liters (probably about 7.6 pounds or 3.5 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb mixed|בָּל֥וּל\rb* \rb with half|חֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb a hin|הַהִֽין׃\rb* \rb of olive oil.|בַּשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb*\f + \fr 15:9 \ft Or \fqa half a hin of oil\ft ; that is, approximately 1.9 quarts or 1.8 liters; similarly in verse 10\f* \v 10 \rb Also present|תַּקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֣י\rb* \rb a hin|הַהִ֑ין\rb* \rb of wine|וְיַ֛יִן\rb* \rb as a drink offering.|לַנֶּ֖סֶךְ\rb* \rb It is a food offering,|אִשֵּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵֽיחַ־\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb This|כָּ֣כָה\rb* \rb is to be done|יֵעָשֶׂ֗ה\rb* \rb for each|הָֽאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb bull,|לַשּׁוֹר֙\rb* \rb ram,|לָאַ֣יִל\rb*\rb |הָאֶחָ֑ד\rb*\rb |אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb lamb,|לַשֶּׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |בַכְּבָשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb goat.|בָעִזִּֽים׃\rb* \v 12 \rb This is how|כָּ֛כָה\rb* \rb you must prepare|תַּעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb each one,|לָאֶחָ֖ד\rb*\rb |כְּמִסְפָּרָֽם׃\rb* \rb no matter how|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb many.|כַּמִּסְפָּ֖ר\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who is native-born|הָאֶזְרָ֥ח\rb* \rb shall prepare|יַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb things in this way|כָּ֖כָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb when he presents|לְהַקְרִ֛יב\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֵּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb as a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵֽיחַ־\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb And for the generations to come,|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a foreigner|גֵּ֜ר\rb* \rb residing|יָגוּר֩\rb* \rb with|אִתְּכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb you or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb someone else|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb among you|בְּתֽוֹכְכֶם֙\rb* \rb wants to prepare|וְעָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֵּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb as a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|רֵֽיחַ־\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb he is to do|תַּעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb exactly as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you do.|יַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \v 15 \rb The assembly|הַקָּהָ֕ל\rb* \rb is to have the same|אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb statute|חֻקָּ֥ה\rb* \rb both for you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and for the foreign resident;|וְלַגֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַגָּ֑ר\rb* \rb it is a permanent|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֤ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come.|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb You and the foreigner|כַּגֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb shall be|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the same before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb The same|אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb law|תּוֹרָ֥ה\rb* \rb and the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb ordinance|וּמִשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb* \rb will apply|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb both to you|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and to the foreigner|וְלַגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb residing|הַגָּ֥ר\rb* \rb with you.”|אִתְּכֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 18 \rb “Speak|דַּבֵּר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and tell them:|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb When you enter|בְּבֹֽאֲכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb am bringing you|מֵבִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb* \v 19 \rb and you eat|בַּאֲכָלְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the food|מִלֶּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb of the land,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֕ה\rb* \rb you shall lift|תָּרִ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb up an offering|תְרוּמָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 20 \rb From the first|רֵאשִׁית֙\rb* \rb of your dough,|עֲרִסֹ֣תֵכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you are to lift|תָּרִ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb up a cake|חַלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb as a contribution;|תְרוּמָ֑ה\rb* \rb offer|תָּרִ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb just like|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb an offering|כִּתְרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb from the threshing floor.|גֹּ֔רֶן\rb* \v 21 \rb Throughout your generations,|לְדֹרֹ֖תֵיכֶֽם׃ס\rb* \rb you are to give|תִּתְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb an offering|תְּרוּמָ֑ה\rb* \rb from the first|מֵרֵאשִׁית֙\rb* \rb of your dough.|עֲרִסֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*
\s1 Offerings for Unintentional Sins
\p \v 22 \rb Now if|וְכִ֣י\rb* \rb you stray unintentionally|תִשְׁגּ֔וּ\rb* \rb and do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb obey|תַעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb commandments|הַמִּצְוֺ֖ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses—|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \v 23 \rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb has commanded|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb you through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֞וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb gave them|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb and continuing through|וָהָ֖לְאָה\rb* \rb the generations to come—|לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb and if|אִ֣ם\rb* \rb it was done|נֶעֶשְׂתָ֣ה\rb* \rb unintentionally|לִשְׁגָגָה֒\rb* \rb without the knowledge|מֵעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the congregation,|הָעֵדָה֮\rb* \rb then the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָעֵדָ֡ה\rb* \rb is to prepare|וְעָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֨ד\rb* \rb young bull|פַּ֣ר\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָר֩\rb* \rb as a burnt offering,|לְעֹלָ֜ה\rb* \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb aroma|לְרֵ֤יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb with its grain offering|וּמִנְחָת֥וֹ\rb* \rb and drink offering|וְנִסְכּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb according to the regulation,|כַּמִּשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb* \rb and one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb male goat|וּשְׂעִיר־\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֥ים\rb* \rb as a sin offering.|לְחַטָּֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb is to make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb for|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֛ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb so that they may be forgiven;|וְנִסְלַ֣ח\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the sin|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb was unintentional|שְׁגָגָ֣ה\rb* \rb and they|וְהֵם֩\rb* \rb have brought|הֵבִ֨יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |קָרְבָּנָ֜ם\rb* \rb a food offering|אִשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and a sin offering,|וְחַטָּאתָ֛ם\rb* \rb presented before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb their unintentional sin.|שִׁגְגָתָֽם׃\rb* \v 26 \rb Then the whole|לְכָל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַת֙\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and the foreigners|וְלַגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb residing|הַגָּ֣ר\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָ֑ם\rb* \rb will be forgiven,|וְנִסְלַ֗ח\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it happened to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb unintentionally.|בִּשְׁגָגָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb Also, if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb person|נֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb sins|תֶּחֱטָ֣א\rb* \rb unintentionally,|בִשְׁגָגָ֑ה\rb* \rb he is to present|וְהִקְרִ֛יבָה\rb* \rb a year-old|בַּת־\rb*\rb |שְׁנָתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb female goat|עֵ֥ז\rb* \rb as a sin offering.|לְחַטָּֽאת׃\rb* \v 28 \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb shall make atonement|וְכִפֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb on behalf of|עַל־\rb* \rb the person|הַנֶּ֧פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who erred|בִשְׁגָגָ֖ה\rb* \rb by sinning unintentionally;|הַשֹּׁגֶ֛גֶת\rb*\rb |בְּחֶטְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb and when atonement has been made|לְכַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb for him,|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb he will be forgiven.|וְנִסְלַ֥ח\rb* \v 29 \rb You|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb shall have|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the same|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb law|תּוֹרָ֤ה\rb* \rb for the one who acts|לָעֹשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb in error,|בִּשְׁגָגָֽה׃\rb* \rb whether he is a native-born|הָֽאֶזְרָח֙\rb* \rb Israelite|בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb or a foreigner|וְלַגֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb residing|הַגָּ֣ר\rb* \rb among you.|בְּתוֹכָ֑ם\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb But the person|וְהַנֶּ֜פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה׀\rb* \rb sins defiantly,|בְּיָ֣ד\rb*\rb |רָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb whether|מִן־\rb* \rb a native|הָֽאֶזְרָח֙\rb* \rb or|וּמִן־\rb* \rb foreigner,|הַגֵּ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb blasphemes|מְגַדֵּ֑ף\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb That|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb person|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb shall be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from among|מִקֶּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb his people.|עַמָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 31 \rb He|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb shall certainly be cut off,|הִכָּרֵ֧ת׀\rb*\rb |תִּכָּרֵ֛ת\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he has despised|בָּזָ֔ה\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb broken|הֵפַ֑ר\rb* \rb His commandment;|מִצְוָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb his guilt remains|עֲוֺנָ֥ה\rb* \rb on him.”|בָֽהּ׃פ\rb*
\s1 A Sabbath-Breaker Stoned
\r \ref Exodus 31:12–17|EXO 31:12-17\ref*)
\p \v 32 \rb While the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb were|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb in the wilderness,|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb was found|וַֽיִּמְצְא֗וּ\rb* \rb gathering|מְקֹשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb wood|עֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּֽת׃\rb* \rb day.|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \v 33 \rb Those who found|הַמֹּצְאִ֥ים\rb* \rb the man|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb gathering|מְקֹשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb wood|עֵצִ֑ים\rb* \rb brought|וַיַּקְרִ֣יבוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation,|הָעֵדָֽה׃\rb* \v 34 \rb and because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb it had not been|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb declared|פֹרַ֔שׁ\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb should be done|יֵּעָשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to him,|לֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb they placed|וַיַּנִּ֥יחוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in custody.|בַּמִּשְׁמָ֑ר\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “The man|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb must surely be put to death.|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמַ֖ת\rb* \rb The whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb is to stone|רָג֨וֹם\rb*\rb |בָֽאֲבָנִים֙\rb* \rb him|אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the camp.”|לַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb So the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָעֵדָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb took|וַיֹּצִ֨יאוּ\rb* \rb the man|אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb outside|מִחוּץ֙\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and stoned|וַיִּרְגְּמ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb him|בָּאֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to death,|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Law of Tassels
\p \v 37 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 38 \rb “Speak|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and tell them|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb that|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb throughout the generations to come|לְדֹרֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb they are to make|וְעָשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb tassels|צִיצִ֛ת\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the corners|כַּנְפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their garments,|בִגְדֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb with|וְנָֽתְנ֛וּ\rb* \rb a blue|תְּכֵֽלֶת׃\rb* \rb cord|פְּתִ֥יל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb each tassel.|צִיצִ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַכָּנָ֖ף\rb* \v 39 \rb These will serve|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb as tassels|לְצִיצִת֒\rb* \rb for you to look at,|וּרְאִיתֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb so that you may remember|וּזְכַרְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that you may obey|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb prostitute yourselves|זֹנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb by following|תָתֻ֜רוּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb your own heart|לְבַבְכֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and your own eyes.|עֵֽינֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אַתֶּ֥ם\rb*
\p \v 40 \rb Then|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you will remember|תִּזְכְּר֔וּ\rb* \rb and obey|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My commandments,|מִצְוֺתָ֑י\rb* \rb and you will be|וִהְיִיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb holy|קְדֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to your God.|לֵֽאלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 41 \rb I|אֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb brought you out|הוֹצֵ֤אתִי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God.|לֵאלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.”|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\c 16
\s1 Korah’s Rebellion
\p \v 1 \rb Now Korah|קֹ֔רַח\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Izhar,|יִצְהָ֥ר\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kohath|קְהָ֖ת\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Levi,|לֵוִ֑י\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb along with some Reubenites—|רְאוּבֵֽן׃\rb*  \rb Dathan|וְדָתָ֨ן\rb* \rb and Abiram,|וַאֲבִירָ֜ם\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Eliab,|אֱלִיאָ֛ב\rb* \rb and On|וְא֥וֹן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Peleth—|פֶּ֖לֶת\rb*  \rb conducted|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \v 2 \rb a rebellion|וַיָּקֻ֙מוּ֙\rb* \rb against|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb along with 250|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתָ֑יִם\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb*\rb |וַאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |מִבְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb renowned|שֵֽׁם׃\rb* \rb as leaders|נְשִׂיאֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the congregation|עֵדָ֛ה\rb* \rb and representatives|קְרִאֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the assembly.|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \v 3 \rb They came together|וַיִּֽקָּהֲל֞וּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and|וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb and told them,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶם֮\rb* \rb “You have taken too much|רַב־\rb* \rb upon yourselves!|לָכֶם֒\rb*\f + \fr 16:3 \ft Figuratively \fqa You have gone too far \ft or \fqa You have appropriated too much authority to yourselves\ft ; similarly in verse 7\f* \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb everyone|כָל־\rb* \rb in the entire|כֻּלָּ֣ם\rb* \rb congregation|הָֽעֵדָה֙\rb* \rb is holy,|קְדֹשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is in their midst.|וּבְתוֹכָ֖ם\rb* \rb Why|וּמַדּ֥וּעַ\rb* \rb then do you exalt|תִּֽתְנַשְּׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb yourselves above|עַל־\rb* \rb the assembly|קְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the LORD?”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb When Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb heard this,|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb he fell|וַיִּפֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb facedown.|עַל־\rb*\rb |פָּנָֽיו׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Then he said|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Korah|קֹ֜רַח\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his followers,|עֲדָתוֹ֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb “Tomorrow morning|בֹּ֠קֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will reveal|וְיֹדַ֨ע\rb* \rb who belongs|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to Him|ל֛וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 16:5 \ft LXX \fqa God has visited and knows those who are His\ft ; cited in \ref 2 Timothy 2:19|2TI 2:19\ref*\f* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb who is holy,|הַקָּד֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and He will bring that person near|וְהִקְרִ֣יב\rb* \rb to Himself.|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb The one|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He chooses|יִבְחַר־\rb* \rb He will bring near|יַקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb to Himself.|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 6 \rb You, Korah,|קֹ֖רַח\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your followers|עֲדָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb are to do|עֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb as follows:|זֹ֖את\rb* \rb Take|קְחוּ־\rb* \rb censers,|מַחְתּ֔וֹת\rb* \v 7 \rb and tomorrow|מָחָ֔ר\rb* \rb you are to place|וּתְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֡שׁ\rb* \rb and incense|קְטֹ֜רֶת\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֨ן\rb* \rb in them|בָהֵ֣ן׀\rb*\rb |וְשִׂימוּ֩\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb Then the man|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb chooses|יִבְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb the one|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb who is holy.|הַקָּד֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb It is you sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִֽי׃\rb* \rb who have taken too much|רַב־\rb* \rb upon yourselves!”|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Korah,|קֹ֑רַח\rb* \rb “Now|נָ֖א\rb* \rb listen,|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb* \rb you sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Levi!|לֵוִֽי׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Is it not enough|הַמְעַ֣ט\rb* \rb for|מִכֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb you that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb has separated you|הִבְדִּיל֩\rb* \rb from the congregation|מֵעֲדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and brought you near|לְהַקְרִ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to Himself|אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb to perform|לַעֲבֹ֗ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the work|עֲבֹדַת֙\rb* \rb at the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb tabernacle,|מִשְׁכַּ֣ן\rb* \rb and to stand|וְלַעֲמֹ֛ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb to minister to them?|לְשָׁרְתָֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb He has brought you near,|וַיַּקְרֵב֙\rb*\rb |אֹֽתְךָ֔\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb you and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your fellow|אַחֶ֥יךָ\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb Levites,|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |לֵוִ֖י\rb* \rb but you are seeking|וּבִקַּשְׁתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb the priesthood|כְּהֻנָּֽה׃\rb* \rb as well.|גַּם־\rb* \v 11 \rb Therefore,|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb it is you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your followers|עֲדָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb who have conspired|הַנֹּעָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD!|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb As for Aaron,|וְאַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb who|מַה־\rb* \rb is he|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you should grumble|תִלּוֹנוּ\rb* \rb against him?”|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb*\rb |לִקְרֹ֛א\rb* \rb Dathan|לְדָתָ֥ן\rb* \rb and Abiram,|וְלַאֲבִירָ֖ם\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Eliab,|אֱלִיאָ֑ב\rb* \rb but they said,|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb “We will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb come!|נַעֲלֶֽה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Is it not enough|הַמְעַ֗ט\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you have brought us up|הֶֽעֱלִיתָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb out of a land|מֵאֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֤ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָב֙\rb* \rb and honey|וּדְבַ֔שׁ\rb* \rb to kill us|לַהֲמִיתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb in the wilderness?|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Must you also|גַּם־\rb* \rb appoint yourself as ruler|תִשְׂתָּרֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |הִשְׂתָּרֵֽר׃\rb* \rb over us?|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \v 14 \rb Moreover,|אַ֡ף\rb* \rb you have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb brought us|הֲבִ֣יאֹתָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶרֶץ֩\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֨ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֤ב\rb* \rb and honey|וּדְבַשׁ֙\rb* \rb or given|וַתִּ֨תֶּן־\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb an inheritance|נַחֲלַ֖ת\rb* \rb of fields|שָׂדֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and vineyards.|וָכָ֑רֶם\rb* \rb Will you gouge out|תְּנַקֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb the eyes|הַעֵינֵ֞י\rb* \rb of these|הָהֵ֛ם\rb* \rb men?|הָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb No, we will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb come!”|נַעֲלֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Then Moses|לְמֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb became very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb angry|וַיִּ֤חַר\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb regard|תֵּ֖פֶן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb their offering.|מִנְחָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb I have not|לֹ֠א\rb* \rb taken|נָשָׂ֔אתִי\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb donkey|חֲמ֨וֹר\rb* \rb from them|מֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb or mistreated|הֲרֵעֹ֖תִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a single|אַחַ֥ד\rb* \rb one of them.”|מֵהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Korah,|קֹ֔רַח\rb* \rb “You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your followers|עֲדָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb are to appear|הֱי֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb tomorrow—|מָחָֽר׃\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and they|וָהֵ֛ם\rb* \rb and Aaron.|וְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \v 17 \rb Each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb is to take|וּקְח֣וּ׀\rb* \rb his censer,|מַחְתָּת֗וֹ\rb* \rb place|וּנְתַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb incense|קְטֹ֔רֶת\rb* \rb in it,|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and present|וְהִקְרַבְתֶּ֞ם\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb it|מַחְתָּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD—|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb 250|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb censers.|מַחְתֹּ֑ת\rb* \rb You|וְאַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb are to present your censers as well.”|מַחְתָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb So each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְח֞וּ\rb* \rb his censer,|מַחְתָּת֗וֹ\rb* \rb put|וַיִּתְּנ֤וּ\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb and incense|קְטֹ֑רֶת\rb* \rb in it,|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽיַּעַמְד֗וּ\rb* \rb with Moses|וּמֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹֽן׃\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֛תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \v 19 \rb When Korah|קֹ֙רַח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had gathered|וַיַּקְהֵ֨ל\rb* \rb his whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb the glory|כְבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation.|הָעֵדָֽה׃פ\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 21 \rb “Separate yourselves|הִבָּ֣דְל֔וּ\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb congregation|הָעֵדָ֣ה\rb* \rb so that I may consume|וַאַכַלֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb in an instant.”|כְּרָֽגַע׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb But Moses and Aaron fell|וַיִּפְּל֤וּ\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “O God,|אֵ֕ל\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the spirits|הָרוּחֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb flesh,|בָּשָׂ֑ר\rb* \rb when one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb sins,|יֶחֱטָ֔א\rb* \rb will You be angry|תִּקְצֹֽף׃פ\rb* \rb with|וְעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation?”|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb*
\s1 Moses Separates the People
\p \v 23 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 24 \rb “Tell|דַּבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb to move away|הֵֽעָלוּ֙\rb* \rb from|מִסָּבִ֔יב\rb* \rb the dwellings|לְמִשְׁכַּן־\rb* \rb of Korah,|קֹ֖רַח\rb* \rb Dathan,|דָּתָ֥ן\rb* \rb and Abiram.”|וַאֲבִירָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Dathan|דָּתָ֣ן\rb* \rb and Abiram,|וַאֲבִירָ֑ם\rb* \rb and the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb followed|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb him.|אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb* \v 26 \rb And he warned|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the congregation,|הָעֵדָ֜ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “Move away|ס֣וּרוּ\rb* \rb now|נָ֡א\rb* \rb from|מֵעַל֩\rb* \rb the tents|אָהֳלֵ֨י\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb wicked|הָֽרְשָׁעִים֙\rb* \rb men.|הָאֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb Do not|וְאַֽל־\rb* \rb touch|תִּגְּע֖וּ\rb* \rb anything|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb that belongs|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to them,|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb you will be swept away|תִּסָּפ֖וּ\rb* \rb because of all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their sins.”|חַטֹּאתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb So they moved away|וַיֵּעָל֗וּ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֧ל\rb* \rb the dwellings|מִשְׁכַּן־\rb* \rb of Korah,|קֹ֛רֶח\rb* \rb Dathan,|דָּתָ֥ן\rb* \rb and Abiram.|וַאֲבִירָ֖ם\rb* \rb Meanwhile,|מִסָּבִ֑יב\rb* \rb Dathan|וְדָתָ֨ן\rb* \rb and Abiram|וַאֲבִירָ֜ם\rb* \rb had come out|יָצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb and stood|נִצָּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb at the entrances|פֶּ֚תַח\rb* \rb to their tents|אָֽהֳלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb with their wives|וּנְשֵׁיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and children|וּבְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and infants.|וְטַפָּֽם׃\rb*
\s1 The Earth Swallows Korah
\p \v 28 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֒\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb* \rb “This is how|בְּזֹאת֙\rb* \rb you will know|תֵּֽדְע֔וּן\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֔נִי\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb things,|הַֽמַּעֲשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb it was not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb my own doing:|מִלִּבִּֽי׃\rb* \v 29 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb men die|יְמֻת֣וּן\rb* \rb a natural death,|כְּמ֤וֹת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb or if they suffer|יִפָּקֵ֖ד\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb the fate|וּפְקֻדַּת֙\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb men,|הָ֣אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb sent me.|שְׁלָחָֽנִי׃\rb* \v 30 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb brings about|יִבְרָ֣א\rb* \rb something unprecedented,|בְּרִיאָ֞ה\rb* \rb and the earth|הָאֲדָמָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opens|וּפָצְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb its mouth|פִּ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and swallows|וּבָלְעָ֤ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb belongs to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb so that they go down|וְיָרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb alive|חַיִּ֖ים\rb* \rb into Sheol,|שְׁאֹ֑לָה\rb* \rb then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb have treated|נִֽאֲצ֛וּ\rb* \rb the LORD with contempt.”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb As soon as Moses had finished|כְּכַלֹּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb saying|לְדַבֵּ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this,|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb the ground|הָאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb beneath them|תַּחְתֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb split open,|וַתִּבָּקַ֥ע\rb* \v 32 \rb and the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opened|וַתִּפְתַּ֤ח\rb* \rb its mouth|פִּ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and swallowed|וַתִּבְלַ֥ע\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their households—|בָּתֵּיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb |וְאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Korah’s|לְקֹ֔רַח\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb men|הָאָדָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their possessions.|הָרֲכֽוּשׁ׃\rb* \v 33 \rb They|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּ֨רְד֜וּ\rb* \rb alive|חַיִּ֖ים\rb* \rb into Sheol|שְׁאֹ֑לָה\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb they owned.|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb The earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb closed|וַתְּכַ֤ס\rb* \rb over them,|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and they vanished|וַיֹּאבְד֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the assembly.|הַקָּהָֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb At their cries,|לְקֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb around them|סְבִיבֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb fled,|נָ֣סוּ\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb saying,|אָֽמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “The earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb may|פֶּן־\rb* \rb swallow us too!”|תִּבְלָעֵ֖נוּ\rb* \v 35 \rb And fire|וְאֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb came forth|יָצְאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and consumed|וַתֹּ֗אכַל\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the 250|הַחֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb who were offering|מַקְרִיבֵ֖י\rb* \rb the incense.|הַקְּטֹֽרֶת׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Censers Reserved for Holy Use
\p \v 36 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 37 \rb “Tell|אֱמֹ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֜ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb to remove|וְיָרֵ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the censers|הַמַּחְתֹּת֙\rb* \rb from|מִבֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the flames|הַשְּׂרֵפָ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb to scatter|זְרֵה־\rb* \rb the coals|הָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb far away,|הָ֑לְאָה\rb* \rb because|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb the censers are holy.|קָדֵֽשׁוּ׃\rb* \v 38 \rb |אֵ֡ת\rb* \rb As for the censers|מַחְתּוֹת֩\rb* \rb of those|הָאֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb who sinned|הַֽחַטָּאִ֨ים\rb* \rb at the cost of their own lives,|בְּנַפְשֹׁתָ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְעָשׂ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb hammer them into|רִקֻּעֵ֤י\rb* \rb sheets|פַחִים֙\rb* \rb to overlay|צִפּ֣וּי\rb* \rb the altar,|לַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb these were presented|הִקְרִיבֻ֥ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and so have become holy.|וַיִּקְדָּ֑שׁוּ\rb* \rb They will serve as|וְיִֽהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb a sign|לְא֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the Israelites.”|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb So Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb censers|מַחְתּ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb brought|הִקְרִ֖יבוּ\rb* \rb by those who had been burned up,|הַשְּׂרֻפִ֑ים\rb* \rb and he had them hammered out|וַֽיְרַקְּע֖וּם\rb* \rb to overlay|צִפּ֥וּי\rb* \rb the altar,|לַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \v 40 \rb just as|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb commanded him|דִּבֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb This was to be a reminder|זִכָּר֞וֹן\rb* \rb to the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb that|לְ֠מַעַן\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb outsider|זָ֗ר\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb is|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb a descendant|מִזֶּ֤רַע\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb should approach|יִקְרַ֜ב\rb* \rb to offer|לְהַקְטִ֥יר\rb* \rb incense|קְטֹ֖רֶת\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb lest he become|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb like Korah|כְקֹ֙רַח֙\rb* \rb and his followers.|וְכַ֣עֲדָת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*
\s1 Murmuring and Plague
\r \ref 1 Corinthians 10:1–13|1CO 10:1-13\ref*)
\p \v 41 \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֤ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb grumbled|וַיִּלֹּ֜נוּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “You|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb have killed|הֲמִתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb people!”|עַ֥ם\rb* \v 42 \rb But|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb when the congregation|הָֽעֵדָה֙\rb* \rb gathered|בְּהִקָּהֵ֤ל\rb* \rb against them,|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּפְנוּ֙\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb and suddenly the cloud|הֶעָנָ֑ן\rb* \rb covered it|כִסָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and the glory|כְּב֥וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb appeared.|וַיֵּרָ֖א\rb*
\p \v 43 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵֽד׃פ\rb* \v 44 \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 45 \rb “Get away|הֵרֹ֗מּוּ\rb* \rb from|מִתּוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb congregation|הָעֵדָ֣ה\rb* \rb so that I may consume|וַאֲכַלֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb in an instant.”|כְּרָ֑גַע\rb* \rb And Moses and Aaron fell|וַֽיִּפְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb facedown.|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 46 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your censer,|הַ֠מַּחְתָּה\rb* \rb place|וְתֶן־\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֜שׁ\rb* \rb from|עָלֶ֨יהָ\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |וְשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb in it,|מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb and add incense.|קְטֹ֔רֶת\rb* \rb Go|וְהוֹלֵ֧ךְ\rb* \rb quickly|מְהֵרָ֛ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and make atonement|וְכַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb for them,|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb wrath|הַקֶּ֛צֶף\rb* \rb has come|יָצָ֥א\rb* \rb out from|מִלִּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD;|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the plague|הַנָּֽגֶף׃\rb* \rb has begun.”|הֵחֵ֥ל\rb*
\p \v 47 \rb So Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb took the censer|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb had ordered|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb and ran|וַיָּ֙רָץ֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the midst|תּ֣וֹך\rb* \rb of the assembly.|הַקָּהָ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb And seeing that the plague|הַנֶּ֖גֶף\rb* \rb had begun|הֵחֵ֥ל\rb* \rb among the people,|בָּעָ֑ם\rb*\rb |וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb he offered the incense|הַקְּטֹ֔רֶת\rb* \rb and made atonement|וַיְכַפֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \v 48 \rb He stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb between|בֵּֽין־\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb the living|הַֽחַיִּ֑ים\rb* \rb and the dead,|הַמֵּתִ֖ים\rb* \rb and the plague|הַמַּגֵּפָֽה׃\rb* \rb was halted.|וַתֵּעָצַ֖ר\rb* \v 49 \rb |וַיִּהְי֗וּ\rb* \rb But those who died|הַמֵּתִים֙\rb* \rb from the plague|בַּמַּגֵּפָ֔ה\rb* \rb numbered 14,700,|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb*\rb |וּשְׁבַ֣ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֑וֹת\rb* \rb in addition to|מִלְּבַ֥ד\rb* \rb those who had died|הַמֵּתִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb account|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of Korah.|קֹֽרַח׃\rb*
\p \v 50 \rb Then Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb since the plague|וְהַמַּגֵּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb had been halted.|נֶעֱצָֽרָה׃פ\rb*
\c 17
\s1 Aaron’s Staff Buds
\p \v 1 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said to|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Speak|דַּבֵּ֣ר׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb and take|וְקַ֣ח\rb* \rb from them|מֵֽאִתָּ֡ם\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb staffs,|מַטּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb one|מַטֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |מַטֶּה֩\rb*\rb |אָ֜ב\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֤ת\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֨ית\rb* \rb from the leader|נְשִֽׂיאֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb of each|כָּל־\rb* \rb tribe.|אֲבֹתָ֔ם\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb Write|תִּכְתֹּ֖ב\rb* \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb man’s name|שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his staff,|מַטֵּֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb write|תִּכְתֹּ֖ב\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the staff|מַטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Levi,|לֵוִ֑י\rb* \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb there must be one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb staff|מַטֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb for the head|לְרֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb of each tribe.|אֲבוֹתָֽם׃\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \v 4 \rb Place the staffs|וְהִנַּחְתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb in the Tent|בְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the Testimony,|הָֽעֵד֔וּת\rb*\f + \fr 17:4 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments; also in verse 10.\f* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I meet|אִוָּעֵ֥ד\rb* \rb with you.|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb* \v 5 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb The staff|מַטֵּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb belonging to the man|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I choose|אֶבְחַר־\rb* \rb will sprout,|יִפְרָ֑ח\rb* \rb and I will rid|וַהֲשִׁכֹּתִ֣י\rb* \rb Myself|מֵֽעָלַ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb of the constant grumbling|תְּלֻנּוֹת֙\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |הֵ֥ם\rb*\rb |מַלִּינִ֖ם\rb* \rb against you.”|עֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb and each|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb of their leaders|נְשִֽׂיאֵיהֶ֡ם\rb* \rb gave him|וַיִּתְּנ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֣יו׀\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb staff—|מַטֶּה֩\rb*  \rb one|מַטֶּ֨ה\rb* \rb for each|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb of the leaders|לְנָשִׂ֤יא\rb* \rb of their tribes,|אֲבֹתָ֔ם\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb staffs in all.|מַטּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb And Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb staff|וּמַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb was among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb them.|מַטּוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb placed|וַיַּנַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the staffs|הַמַּטֹּ֖ת\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb in the Tent|בְּאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb of the Testimony.|הָעֵדֻֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֗ת\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb entered|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of the Testimony|הָעֵד֔וּת\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb that Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb staff,|מַטֵּֽה־\rb* \rb representing the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Levi,|לֵוִ֑י\rb* \rb had sprouted,|פָּרַ֥ח\rb* \rb put forth|וַיֹּ֤צֵֽא\rb* \rb buds,|פֶ֙רַח֙\rb* \rb blossomed,|וַיָּ֣צֵֽץ\rb*\rb |צִ֔יץ\rb* \rb and produced|וַיִּגְמֹ֖ל\rb* \rb almonds.|שְׁקֵדִֽים׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought out|וַיֹּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the staffs|הַמַּטֹּת֙\rb* \rb from the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb They saw them,|וַיִּרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb and each man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְח֖וּ\rb* \rb his own staff.|מַטֵּֽהוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Put|הָשֵׁ֞ב\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb staff|מַטֵּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb back in front of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Testimony,|הָעֵד֔וּת\rb* \rb to be kept|לְמִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb as a sign|לְא֖וֹת\rb* \rb for the rebellious,|לִבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |מֶ֑רִי\rb* \rb so that you may put an end|וּתְכַ֧ל\rb* \rb to their grumbling|תְּלוּנֹּתָ֛ם\rb* \rb against Me,|מֵעָלַ֖י\rb* \rb lest|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb they die.”|יָמֻֽתוּ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |עָשָֽׂה׃ס\rb* \rb had commanded him.|צִוָּ֧ה\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Then the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Look,|הֵ֥ן\rb* \rb we are perishing!|גָּוַ֛עְנוּ\rb* \rb We are lost;|אָבַ֖דְנוּ\rb* \rb we are all|כֻּלָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb lost!|אָבָֽדְנוּ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Anyone|כֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb who comes near|הַקָּרֵ֧ב׀\rb*\rb |הַקָּרֵ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|מִשְׁכַּ֥ן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will die.|יָמ֑וּת\rb*\rb |הַאִ֥ם\rb* \rb Are we all|תַּ֖מְנוּ\rb* \rb going to perish?”|לִגְוֺֽעַ׃ס\rb*
\c 18
\s1 Duties of Priests and Levites
\p \v 1 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb* \rb “You|אַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb and your father’s|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb house|וּבֵית־\rb* \rb must bear|תִּשְׂא֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the iniquity involving|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb the sanctuary.|הַמִּקְדָּ֑שׁ\rb* \rb And you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb alone|אִתָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb must bear|תִּשְׂא֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the iniquity involving|עֲוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb your priesthood.|כְּהֻנַּתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb But bring|הַקְרֵ֣ב\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb also|וְגַ֣ם\rb* \rb your brothers|אַחֶיךָ֩\rb* \rb from the tribe|מַטֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb of Levi,|לֵוִ֜י\rb* \rb the tribe|שֵׁ֤בֶט\rb* \rb of your father,|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb that they may join|וְיִלָּו֥וּ\rb* \rb you|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and assist|וִֽישָׁרְת֑וּךָ\rb* \rb you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of the Testimony.|הָעֵדֻֽת׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And they shall attend|וְשָֽׁמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to your duties|מִֽשְׁמַרְתְּךָ֔\rb* \rb and to all the duties|וּמִשְׁמֶ֖רֶת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb of the Tent;|הָאֹ֑הֶל\rb*\rb |אַךְ֩\rb* \rb but|אֶל־\rb* \rb they must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb come near|יִקְרָ֔בוּ\rb* \rb to the furnishings|כְּלֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֤דֶשׁ\rb* \rb or|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the altar,|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb both|גַם־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּֽם׃\rb* \rb will die.|יָמֻ֥תוּ\rb* \v 4 \rb They are to join|וְנִלְו֣וּ\rb* \rb you|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and attend|וְשָֽׁמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb to the duties|מִשְׁמֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb doing all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the work|עֲבֹדַ֣ת\rb* \rb at the Tent;|הָאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb but no|לֹא־\rb* \rb outsider|וְזָ֖ר\rb* \rb may come near|יִקְרַ֥ב\rb* \rb you.|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb And you shall attend|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb to the duties|מִשְׁמֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb of the altar,|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb so that wrath|קֶ֖צֶף\rb* \rb may not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb fall|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb again.|ע֛וֹד\rb* \v 6 \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb I Myself|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb have selected|לָקַ֙חְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your fellow|אֲחֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb as a gift|מַתָּנָ֤ה\rb* \rb to you,|לָכֶ֞ם\rb* \rb dedicated|נְתֻנִים֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to perform|לַעֲבֹ֕ד\rb* \rb the service|עֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb for the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 7 \rb But only you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |אִ֠תְּךָ\rb* \rb shall attend|תִּשְׁמְר֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to your priesthood|כְּהֻנַּתְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb for everything|לְכָל־\rb* \rb concerning|דְּבַ֧ר\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֛חַ\rb* \rb and what is inside|וּלְמִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb the veil,|לַפָּרֹ֖כֶת\rb* \rb and you are to perform that service.|וַעֲבַדְתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb I am giving|אֶתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you the work|עֲבֹדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the priesthood|כְּהֻנַּתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as a gift,|מַתָּנָ֗ה\rb* \rb but any outsider|וְהַזָּ֥ר\rb* \rb who comes near the sanctuary|הַקָּרֵ֖ב\rb* \rb must be put to death.”|יוּמָֽת׃ס\rb*
\s1 Offerings for Priests and Levites
\p \v 8 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹן֒\rb* \rb “Behold,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb have put|נָתַ֣תִּֽי\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in charge|מִשְׁמֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb of My offerings.|תְּרוּמֹתָ֑י\rb* \rb As for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the sacred offerings|קָדְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites,|יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb* \rb I have given them|נְתַתִּ֧ים\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֨\rb* \rb and your sons|וּלְבָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb as a portion|לְמָשְׁחָ֛ה\rb* \rb and a permanent|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb statute.|לְחָק־\rb* \v 9 \rb |זֶֽה־\rb* \rb A portion of|מִן־\rb* \rb the most holy offerings|מִקֹּ֥דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb reserved from the fire|הָאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb yours.|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb From all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the offerings|קָ֠רְבָּנָם\rb*\rb |לְֽכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they render|יָשִׁ֣יבוּ\rb* \rb to Me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb as most holy offerings,|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |קָֽדָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb whether grain offerings|מִנְחָתָ֞ם\rb*\rb |וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb or sin offerings|חַטָּאתָ֗ם\rb*\rb |וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb or guilt offerings,|אֲשָׁמָם֙\rb* \rb that part belongs|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb and your sons.|וּלְבָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb You are to eat it|תֹּאכֲלֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb as a most holy offering,|בְּקֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*\f + \fr 18:10 \ft Or \fqa You are to eat it in a most holy place\f* \rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָר֙\rb* \rb may eat|יֹאכַ֣ל\rb* \rb it.|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb You shall regard it|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb as holy.|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |לָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb And this|וְזֶה־\rb* \rb is yours as well:|לְּךָ֞\rb* \rb the offering|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of their gifts,|מַתָּנָ֗ם\rb* \rb along with all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the wave offerings|תְּנוּפֹת֮\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites.|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb I have given this|נְתַתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb and your sons|וּלְבָנֶ֧יךָ\rb* \rb and daughters|וְלִבְנֹתֶ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |אִתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb as a permanent|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb statute.|לְחָק־\rb* \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb ceremonially clean person|טָה֥וֹר\rb* \rb in your household|בְּבֵיתְךָ֖\rb* \rb may eat it.|יֹאכַ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 12 \rb I give you|יִתְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the freshest|חֵ֣לֶב\rb* \rb olive oil|יִצְהָ֔ר\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the finest|חֵ֖לֶב\rb* \rb new wine|תִּיר֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and grain|וְדָגָ֑ן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Israelites give|נְתַתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb as their firstfruits.|רֵאשִׁיתָ֛ם\rb* \v 13 \rb The firstfruits|בִּכּוּרֵ֞י\rb* \rb of everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb in their land|בְּאַרְצָ֛ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they bring|יָבִ֥יאוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will belong|יִהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb to you.|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb ceremonially clean person|טָה֥וֹר\rb* \rb in your household|בְּבֵיתְךָ֖\rb* \rb may eat them.|יֹאכֲלֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb devoted thing|חֵ֥רֶם\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb belongs to you.|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \v 15 \rb The firstborn|פֶּ֣טֶר\rb*\rb |רֶ֠חֶם\rb*\rb |לְֽכָל־\rb* \rb of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb womb,|בָּשָׂ֞ר\rb* \rb whether|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb man|בָּאָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb or beast,|וּבַבְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb that is offered|יַקְרִ֧יבוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb belongs|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb to you.|לָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb But|אַ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb you must surely redeem|פָּדֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |תִפְדֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb every firstborn|בְּכ֣וֹר\rb* \rb son|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and|תִּפְדֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb every firstborn male|בְּכֽוֹר־\rb* \rb of unclean|הַטְּמֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb animals.|הַבְּהֵמָ֥ה\rb* \v 16 \rb You are to pay the redemption price|וּפְדוּיָו֙\rb* \rb for a month-old male|מִבֶּן־\rb*\rb |חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |תִּפְדֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb according to your valuation:|בְּעֶ֨רְכְּךָ֔\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb of silver,|כֶּ֛סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 18:16 \fqa 5 shekels \ft is approximately 2 ounces or 57 grams of silver.\f* \rb according to the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb shekel,|בְּשֶׁ֣קֶל\rb* \rb which|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb gerahs.|גֵּרָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 18:16 \fqa 20 gerahs \ft is equivalent to one shekel (approximately 0.4 ounces or 11.4 grams).\f*
\p \v 17 \rb But|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb redeem|תִפְדֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּֽכוֹר־\rb* \rb of an ox,|שׁ֡וֹר\rb* \rb a sheep,|כֶּ֜שֶׂב\rb*\rb |אֽוֹ־\rb*\rb |בְכ֥וֹר\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb*\rb |בְכ֨וֹר\rb* \rb a goat;|עֵ֛ז\rb* \rb they|הֵ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are holy.|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb You are to splatter|תִּזְרֹ֤ק\rb* \rb their blood|דָּמָ֞ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and burn|תַּקְטִ֔יר\rb* \rb their fat|חֶלְבָּ֣ם\rb* \rb as a food offering,|אִשֶּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb a pleasing|נִיחֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb aroma|לְרֵ֥יחַ\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 18 \rb And their meat|וּבְשָׂרָ֖ם\rb* \rb belongs|יִהְיֶה־\rb* \rb to you,|לָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb just as the breast|כַּחֲזֵ֧ה\rb* \rb and right|הַיָּמִ֖ין\rb* \rb thigh|וּכְשׁ֥וֹק\rb* \rb of the wave offering|הַתְּנוּפָ֛ה\rb* \rb belong|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb to you.|לְךָ֥\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb All|כֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֳּדָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb offerings|תְּרוּמֹ֣ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֮\rb* \rb present|יָרִ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֒\rb* \rb I give|נָתַ֣תִּֽי\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb and to your sons|וּלְבָנֶ֧יךָ\rb* \rb and daughters|וְלִבְנֹתֶ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |אִתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb as a permanent|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb statute.|לְחָק־\rb* \rb It|הִוא֙\rb* \rb is a permanent|עוֹלָ֥ם\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִית֩\rb* \rb of salt|מֶ֨לַח\rb*\f + \fr 18:19 \ft That is, a perpetual covenant\f* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb and your offspring.”|וּלְזַרְעֲךָ֥\rb*\rb |אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb “You will have no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb inheritance|תִנְחָ֔ל\rb* \rb in their land,|בְּאַרְצָם֙\rb* \rb nor|לֹא־\rb* \rb will you have|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb any portion|וְחֵ֕לֶק\rb* \rb among them.|בְּתוֹכָ֑ם\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb am your portion|חֶלְקְךָ֙\rb* \rb and your inheritance|וְנַחֲלָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֛תִּי\rb* \rb to the Levites|וְלִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |לֵוִ֔י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the tithes|מַֽעֲשֵׂ֥ר\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb as an inheritance|לְנַחֲלָ֑ה\rb* \rb in return for|חֵ֤לֶף\rb* \rb the work|עֲבֹֽדָתָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb do,|עֹֽבְדִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the service|עֲבֹדַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 22 \rb No|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb may the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb come|אֶל־\rb* \rb near|יִקְרְב֥וּ\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb or they will incur|לָשֵׂ֥את\rb* \rb guilt|חֵ֖טְא\rb* \rb and die.|לָמֽוּת׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb The Levites|הַלֵּוִ֜י\rb*\rb |ה֗וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to perform|וְעָבַ֨ד\rb* \rb the work|עֲבֹדַת֙\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb and they|וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb must bear|יִשְׂא֣וּ\rb* \rb their iniquity.|עֲוֺנָ֑ם\rb* \rb This is a permanent|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb statute|חֻקַּ֤ת\rb* \rb for the generations to come.|לְדֹרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb The Levites will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb receive an inheritance|יִנְחֲל֖וּ\rb*\rb |נַחֲלָֽה׃\rb* \rb among|וּבְתוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \v 24 \rb For|כִּ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb to the Levites|לַלְוִיִּ֖ם\rb* \rb as their inheritance|לְנַחֲלָ֑ה\rb* \rb the tithe|מַעְשַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb present|יָרִ֤ימוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb as a contribution.|תְּרוּמָ֔ה\rb* \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֙\rb* \rb I told them|אָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that they would not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb receive an inheritance|יִנְחֲל֖וּ\rb*\rb |נַחֲלָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb among|בְּתוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb the Israelites.”|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb instructed|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 26 \rb “Speak|תְּדַבֵּר֮\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֣ם\rb* \rb and tell them:|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶם֒\rb* \rb ‘When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you receive|תִ֠קְחוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tithe|הַֽמַּעֲשֵׂ֗ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֧תִּי\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |מֵאִתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb as your inheritance,|בְּנַחֲלַתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb you must present|וַהֲרֵמֹתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb part|מִן־\rb* \rb of it|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb as an offering|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD—|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb a tithe|מַעֲשֵׂ֖ר\rb* \rb of the tithe.|הַֽמַּעֲשֵֽׂר׃\rb* \v 27 \rb Your offering|תְּרוּמַתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb will be reckoned|וְנֶחְשַׁ֥ב\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as grain|כַּדָּגָן֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the threshing floor|הַגֹּ֔רֶן\rb* \rb or juice|וְכַֽמְלֵאָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the winepress.|הַיָּֽקֶב׃\rb* \v 28 \rb So|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb are to present|תָּרִ֤ימוּ\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb an offering|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the tithes|מַעְשְׂרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you receive|תִּקְח֔וּ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb from the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and from these|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you are to give|וּנְתַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb offering|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb to Aaron|לְאַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb the priest.|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \v 29 \rb You must present|תָּרִ֕ימוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the offering|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb due the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb from|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the best|חֶלְבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb of every|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb gift,|מַתְּנֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the holiest part|מִקְדְּשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of it.’|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Therefore say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb to the Levites,|אֲלֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb ‘When you have presented|בַּהֲרִֽימְכֶ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the best part,|חֶלְבּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb it will be reckoned|וְנֶחְשַׁב֙\rb* \rb to you|לַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb as the produce|כִּתְבוּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the threshing floor|גֹּ֖רֶן\rb*\rb |וְכִתְבוּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb or winepress.|יָֽקֶב׃\rb* \v 31 \rb And you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb and your households|וּבֵֽיתְכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb may eat the rest of it anywhere;|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |מָק֔וֹם\rb* \rb it|הוּא֙\rb* \rb is the compensation|שָׂכָ֥ר\rb* \rb for|חֵ֥לֶף\rb* \rb your work|עֲבֹֽדַתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb at the Tent|בְּאֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 32 \rb Once you have presented|בַּהֲרִֽימְכֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the best part|חֶלְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of it,|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb you will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb incur|תִשְׂא֤וּ\rb* \rb guilt|חֵ֔טְא\rb* \rb because of it.|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb But|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb defile|תְחַלְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb the sacred offerings|קָדְשֵׁ֧י\rb*\rb |בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb or else|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb you will die.’”|תָמֽוּתוּ׃פ\rb*
\c 19
\s1 The Red Heifer
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “This|זֹ֚את\rb* \rb is the statute|חֻקַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the law|הַתּוֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb has commanded:|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Instruct|דַּבֵּ֣ר׀\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb to bring|וְיִקְח֣וּ\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶיךָ֩\rb* \rb an unblemished|תְּמִימָ֗ה\rb* \rb red|אֲדֻמָּ֜ה\rb* \rb heifer|פָרָ֨ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb has no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb defect|מ֔וּם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb and has never|לֹא־\rb* \rb been placed|עָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb under a yoke.|עֹֽל׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Give|וּנְתַתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֖ר\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb and he will have it brought|וְהוֹצִ֤יא\rb*\rb |אֹתָהּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb outside|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and slaughtered|וְשָׁחַ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb in his presence.|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֧ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֞ח\rb* \rb some of its blood|מִדָּמָ֖הּ\rb* \rb on his finger|בְּאֶצְבָּע֑וֹ\rb* \rb and sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֞ה\rb* \rb it|מִדָּמָ֖הּ\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb*\rb |נֹ֨כַח\rb* \rb the front|פְּנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the Tent|אֹֽהֶל־\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵ֛ד\rb* \v 5 \rb Then the heifer|הַפָּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb must be burned|וְשָׂרַ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in his sight.|לְעֵינָ֑יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Its hide,|עֹרָ֤הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its flesh,|בְּשָׂרָהּ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and its blood|דָּמָ֔הּ\rb* \rb are to be burned,|יִשְׂרֹֽף׃\rb* \rb along with|עַל־\rb* \rb its dung.|פִּרְשָׁ֖הּ\rb* \v 6 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֣ח\rb* \rb cedar|אֶ֛רֶז\rb* \rb wood,|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb hyssop,|וְאֵז֖וֹב\rb* \rb and scarlet wool|וּשְׁנִ֣י\rb*\rb |תוֹלָ֑עַת\rb* \rb and throw|וְהִשְׁלִ֕יךְ\rb* \rb them|אֶל־\rb* \rb onto|תּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the burning|שְׂרֵפַ֥ת\rb* \rb heifer.|הַפָּרָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb must wash|וְכִבֶּ֨ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֜יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֤ץ\rb* \rb his body|בְּשָׂרוֹ֙\rb* \rb in water;|בַּמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb after that|וְאַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb he may enter|יָב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp,|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb but he|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb will be ceremonially unclean|וְטָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening.|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb* \v 8 \rb The one who burned|וְהַשֹּׂרֵ֣ף\rb* \rb the heifer|אֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb must also wash|יְכַבֵּ֤ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָיו֙\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb his body|בְּשָׂר֖וֹ\rb*\rb |בַּמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb in water,|בַּמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb and he too will be ceremonially unclean|וְטָמֵ֖א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening.|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb who is ceremonially clean|טָה֗וֹר\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb is to gather up|וְאָסַ֣ף׀\rb* \rb the ashes|אֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of the heifer|הַפָּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb and store them|וְהִנִּ֛יחַ\rb* \rb in a ceremonially clean|טָה֑וֹר\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֣וֹם\rb* \rb outside|מִח֥וּץ\rb* \rb the camp.|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb They must be|וְ֠הָיְתָה\rb* \rb kept|לְמִשְׁמֶ֛רֶת\rb* \rb by the congregation|לַעֲדַ֨ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל\rb* \rb for preparing the water|לְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of purification;|נִדָּ֖ה\rb* \rb this is|הִֽוא׃\rb* \rb for purification from sin.|חַטָּ֥את\rb* \v 10 \rb The man who has gathered up|הָאֹסֵ֨ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ashes|אֵ֤פֶר\rb* \rb of the heifer|הַפָּרָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb must also wash|וְ֠כִבֶּס\rb* \rb his clothes,|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb and he will be ceremonially unclean|וְטָמֵ֖א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening.|הָעָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb This|וְֽהָיְתָ֞ה\rb* \rb is a permanent|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb statute|לְחֻקַּ֥ת\rb* \rb for the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb and for the foreigner|וְלַגֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb residing|הַגָּ֥ר\rb* \rb among them.|בְּתוֹכָ֖ם\rb*
\s1 Purification of the Unclean
\p \v 11 \rb Whoever touches|הַנֹּגֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb dead|בְּמֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |אָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb body|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb will be unclean|וְטָמֵ֖א\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days.|יָמִֽים׃\rb* \v 12 \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb must purify himself|יִתְחַטָּא־\rb* \rb with the water|ב֞וֹ\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֛י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֧וֹם\rb* \rb and on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb day;|וּבַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb then he will be clean.|יִטְהָ֑ר\rb* \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he does not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb purify himself|יִתְחַטָּ֜א\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֛י\rb*\rb |וּבַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb and seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֖י\rb* \rb days,|בַּיּ֧וֹם\rb* \rb he will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be clean.|יִטְהָֽר׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Anyone|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb who touches|הַנֹּגֵ֡עַ\rb* \rb a human|הָאָדָ֨ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |יָמ֜וּת\rb* \rb corpse|בְּמֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֶפֶשׁ֩\rb* \rb and fails|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to purify|יִתְחַטָּ֗א\rb* \rb himself|אֶת־\rb* \rb defiles|טִמֵּ֔א\rb* \rb the tabernacle|מִשְׁכַּ֤ן\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb That|הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb person|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb must be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from Israel.|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb He remains|יִהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb unclean,|טָמֵ֣א\rb* \rb because|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the water|מֵ֨י\rb* \rb of purification|נִדָּ֜ה\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb been sprinkled|זֹרַ֤ק\rb* \rb on him,|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and his uncleanness|טֻמְאָת֥וֹ\rb* \rb is still on him.|ע֖וֹד\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb This|זֹ֚את\rb* \rb is the law|הַתּוֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a person|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb dies|יָמ֣וּת\rb* \rb in a tent:|בְּאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb Everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who enters|הַבָּ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the tent|הָאֹ֙הֶל֙\rb* \rb and everyone|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb already in the tent|בָּאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֖א\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days,|יָמִֽים׃\rb* \v 15 \rb and any|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb open|פָת֔וּחַ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb container|כְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb without|אֵין־\rb* \rb a lid|צָמִ֥יד\rb* \rb fastened|פָּתִ֖יל\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb is unclean.|טָמֵ֖א\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Anyone|וְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the open field|פְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb touches|יִגַּ֜ע\rb* \rb someone who has been killed|בַּֽחֲלַל־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb has died of natural causes,|בְמֵ֔ת\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb anyone who touches a human|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb bone|בְעֶ֥צֶם\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb a grave,|בְקָ֑בֶר\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֖א\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days.|יָמִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb For the purification of the unclean person,|לַטָּמֵ֔א\rb* \rb take|וְלָֽקְחוּ֙\rb* \rb some of the ashes|מֵעֲפַ֖ר\rb* \rb of the burnt|שְׂרֵפַ֣ת\rb* \rb sin offering,|הַֽחַטָּ֑את\rb* \rb put them|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb a jar,|כֶּֽלִי׃\rb* \rb and pour fresh|חַיִּ֖ים\rb* \rb water|מַ֥יִם\rb*\f + \fr 19:17 \ft Or \fqa flowing water \ft or \fqa living water\f* \rb over them.|עָלָ֛יו\rb* \v 18 \rb Then a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb who is ceremonially clean|טָהוֹר֒\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֨ח\rb* \rb some hyssop,|אֵז֜וֹב\rb* \rb dip|וְטָבַ֣ל\rb* \rb it in the water,|בַּמַּיִם֮\rb* \rb and sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the tent,|הָאֹ֙הֶל֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the furnishings,|הַכֵּלִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and the people|הַנְּפָשׁ֖וֹת\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were|הָֽיוּ־\rb* \rb there.|שָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb He is also to sprinkle the one who touched|הַנֹּגֵ֗עַ\rb* \rb a bone,|בַּעֶ֙צֶם֙\rb* \rb a grave,|בַקָּֽבֶר׃\rb* \rb or a person who has died|בַמֵּ֖ת\rb*\rb |א֥וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb been slain.|בֶֽחָלָ֔ל\rb*\rb |א֥וֹ\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb The man who is ceremonially clean|הַטָּהֹר֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb is to sprinkle|וְהִזָּ֤ה\rb* \rb the unclean person|הַטָּמֵ֔א\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֖י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb and on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֑י\rb* \rb day.|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb After he purifies|וְחִטְּאוֹ֙\rb* \rb the unclean person on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day,|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the one being cleansed must wash|וְכִבֶּ֧ס\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֛יו\rb* \rb and bathe|וְרָחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb in water,|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb and that evening|בָּעָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb he will be clean.|וְטָהֵ֥ר\rb* \v 20 \rb But if a person|וְאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is unclean|יִטְמָא֙\rb* \rb does not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb purify|יִתְחַטָּ֔א\rb* \rb himself,|הַהִ֖וא\rb* \rb he|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb will be cut off|וְנִכְרְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the assembly,|הַקָּהָ֑ל\rb* \rb because|כִּי֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he has defiled|טִמֵּ֗א\rb* \rb the sanctuary|מִקְדַּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb The water|מֵ֥י\rb* \rb of purification|נִדָּ֛ה\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb been sprinkled|זֹרַ֥ק\rb* \rb on him;|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is unclean.|טָמֵ֥א\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb This|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb is a permanent|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb statute|לְחֻקַּ֣ת\rb* \rb for the people:|לָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb The one who sprinkles|וּמַזֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the water|מֵֽי־\rb* \rb of purification|הַנִּדָּה֙\rb* \rb must wash|יְכַבֵּ֣ס\rb* \rb his clothes,|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb and whoever touches|וְהַנֹּגֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb the water|בְּמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of purification|הַנִּדָּ֔ה\rb* \rb will be unclean|יִטְמָ֖א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening.|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb* \v 22 \rb Anything|וְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the unclean|הַטָּמֵ֖א\rb* \rb person touches|יִגַּע־\rb* \rb will become unclean,|יִטְמָ֑א\rb* \rb and anyone|וְהַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who touches it|הַנֹּגַ֖עַת\rb* \rb will be unclean|תִּטְמָ֥א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening.”|הָעָֽרֶב׃פ\rb*
\c 20
\s1 Water from the Rock
\r \ref Exodus 17:1–7|EXO 17:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the first|הָֽרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֨עֵדָ֤ה\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb* \rb entered|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb the Wilderness|מִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Zin|צִן֙\rb* \rb and|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb stayed|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Kadesh.|בְּקָדֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb There|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb Miriam|מִרְיָ֔ם\rb* \rb died|וַתָּ֤מָת\rb* \rb and was buried.|וַתִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Now there was|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb for the congregation,|לָעֵדָ֑ה\rb* \rb so they gathered|וַיִּקָּ֣הֲל֔וּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron.|אַהֲרֹֽן׃\rb* \v 3 \rb The people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb quarreled|וַיָּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “If only|וְל֥וּ\rb* \rb we had perished|גָוַ֛עְנוּ\rb*\rb |בִּגְוַ֥ע\rb* \rb with our brothers|אַחֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD!|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb Why|וְלָמָ֤ה\rb* \rb have you brought|הֲבֵאתֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb* \rb for us|אֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb* \rb and our livestock|וּבְעִירֵֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb to die|לָמ֣וּת\rb* \rb here?|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \v 5 \rb Why|וְלָמָ֤ה\rb* \rb have you led us up|הֶֽעֱלִיתֻ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to bring|לְהָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb wretched|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb place?|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb It is not|לֹ֣א׀\rb* \rb a place|מְק֣וֹם\rb* \rb of grain,|זֶ֗רַע\rb* \rb figs,|וּתְאֵנָ֤ה\rb* \rb vines,|וְגֶ֙פֶן֙\rb* \rb or pomegranates—|וְרִמּ֔וֹן\rb*  \rb and there is no|אַ֖יִן\rb* \rb water|וּמַ֥יִם\rb* \rb to drink!”|לִשְׁתּֽוֹת׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹא֩\rb* \rb from the presence|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the assembly|הַקָּהָ֗ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֙תַח֙\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb They fell facedown,|וַֽיִּפְּל֖וּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and the glory|כְבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֥א\rb* \rb to them.|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb* \v 7 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 8 \rb “Take|קַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the staff|הַמַּטֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb and assemble|וְהַקְהֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the congregation.|הָעֵדָה֙\rb* \rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and your brother|אָחִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb are to speak|וְדִבַּרְתֶּ֧ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the rock|הַסֶּ֛לַע\rb* \rb while they watch,|לְעֵינֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and it will pour out|וְנָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb its water.|מֵימָ֑יו\rb* \rb You will bring out|וְהוֹצֵאתָ֨\rb* \rb water|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the rock|הַסֶּ֔לַע\rb* \rb and provide drink|וְהִשְׁקִיתָ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and their livestock.”|בְּעִירָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the staff|הַמַּטֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb from the LORD’s|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb presence,|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb he had been commanded.|צִוָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb* \rb and Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gathered|וַיַּקְהִ֜לוּ\rb* \rb the assembly|הַקָּהָ֖ל\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb front|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the rock,|הַסָּ֑לַע\rb* \rb and Moses said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|לָהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “Listen|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb* \rb now,|נָא֙\rb* \rb you rebels,|הַמֹּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb must we bring you water|מָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb out|נוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb of|הֲמִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb rock?”|הַסֶּ֣לַע\rb* \v 11 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb raised|וַיָּ֨רֶם\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֗וֹ\rb* \rb and struck|וַיַּ֧ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the rock|הַסֶּ֛לַע\rb* \rb twice|פַּעֲמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb with his staff,|בְּמַטֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb so that a great amount of|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb water|מַ֣יִם\rb* \rb gushed out,|וַיֵּצְאוּ֙\rb* \rb and the congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and their livestock|וּבְעִירָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb were able to drink.|וַתֵּ֥שְׁתְּ\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb Aaron,|אַהֲרֹן֒\rb* \rb “Because|יַ֚עַן\rb* \rb you did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb trust|הֶאֱמַנְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb Me|בִּ֔י\rb* \rb to show My holiness|לְהַ֨קְדִּישֵׁ֔נִי\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb bring|תָבִ֙יאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb assembly|הַקָּהָ֣ל\rb* \rb into the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb them.”|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb These|הֵ֚מָּה\rb* \rb were the waters|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Meribah,|מְרִיבָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 20:13 \fqa Meribah \ft means \fqa quarreling\ft ; also in verse 24; see \ref Exodus 17:7|EXO 17:7\ref*.\f* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb quarreled|רָב֥וּ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and He showed His holiness|וַיִּקָּדֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb among them.|בָּֽם׃ס\rb*
\s1 Edom Refuses Passage
\p \v 14 \rb From Kadesh,|מִקָּדֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֛ים\rb* \rb to tell|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Edom,|אֱד֑וֹם\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֣יךָ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the hardship|הַתְּלָאָ֖ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb has befallen us,|מְצָאָֽתְנוּ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb how our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּרְד֤וּ\rb* \rb to Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יְמָה\rb* \rb where we lived|וַנֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb*\rb |בְּמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb years.|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb The Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb mistreated|וַיָּרֵ֥עוּ\rb* \rb us|לָ֛נוּ\rb* \rb and our fathers,|וְלַאֲבֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \v 16 \rb and when we cried out|וַנִּצְעַ֤ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb He heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb our voice,|קֹלֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb an angel,|מַלְאָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and brought us|וַיֹּצִאֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb out of Egypt.|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb*
\p \rb Now look,|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb are in Kadesh,|בְקָדֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb a city|עִ֖יר\rb* \rb on the edge|קְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of your territory.|גְבוּלֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 17 \rb Please|נָּ֣א\rb* \rb let us pass|נַעְבְּרָה־\rb* \rb through your land.|בְאַרְצֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb We will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb go through|נַעֲבֹר֙\rb* \rb any field|בְּשָׂדֶ֣ה\rb* \rb or vineyard,|וּבְכֶ֔רֶם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb drink|נִשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb water|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb from any well.|בְאֵ֑ר\rb* \rb We will stay on|נֵלֵ֗ךְ\rb* \rb the King’s|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Highway;|דֶּ֧רֶךְ\rb* \rb we will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb turn|נִטֶּה֙\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֣ין\rb* \rb or to the left|וּשְׂמֹ֔אול\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb we have passed through|נַעֲבֹ֖ר\rb* \rb your territory.”|גְּבוּלֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb But Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb* \rb answered,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “You may not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb travel|תַעֲבֹ֖ר\rb* \rb through our land,|בִּ֑י\rb* \rb or we will come out|אֵצֵ֥א\rb* \rb and confront you|לִקְרָאתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb with the sword.”|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb “We will stay|נַעֲלֶה֒\rb* \rb on the main road,”|בַּֽמְסִלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֘ל\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֥יו\rb* \rb “and if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb we|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb or our herds|וּמִקְנַ֔י\rb* \rb drink|נִשְׁתֶּה֙\rb* \rb your water,|מֵימֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb we will pay|וְנָתַתִּ֖י\rb* \rb for it.|מִכְרָ֑ם\rb* \rb There will be no|אֵין־\rb* \rb problem;|דָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb only|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb let us pass through|אֶֽעֱבֹֽרָה׃\rb* \rb on foot.”|בְּרַגְלַ֥י\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb But Edom|אֱדוֹם֙\rb* \rb insisted,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “You may not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb pass through.”|תַעֲבֹ֑ר\rb* \rb And they came out|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb to confront the Israelites|לִקְרָאת֔וֹ\rb* \rb with a large|כָּבֵ֖ד\rb* \rb army|בְּעַ֥ם\rb* \rb and a strong|חֲזָקָֽה׃\rb* \rb hand.|וּבְיָ֥ד\rb* \v 21 \rb So Edom|אֱד֗וֹם\rb* \rb refused|וַיְמָאֵ֣ן׀\rb* \rb to allow|נְתֹן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to pass|עֲבֹ֖ר\rb* \rb through their territory,|בִּגְבֻל֑וֹ\rb* \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb turned away|וַיֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb from them.|מֵעָלָֽיו׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Death of Aaron
\p \v 22 \rb After they had set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from Kadesh,|מִקָּדֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֧אוּ\rb* \rb to Mount|הָהָֽר׃\rb* \rb Hor.|הֹ֥ר\rb* \v 23 \rb And at Mount|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb Hor,|בְּהֹ֣ר\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of the land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Edom,|אֱד֖וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and Aaron,|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 24 \rb “Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb will be gathered|יֵאָסֵ֤ף\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his people;|עַמָּ֔יו\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb enter|יָבֹא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb the Israelites,|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb because|עַ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb both of you rebelled|מְרִיתֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against My command|פִּ֖י\rb* \rb at the waters|לְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Meribah.|מְרִיבָֽה׃\rb* \v 25 \rb Take|קַ֚ח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֖ר\rb* \rb and bring them up|וְהַ֥עַל\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb Mount|הָהָֽר׃\rb* \rb Hor.|הֹ֥ר\rb* \v 26 \rb Remove|וְהַפְשֵׁ֤ט\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb priestly garments|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb and put them on|וְהִלְבַּשְׁתָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Eleazar.|אֶלְעָזָ֣ר\rb* \rb Aaron|וְאַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb will be gathered to his people|יֵאָסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb and will die|וּמֵ֥ת\rb* \rb there.”|שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb had commanded,|צִוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and they climbed|וַֽיַּעֲלוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Mount|הָהָ֔ר\rb* \rb Hor|הֹ֣ר\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation.|הָעֵדָֽה׃\rb* \v 28 \rb After Moses|מֹשֶׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb had removed|וַיַּפְשֵׁט֩\rb* \rb Aaron’s|אַהֲרֹ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb garments|בְּגָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb and put them on|וַיַּלְבֵּ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Eleazar,|אֶלְעָזָ֣ר\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֛ן\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֧מָת\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb on top|בְּרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the mountain.|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb and Eleazar|וְאֶלְעָזָ֖ר\rb* \rb came down|וַיֵּ֧רֶד\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the mountain.|הָהָֽר׃\rb* \v 29 \rb When the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֑ן\rb* \rb had died,|גָוַ֖ע\rb* \rb the entire|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb* \rb mourned|וַיִּבְכּ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb for him|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb days.|י֔וֹם\rb*
\c 21
\s1 The Defeat of Arad
\p \v 1 \rb When the Canaanite|הַכְּנַעֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Arad,|עֲרָד֙\rb* \rb who lived|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in the Negev,|הַנֶּ֔גֶב\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֞ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb was coming|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb along the road|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb to Atharim,|הָאֲתָרִ֑ים\rb* \rb he attacked|וַיִּלָּ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and captured|וַיִּ֥שְׁבְּ׀\rb* \rb some|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb prisoners.|שֶֽׁבִי׃\rb* \v 2 \rb So Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb made|וַיִּדַּ֨ר\rb* \rb a vow|נֶ֛דֶר\rb* \rb to the LORD:|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb You will deliver|נָתֹ֨ן\rb*\rb |תִּתֵּ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb into our hands,|בְּיָדִ֔י\rb* \rb we will devote|וְהַֽחֲרַמְתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their cities to destruction.|עָרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*\f + \fr 21:2 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verse 3.\f*”
\p \v 3 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֨ע\rb* \rb Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb plea|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb and delivered up|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Canaanites.|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb Israel devoted|וַיַּחֲרֵ֥ם\rb* \rb them|אֶתְהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their cities to destruction;|עָרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb so they named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שֵׁם־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb Hormah.|חָרְמָֽה׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 21:3 \fqa Hormah \ft means \fqa destruction\ft .\f*
\s1 The Bronze Serpent
\p \v 4 \rb Then they set out|וַיִּסְע֞וּ\rb* \rb from Mount|הָהָר֙\rb* \rb Hor|מֵהֹ֤ר\rb* \rb along the route|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb to the Red|ס֔וּף\rb* \rb Sea,|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 21:4 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb in order to bypass|לִסְבֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Edom.|אֱד֑וֹם\rb* \rb But the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb grew impatient|וַתִּקְצַ֥ר\rb*\rb |נֶֽפֶשׁ־\rb* \rb on the journey|בַּדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb* \v 5 \rb |הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb against God|בֵּֽאלֹהִים֮\rb* \rb and against Moses:|וּבְמֹשֶׁה֒\rb* \rb “Why|לָמָ֤ה\rb* \rb have you led us up|הֶֽעֱלִיתֻ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to die|לָמ֖וּת\rb* \rb in the wilderness?|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb There is no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb or water,|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and we|וְנַפְשֵׁ֣נוּ\rb* \rb detest|קָ֔צָה\rb* \rb this wretched|הַקְּלֹקֵֽל׃\rb* \rb food!”|בַּלֶּ֖חֶם\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיְשַׁלַּ֨ח\rb* \rb venomous|הַשְּׂרָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb snakes|הַנְּחָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb among the people,|בָּעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb and many|רָ֖ב\rb*\rb |עַם־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb were bitten|וַֽיְנַשְּׁכ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and died.|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Then the people|הָעָ֨ם\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹא֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb “We have sinned|חָטָ֗אנוּ\rb* \rb by|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb speaking|דִבַּ֤רְנוּ\rb* \rb against the LORD|בַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb and against you.|וָבָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb Intercede|הִתְפַּלֵּל֙\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb so He will take|וְיָסֵ֥ר\rb* \rb the snakes|הַנָּחָ֑שׁ\rb* \rb away from us.”|מֵעָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb interceded|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb for|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Make|עֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb* \rb a fiery serpent|שָׂרָ֔ף\rb* \rb and mount|וְשִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a pole.|נֵ֑ס\rb*\rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb When anyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who is bitten|הַנָּשׁ֔וּךְ\rb* \rb looks at it,|וְרָאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb he will live.”|וָחָֽי׃\rb* \v 9 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a bronze|נְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb snake|נְחַ֣שׁ\rb* \rb and mounted|וַיְשִׂמֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb a pole.|הַנֵּ֑ס\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb anyone who|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb was bitten|נָשַׁ֤ךְ\rb* \rb looked|וְהִבִּ֛יט\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb*\rb |נְחַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb snake,|הַנָּחָשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he would live.|וָחָֽי׃\rb*
\s1 The Journey to Moab
