\p \v 21 \rb Then Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Sihon|סִיחֹ֥ן\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of the Amorites,|הָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 22 \rb “Let us pass|אֶעְבְּרָ֣ה\rb* \rb through your land.|בְאַרְצֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb We will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb turn aside into|נִטֶּה֙\rb* \rb any field|בְּשָׂדֶ֣ה\rb* \rb or vineyard,|וּבְכֶ֔רֶם\rb* \rb or|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb drink|נִשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb water|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb from any well.|בְאֵ֑ר\rb* \rb We will stay on|נֵלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb the King’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb Highway|בְּדֶ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb we have passed through|נַעֲבֹ֖ר\rb* \rb your territory.”|גְּבֻלֶֽךָ׃\rb*
