\c 22
\s1 Balak Summons Balaam
\p \v 1 \rb Then the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb traveled on|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb in the plains|בְּעַֽרְב֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb near the Jordan,|לְיַרְדֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb across from|מֵעֵ֖בֶר\rb* \rb Jericho.|יְרֵחֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Now Balak|בָּלָ֖ק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zippor|צִפּ֑וֹר\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb to the Amorites,|לָֽאֱמֹרִֽי׃\rb* \v 3 \rb and Moab|מוֹאָ֜ב\rb* \rb was terrified|וַיָּ֨גָר\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb were numerous.|רַב־\rb* \rb Indeed, Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb dreaded|וַיָּ֣קָץ\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 4 \rb So the Moabites|מוֹאָ֜ב\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Midian,|מִדְיָ֗ן\rb*\rb |עַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb “This horde|הַקָּהָל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will devour|יְלַחֲכ֤וּ\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb around us,|סְבִ֣יבֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb as an ox|הַשּׁ֔וֹר\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb licks up|כִּלְחֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb the grass|יֶ֣רֶק\rb* \rb of the field.”|הַשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb Since Balak|וּבָלָ֧ק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zippor|צִפּ֛וֹר\rb* \rb was king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Moab|לְמוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb at that|הַהִֽוא׃\rb* \rb time,|בָּעֵ֥ת\rb* \v 5 \rb he sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֜ים\rb* \rb to summon|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Beor|בְּע֗וֹר\rb* \rb at Pethor,|פְּ֠תוֹרָה\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb is by|עַל־\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֛ר\rb*\f + \fr 22:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\f* \rb in the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of his people.|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \rb “Behold,|הִ֠נֵּה\rb* \rb a people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb has come out|יָצָ֤א\rb* \rb of Egypt,”|מִמִּצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb said Balak.|לִקְרֹא־\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb |הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb “They cover|כִסָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the face|עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb and have settled|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb next to me.|מִמֻּלִֽי׃\rb* \v 6 \rb So please|נָּ֨א\rb* \rb come|לְכָה־\rb* \rb now|וְעַתָּה֩\rb* \rb and put a curse|אָֽרָה־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb people,|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they|הוּא֙\rb* \rb are too mighty|עָצ֥וּם\rb* \rb for me.|מִמֶּ֔נִּי\rb* \rb Perhaps I may|אוּלַ֤י\rb* \rb be able|אוּכַל֙\rb* \rb to defeat|נַכֶּה־\rb* \rb them|בּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and drive them out|וַאֲגָרְשֶׁ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the land;|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֗עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb that those|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you bless|תְּבָרֵךְ֙\rb* \rb are blessed,|מְבֹרָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and those|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you curse|תָּאֹ֖ר\rb* \rb are cursed.”|יוּאָֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb The elders|זִקְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָב֙\rb*\rb |וְזִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and Midian|מִדְיָ֔ן\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּ֨לְכ֜וּ\rb* \rb with the fees for divination|וּקְסָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb in hand.|בְּיָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb They came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and relayed|וַיְדַבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Balak.|בָלָֽק׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb “Spend|לִ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb the night|הַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb here,”|פֹה֙\rb* \rb Balaam replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “and I will give|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb you the answer|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb that|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb speaks|יְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to me.”|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb So the princes|שָׂרֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb stayed|וַיֵּשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Balaam.|בִּלְעָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and asked,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֛י\rb* \rb are these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb with you?”|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb And Balaam|בִּלְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb “Balak|בָּלָ֧ק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zippor,|צִפֹּ֛ר\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Moab,|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb sent me|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb this message:|אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \v 11 \rb ‘Behold,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb a people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb has come out|הַיֹּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and they cover|וַיְכַ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the face|עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of the land.|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb Now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb come|לְכָ֤ה\rb* \rb and put a curse|קָֽבָה־\rb* \rb on them|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb for me.|לִּי֙\rb* \rb Perhaps I may|אוּלַ֥י\rb* \rb be able|אוּכַ֛ל\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּ֥חֶם\rb* \rb against them|בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and drive them away.’”|וְגֵרַשְׁתִּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam,|בִּלְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb “Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go|תֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb with them.|עִמָּהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb You are not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb to curse|תָאֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this people,|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb are blessed.”|בָר֖וּךְ\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb So Balaam|בִּלְעָם֙\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֤קָם\rb* \rb the next morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balak’s|בָלָ֔ק\rb* \rb princes,|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb “Go back|לְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb your homeland,|אַרְצְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has refused|מֵאֵ֣ן\rb* \rb to let me|לְתִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb go|לַהֲלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb with you.”|עִמָּכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb And the princes|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb arose,|וַיָּק֙וּמוּ֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balak,|בָּלָ֑ק\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “Balaam|בִּלְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb refused|מֵאֵ֥ן\rb* \rb to come|הֲלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb with us.”|עִמָּֽנוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Then Balak|בָּלָ֑ק\rb* \rb sent|שְׁלֹ֣חַ\rb* \rb other|וַיֹּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb princes,|שָׂרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb more numerous|רַבִּ֥ים\rb* \rb and more distinguished|וְנִכְבָּדִ֖ים\rb* \rb than the first messengers.|מֵאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb They came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb Balak|בָּלָ֣ק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zippor|צִפּ֔וֹר\rb* \rb says:|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb ‘Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb let nothing|אַל־\rb* \rb hinder|תִמָּנַ֖ע\rb* \rb you from coming|מֵהֲלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \v 17 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will honor you|כַבֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb richly|מְאֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֲכַבֶּדְךָ֙\rb* \rb and do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb whatever|וְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you say.|תֹּאמַ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb So please|נָּא֙\rb* \rb come|וּלְכָה־\rb* \rb and put a curse|קָֽבָה־\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb on this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb people for me!’”|הָעָ֥ם\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb But Balaam|בִּלְעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֣עַן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Balak,|בָלָ֔ק\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb Balak|בָלָ֛ק\rb* \rb were to give|יִתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֥י\rb* \rb his house|בֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb full|מְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold,|וְזָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb I could|אוּכַ֗ל\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb anything small|קְטַנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb great|גְדוֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb to go beyond|לַעֲבֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the command|פִּי֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God.|אֱלֹהָ֔י\rb* \v 19 \rb So now,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb stay|שְׁב֨וּ\rb* \rb here|בָזֶ֛ה\rb* \rb overnight|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb as the others did,|גַּם־\rb*\rb |אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that I may find out|וְאֵ֣דְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb else|יֹּסֵ֥ף\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has to tell me.”|דַּבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |עִמִּֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb That night|לַיְלָה֒\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים׀\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָם֮\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Since|אִם־\rb* \rb these men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb have come|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to summon|לִקְרֹ֤א\rb* \rb you,|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb get up|ק֖וּם\rb* \rb and go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb with them,|אִתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb but you must only|וְאַ֗ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I tell you.”|אֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb* \v 21 \rb So in the morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָם֙\rb* \rb got up,|וַיָּ֤קָם\rb* \rb saddled|וַֽיַּחֲבֹ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his donkey,|אֲתֹנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the princes|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Moab.|מוֹאָֽב׃\rb*
\s1 The Angel and Balaam’s Donkey
\p \v 22 \rb Then God’s|אֱלֹהִים֮\rb* \rb anger|אַ֣ף\rb* \rb was kindled|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Balaam|הוּא֒\rb* \rb was going along,|הוֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and the angel|מַלְאַ֧ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 22:22 \ft Or \fqa Angel\ft ; here through the rest of chapter 22; corresponding pronouns may also be capitalized.\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb stood|וַיִּתְיַצֵּ֞ב\rb* \rb in the road|בַּדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb to oppose|לְשָׂטָ֣ן\rb* \rb him.|ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb Balaam|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb was riding|רֹכֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb his donkey,|אֲתֹנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and his two|וּשְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb servants|נְעָרָ֖יו\rb* \rb were with him.|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb When the donkey|הָאָתוֹן֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֣רֶא\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb standing|נִצָּ֣ב\rb* \rb in the road|בַּדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb with a drawn|שְׁלוּפָה֙\rb* \rb sword|וְחַרְבּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb in his hand,|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb she|הָֽאָתוֹן֙\rb* \rb turned|וַתֵּ֤ט\rb* \rb off|מִן־\rb* \rb the path|הַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb and went|וַתֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb into a field.|בַּשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb So Balaam|בִּלְעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb beat|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb her|הָ֣אָת֔וֹן\rb* \rb to return her|לְהַטֹּתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to the path.|הַדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Then the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb in a narrow passage|בְּמִשְׁע֖וֹל\rb* \rb between two vineyards,|הַכְּרָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb with walls|גָּדֵ֥ר\rb* \rb on either side.|מִזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְגָדֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |מִזֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 25 \rb And the donkey|הָאָת֜וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֨רֶא\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and pressed herself|וַתִּלָּחֵץ֙\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wall,|הַקִּ֔יר\rb* \rb crushing|וַתִּלְחַ֛ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Balaam’s|בִּלְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb foot|רֶ֥גֶל\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb it.|הַקִּ֑יר\rb* \rb So he beat her|לְהַכֹּתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb once again.|וַיֹּ֖סֶף\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb And the angel|מַלְאַךְ־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb moved|עֲב֑וֹר\rb* \rb on ahead|וַיּ֥וֹסֶף\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb in a narrow|צָ֔ר\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֣וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb there was no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb room|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb to turn|לִנְט֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֥ין\rb* \rb or left.|וּשְׂמֹֽאול׃\rb* \v 27 \rb When the donkey|הָֽאָתוֹן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֤רֶא\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb she lay down|וַתִּרְבַּ֖ץ\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb Balaam,|בִּלְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and he|בִּלְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb became furious|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb*\rb |אַ֣ף\rb* \rb and beat|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her|הָאָת֖וֹן\rb* \rb with his staff.|בַּמַּקֵּֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opened|וַיִּפְתַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the donkey’s|הָאָת֑וֹן\rb* \rb mouth,|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb and she said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Balaam,|לְבִלְעָם֙\rb* \rb “What|מֶה־\rb* \rb have I done|עָשִׂ֣יתִֽי\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have beaten me|הִכִּיתַ֔נִי\rb* \rb these|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb times?”|רְגָלִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָם֙\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the donkey,|לָֽאָת֔וֹן\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb “You have made a fool|הִתְעַלַּ֖לְתְּ\rb* \rb of me!|בִּ֑י\rb* \rb If|ל֤וּ\rb* \rb I had|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb a sword|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb in my hand,|בְּיָדִ֔י\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I would kill you|הֲרַגְתִּֽיךְ׃\rb* \rb right now!”|עַתָּ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb But the donkey|הָאָת֜וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Balaam,|בִּלְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb “Am I|אָנֹכִ֨י\rb* \rb not|הֲלוֹא֩\rb* \rb the donkey|אֲתֹֽנְךָ֜\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have ridden|רָכַ֣בְתָּ\rb*\rb |עָלַ֗י\rb* \rb all your life|מֵעֽוֹדְךָ֙\rb* \rb until today?|עַד־\rb*\rb |הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb Have I ever treated|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb this way|כֹּ֑ה\rb* \rb before?”|הַֽהַסְכֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |הִסְכַּ֔נְתִּי\rb*
\p \rb “No,”|לֹֽא׃\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opened|וַיְגַ֣ל\rb* \rb Balaam’s|בִלְעָם֒\rb* \rb eyes,|עֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb and he saw|וַיַּ֞רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb standing|נִצָּ֣ב\rb* \rb in the road|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb with a drawn|שְׁלֻפָ֖ה\rb* \rb sword|וְחַרְבּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb in his hand.|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb And Balaam bowed low|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb*\rb |וַיִּקֹּ֥ד\rb* \rb and fell facedown.|לְאַפָּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb The angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb asked him,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “Why|עַל־\rb*\rb |מָ֗ה\rb* \rb have you beaten|הִכִּ֙יתָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your donkey|אֲתֹ֣נְךָ֔\rb* \rb these|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb three|שָׁל֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb times?|רְגָלִ֑ים\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb have come out|יָצָ֣אתִי\rb* \rb to oppose you,|לְשָׂטָ֔ן\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your way|הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb is perverse|יָרַ֥ט\rb*\f + \fr 22:32 \ft Or \fqa reckless \ft or \fqa contrary\f* \rb before me.|לְנֶגְדִּֽי׃\rb* \v 33 \rb The donkey|הָֽאָת֔וֹן\rb* \rb saw me|וַתִּרְאַ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb and turned away|וַתֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb from me|לְפָנַ֔י\rb* \rb these|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb times.|רְגָלִ֑ים\rb* \rb If she had not|אוּלַי֙\rb* \rb turned away,|נָטְתָ֣ה\rb*\rb |מִפָּנַ֔י\rb* \rb then by now|עַתָּ֛ה\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I would surely have killed|הָרַ֖גְתִּי\rb* \rb you|אֹתְכָ֥ה\rb* \rb and let her|וְאוֹתָ֥הּ\rb* \rb live.”|הֶחֱיֵֽיתִי׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb “I have sinned,”|חָטָ֔אתִי\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֜ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb “for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb realize|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb were standing|נִצָּ֥ב\rb* \rb in the road|בַּדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb* \rb to confront me.|לִקְרָאתִ֖י\rb* \rb And now,|וְעַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb this is displeasing|רַ֥ע\rb* \rb in your sight,|בְּעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb I will go back|אָשׁ֥וּבָה\rb* \rb home.”|לִּֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb But the angel|מַלְאַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam,|בִּלְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb “Go|לֵ֚ךְ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the men,|הָ֣אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb but you are to speak|אֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |אֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb only|וְאֶ֗פֶס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I tell you.”|תְדַבֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb So Balaam|בִּלְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the princes|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Balak.|בָלָֽק׃\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb When Balak|בָּלָ֖ק\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Balaam|בִלְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb was coming,|בָ֣א\rb* \rb he went out|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb to meet him|לִקְרָאת֜וֹ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Moabite|מוֹאָ֗ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the Arnon|אַרְנֹ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb border,|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb at the edge|בִּקְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of his territory.|הַגְּבֽוּל׃\rb* \v 37 \rb And he|בָּלָ֜ק\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam,|בִּלְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb “Did I not|הֲלֹא֩\rb* \rb send you an urgent summons?|שָׁלֹ֨חַ\rb*\rb |שָׁלַ֤חְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |לִקְרֹא־\rb*\rb |לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb did you not come|הָלַ֖כְתָּ\rb* \rb to me?|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb Am I really|הַֽאֻמְנָ֔ם\rb* \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb able|אוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb to reward you richly?”|כַּבְּדֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 38 \rb “See,|הִֽנֵּה־\rb* \rb I have come|בָ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb to you,”|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֜ם\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |בָּלָ֗ק\rb* \rb |עַתָּ֕ה\rb*\rb |הֲיָכ֥וֹל\rb* \rb “but can|אוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb I say|דַּבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb just anything?|מְא֑וּמָה\rb* \rb I must speak|אֲדַבֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb only the word|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb puts|יָשִׂ֧ים\rb* \rb in my mouth.”|בְּפִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb So Balaam|בִּלְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb accompanied|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb Balak,|בָּלָ֑ק\rb* \rb and they came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb*\rb |קִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb to Kiriath-huzoth.|חֻצֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 40 \rb Balak|בָּלָ֖ק\rb* \rb sacrificed|וַיִּזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb cattle|בָּקָ֣ר\rb* \rb and sheep,|וָצֹ֑אן\rb* \rb and he gave portions|וַיְשַׁלַּ֣ח\rb* \rb to Balaam|לְבִלְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and the princes|וְלַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were with him.|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 41 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb The next morning,|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb Balak|בָּלָק֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and brought him|וַֽיַּעֲלֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb up to|בָּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb Bamoth-baal.|בָּ֑עַל\rb* \rb From there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb he could see|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb the outskirts of the camp|קְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb*
\c 23
\s1 Balaam’s First Oracle
\p \v 1 \rb Then Balaam|בִּלְעָם֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balak,|בָּלָ֔ק\rb* \rb “Build|בְּנֵה־\rb* \rb for me|לִ֥י\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּחֹ֑ת\rb* \rb here,|בָזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb and prepare|וְהָכֵ֥ן\rb* \rb for me|לִי֙\rb*\rb |בָּזֶ֔ה\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb bulls|פָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb rams.”|אֵילִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb So Balak|בָּלָ֔ק\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb had instructed,|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb and Balak|בָּלָ֧ק\rb* \rb and Balaam|וּבִלְעָ֛ם\rb* \rb offered|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb a bull|פָּ֥ר\rb* \rb and a ram|וָאַ֖יִל\rb* \rb on each altar.|בַּמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb “Stay|הִתְיַצֵּב֮\rb* \rb here by|עַל־\rb* \rb your burnt offering|עֹלָתֶךָ֒\rb* \rb while I am gone,”|וְאֵֽלְכָ֗ה\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֜ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Balak.|לְבָלָ֗ק\rb* \rb “Perhaps|אוּלַ֞י\rb*\rb |יִקָּרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb will meet with me.|לִקְרָאתִ֔י\rb*\rb |וּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb And whatever|מַה־\rb* \rb He reveals to me,|יַּרְאֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb I will tell|וְהִגַּ֣דְתִּי\rb* \rb you.”|לָ֑ךְ\rb*
\p \rb So Balaam went off|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to a barren height,|שֶֽׁפִי׃\rb* \v 4 \rb and God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb met|וַיִּקָּ֥ר\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb him.|בִּלְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb “I have set up|עָרַ֔כְתִּי\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb altars,”|הַֽמִּזְבְּחֹת֙\rb* \rb Balaam said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb “and on each altar|בַּמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \rb I have offered|וָאַ֛עַל\rb* \rb a bull|פָּ֥ר\rb* \rb and a ram.”|וָאַ֖יִל\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb put|וַיָּ֧שֶׂם\rb* \rb a message|דָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb in Balaam’s|בִלְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb mouth,|בְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb saying,|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb “Return|שׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balak|בָּלָ֖ק\rb* \rb and|וְכֹ֥ה\rb* \rb give him this message.”|תְדַבֵּֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So he returned|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb to Balak,|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb who|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb was standing|נִצָּ֖ב\rb* \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb his burnt offering,|עֹלָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the princes|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Moab.|מוֹאָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb And Balaam lifted up|וַיִּשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb an oracle,|מְשָׁל֖וֹ\rb* \rb saying:|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Balak|בָלָ֤ק\rb* \rb brought me|יַנְחֵ֨נִי\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Aram,|אֲ֠רָם\rb*
\q2 \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb from the mountains|מֵֽהַרְרֵי־\rb* \rb of the east.|קֶ֔דֶם\rb*
\q1 \rb ‘Come,’ he said,|לְכָה֙\rb* \rb ‘put a curse|אָֽרָה־\rb* \rb on Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb for me;|לִּ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb come|וּלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and denounce|זֹעֲמָ֥ה\rb* \rb Israel!’|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb How|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb can I curse those whom|קַבֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb God|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb cursed?|אֶקֹּ֔ב\rb*
\q2 \rb How|וּמָ֣ה\rb* \rb can I denounce those whom|אֶזְעֹ֔ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb denounced?|זָעַ֖ם\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I see them|אֶרְאֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb from atop|מֵרֹ֤אשׁ\rb* \rb the rocky cliffs,|צֻרִים֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and I watch them|אֲשׁוּרֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb from the hills.|וּמִגְּבָע֖וֹת\rb*
\q1 \rb Behold,|הֶן־\rb* \rb a people|עָם֙\rb* \rb dwelling|יִשְׁכֹּ֔ן\rb* \rb apart,|לְבָדָ֣ד\rb*
\q2 \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb reckoning themselves|יִתְחַשָּֽׁב׃\rb* \rb among the nations.|וּבַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb can count|מָנָה֙\rb* \rb the dust|עֲפַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*
\q2 \rb or number|וּמִסְפָּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb even a fourth|רֹ֣בַע\rb* \rb of Israel?|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*
\q1 \rb Let me|נַפְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb die|תָּמֹ֤ת\rb* \rb the death|מ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the righteous;|יְשָׁרִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb let my end|אַחֲרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb be|וּתְהִ֥י\rb* \rb like theirs!”|כָּמֹֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Then Balak|בָּלָק֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam,|בִּלְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb “What|מֶ֥ה\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֖יתָ\rb* \rb to me?|לִ֑י\rb* \rb I brought you here|לְקַחְתִּ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to curse|לָקֹ֤ב\rb* \rb my enemies,|אֹיְבַי֙\rb* \rb and behold,|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb you have only blessed them!”|בֵּרַ֥כְתָּ\rb*\rb |בָרֵֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But Balaam replied,|וַיַּ֖עַן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “Should I not|הֲלֹ֗א\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb speak|לְדַבֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb exactly what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb puts|יָשִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb in my mouth?”|בְּפִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶשְׁמֹ֖ר\rb*
\s1 Balaam’s Second Oracle
\p \v 13 \rb Then Balak|בָּלָ֗ק\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb “Please come|לְךָ\rb*\rb |נָּ֨א\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֜י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb another|אַחֵר֙\rb* \rb place|מָק֤וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you can see them.|תִּרְאֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb You will only|אֶ֚פֶס\rb* \rb see|תִרְאֶ֔ה\rb* \rb the outskirts of their camp—|קָצֵ֣הוּ\rb*  \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |תִרְאֶ֑ה\rb* \rb all of them.|וְכֻלּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb And from there,|מִשָּֽׁם׃\rb* \rb curse them|וְקָבְנוֹ־\rb* \rb for me.”|לִ֖י\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb So Balak took him|וַיִּקָּחֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to the field|שְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Zophim,|צֹפִ֔ים\rb* \rb to the|אֶל־\rb* \rb top|רֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb of Pisgah,|הַפִּסְגָּ֑ה\rb* \rb where he built|וַיִּ֙בֶן֙\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּחֹ֔ת\rb* \rb and offered|וַיַּ֛עַל\rb* \rb a bull|פָּ֥ר\rb* \rb and a ram|וָאַ֖יִל\rb* \rb on each altar.|בַּמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Balaam said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balak,|בָּלָ֔ק\rb* \rb “Stay|הִתְיַצֵּ֥ב\rb* \rb here|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb your burnt offering|עֹלָתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb while I|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb meet the LORD|אִקָּ֥רֶה\rb* \rb over there.”|כֹּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb met|וַיִּקָּ֤ר\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and put|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb* \rb a message|דָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb in his mouth,|בְּפִ֑יו\rb* \rb saying,|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb “Return|שׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balak|בָּלָ֖ק\rb* \rb and speak|תְדַבֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb what I tell you.”|וְכֹ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb So he returned|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to Balak,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb who was standing|נִצָּב֙\rb* \rb there|וְהִנּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb his burnt offering|עֹ֣לָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb with|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb the princes|וְשָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Moab.|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb*
\p \rb “What|מַה־\rb* \rb did the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb say?”|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb Balak|בָּלָ֔ק\rb* \rb asked.|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then Balaam lifted up|וַיִּשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb an oracle,|מְשָׁל֖וֹ\rb* \rb saying:|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Arise,|ק֤וּם\rb* \rb O Balak,|בָּלָק֙\rb* \rb and listen;|וּֽשֲׁמָ֔ע\rb*
