\s1 Balak Dismisses Balaam
\p \v 10 \rb Then Balak’s|בָּלָק֙\rb* \rb anger|אַ֤ף\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam,|בִּלְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and he struck his hands|כַּפָּ֑יו\rb* \rb together|וַיִּסְפֹּ֖ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |בָּלָ֜ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Balaam,|בִּלְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb “I summoned you|קְרָאתִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to curse|לָקֹ֤ב\rb* \rb my enemies,|אֹֽיְבַי֙\rb* \rb but behold,|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb you have persisted in blessing them|בֵּרַ֣כְתָּ\rb*\rb |בָרֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb these|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb times.|פְּעָמִֽים׃\rb* \v 11 \rb Therefore , flee|בְּרַח־\rb* \rb at once|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb home!|מְקוֹמֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb I said|אָמַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb* \rb I would reward you richly,|כַּבֵּ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֲכַבֶּדְךָ֔\rb* \rb but instead|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has denied|מְנָעֲךָ֥\rb* \rb your reward.”|מִכָּבֽוֹד׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Balaam|בִּלְעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb Balak,|בָּלָ֑ק\rb* \rb “Did I not|הֲלֹ֗א\rb* \rb already|גַּ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb tell|דִּבַּ֥רְתִּי\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb the messengers|מַלְאָכֶ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you sent me|שָׁלַ֥חְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֖י\rb* \v 13 \rb that even if|אִם־\rb* \rb Balak|בָלָ֜ק\rb* \rb were to give|יִתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֨י\rb* \rb his house|בֵיתוֹ֮\rb* \rb full|מְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold,|וְזָהָב֒\rb* \rb I could|אוּכַ֗ל\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb anything of my own accord,|מִלִּבִּ֑י\rb* \rb good|טוֹבָ֛ה\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb bad,|רָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb to go beyond|לַעֲבֹר֙\rb* \rb the command|פִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the LORD?|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb I must speak|יְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb says.|אֲדַבֵּֽר׃\rb* \v 14 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb I am going back|הוֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb to my people,|לְעַמִּ֑י\rb* \rb but come,|לְכָה֙\rb* \rb let me warn you|אִיעָ֣צְךָ֔\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֜ה\rb* \rb to your people|לְעַמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb in the days|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb to come.”|בְּאַחֲרִ֥ית\rb*
