\c 25
\s1 Moab Seduces Israel
\r \ref 1 Corinthians 10:1–13|1CO 10:1-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb While Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb was staying|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Shittim,|בַּשִּׁטִּ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 25:1 \ft Or \fqa Acacia Grove\f* \rb the men|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb began|וַיָּ֣חֶל\rb* \rb to indulge in sexual immorality|לִזְנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the daughters|בְּנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Moab,|מוֹאָֽב׃\rb* \v 2 \rb who also invited|וַתִּקְרֶ֣אןָ\rb* \rb them|לָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb to the sacrifices|לְזִבְחֵ֖י\rb* \rb for their gods.|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ן\rb* \rb And the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb ate|וַיֹּ֣אכַל\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוּ֖וּ\rb* \rb to these gods.|לֵֽאלֹהֵיהֶֽן׃\rb* \v 3 \rb So Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb joined in worshiping|וַיִּצָּ֥מֶד\rb* \rb Baal of Peor,|פְּע֑וֹר\rb* \rb and the anger|אַ֥ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against them.|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֚ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the leaders|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and execute|וְהוֹקַ֥ע\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb in|נֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb broad daylight|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb* \rb before the LORD,|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb so that His|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb fierce|חֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb anger|אַף־\rb* \rb may turn away|וְיָשֹׁ֛ב\rb* \rb from Israel.”|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the judges|שֹׁפְטֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb “Each of you must kill|הִרְגוּ֙\rb* \rb all of his men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb who have joined in worshiping|הַנִּצְמָדִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לְבַ֥עַל\rb* \rb Baal of Peor.”|פְּעֽוֹר׃\rb*
\s1 The Zeal of Phinehas
\p \v 6 \rb Just then|וְהִנֵּ֡ה\rb* \rb an Israelite|מִבְּנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ֩\rb*\rb |בָּ֗א\rb* \rb brought|וַיַּקְרֵ֤ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his family|אֶחָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a Midianite woman|הַמִּדְיָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וּלְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֣ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb while they|וְהֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb were weeping|בֹכִ֔ים\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 7 \rb On seeing this,|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb* \rb Phinehas|פִּֽינְחָס֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eleazar,|אֶלְעָזָ֔ר\rb* \rb the son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the assembly,|הָֽעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a spear|רֹ֖מַח\rb* \rb in his hand,|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb followed|וַ֠יָּבֹא\rb*\rb |אַחַ֨ר\rb* \rb the Israelite|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb his tent,|הַקֻּבָּ֗ה\rb* \rb and drove the spear through|וַיִּדְקֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb both of them—|שְׁנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb through the Israelite|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and on through|אֶל־\rb* \rb the belly|קֳבָתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb of the woman.|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*
\p \rb So the plague|הַמַּגֵּפָ֔ה\rb* \rb against|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb was halted,|וַתֵּֽעָצַר֙\rb* \v 9 \rb |וַיִּהְי֕וּ\rb* \rb but those who died|הַמֵּתִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the plague|בַּמַּגֵּפָ֑ה\rb* \rb numbered 24,000.|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃פ\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 11 \rb “Phinehas|פִּֽינְחָ֨ס\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eleazar,|אֶלְעָזָ֜ר\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֣ן\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb has turned|הֵשִׁ֤יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִי֙\rb* \rb away from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the Israelites;|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb for he was zealous|בְּקַנְא֥וֹ\rb* \rb for My sake|קִנְאָתִ֖י\rb* \rb among them,|בְּתוֹכָ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that I did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb consume|כִלִּ֥יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in My zeal.|בְּקִנְאָתִֽי׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Declare,|אֱמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb therefore,|לָכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb that|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I am granting|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb him|ל֛וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb of peace.|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 13 \rb It will be|וְהָ֤יְתָה\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֖ית\rb* \rb of permanent|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb priesthood|כְּהֻנַּ֣ת\rb* \rb for him|לּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb and his descendants,|וּלְזַרְע֣וֹ\rb* \rb because|תַּ֗חַת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb he was zealous|קִנֵּא֙\rb* \rb for his God|לֵֽאלֹהָ֔יו\rb* \rb and made atonement|וַיְכַפֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the Israelites.”|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb The name|וְשֵׁם֩\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of the Israelite|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb who was slain|הַמֻּכֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |הֻכָּה֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Midianite woman|הַמִּדְיָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb was Zimri|זִמְרִ֖י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Salu,|סָל֑וּא\rb* \rb the leader|נְשִׂ֥יא\rb* \rb of a Simeonite|לַשִּׁמְעֹנִֽי׃\rb* \rb family.|אָ֖ב\rb*\rb |בֵֽית־\rb* \v 15 \rb And the name|וְשֵׁ֨ם\rb* \rb of the slain|הַמֻּכָּ֛ה\rb* \rb Midianite|הַמִּדְיָנִ֖ית\rb* \rb woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֧ה\rb* \rb was Cozbi,|כָּזְבִּ֣י\rb* \rb the daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Zur,|צ֑וּר\rb* \rb a tribal|אֻמּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb chief|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of a Midianite|בְּמִדְיָ֖ן\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb family.|אָ֛ב\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֵּאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 17 \rb “Attack|צָר֖וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Midianites|הַמִּדְיָנִ֑ים\rb* \rb and strike them dead.|וְהִכִּיתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they|הֵם֙\rb* \rb assailed|צֹרְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb deceitfully|בְּנִכְלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they seduced|נִכְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the matter|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of Peor|פְּע֑וֹר\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb*\rb |דְּבַ֞ר\rb* \rb their sister|אֲחֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb Cozbi,|כָּזְבִּ֨י\rb* \rb the daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of the Midianite|מִדְיָן֙\rb* \rb leader,|נְשִׂ֤יא\rb* \rb the woman who was killed|הַמֻּכָּ֥ה\rb* \rb on the day|בְיוֹם־\rb* \rb the plague|הַמַּגֵּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|עַל־\rb* \rb because of|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb Peor.”|פְּעֽוֹר׃\rb*
