\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the plague had ended,|הַמַּגֵּפָ֑ה פ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֧ל\rb* \rb and Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֛ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֥ן\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “Take a census|שְׂא֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |רֹ֣אשׁ׀\rb* \rb of the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֣ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb by the houses|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of their fathers—|אֲבֹתָ֑ם\rb*  \rb all those|כָּל־\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּ֨ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֛ה\rb* \rb or older|וָמַ֖עְלָה\rb* \rb who can serve|יֹצֵ֥א\rb* \rb in the army|צָבָ֖א\rb* \rb of Israel.”|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So on the plains|בְּעַֽרְבֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the Jordan,|יַרְדֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb across from Jericho,|יְרֵח֖וֹ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb and Eleazar|וְאֶלְעָזָ֧ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb issued|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb the instruction,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 4 \rb “Take a census of the men twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb years of age|מִבֶּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb or older,|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb*\f + \fr 26:4 \fqa Take a census of the men \ft is implied but not included in the Hebrew; see verse 2.\f* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has commanded|צִוָּ֨ה\rb* \rb Moses.”|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*
