\c 32
\s1 The Tribes East of the Jordan
\r \ref Deuteronomy 3:12–22|DEU 3:12-22\ref*; \ref Joshua 13:8–14|JOS 13:8-14\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now the Reubenites|לִבְנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֛ן\rb* \rb and Gadites,|וְלִבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֖ד\rb* \rb who had|הָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb large|עָצ֣וּם\rb* \rb herds and flocks,|וּמִקְנֶ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |רַ֗ב\rb* \rb surveyed|וַיִּרְא֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lands|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Jazer|יַעְזֵר֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb and Gilead,|גִּלְעָ֔ד\rb* \rb and they saw|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb that the region|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb was suitable|מְק֥וֹם\rb* \rb for livestock.|מִקְנֶֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb So the Gadites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |גָ֖ד\rb* \rb and Reubenites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֑ן\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the leaders|נְשִׂיאֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the congregation,|הָעֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and said,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 3 \rb “Ataroth,|עֲטָר֤וֹת\rb* \rb Dibon,|וְדִיבֹן֙\rb* \rb Jazer,|וְיַעְזֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Nimrah,|וְנִמְרָ֔ה\rb* \rb Heshbon,|וְחֶשְׁבּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb Elealeh,|וְאֶלְעָלֵ֑ה\rb* \rb Sebam,|וּשְׂבָ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 32:3 \ft Hebrew; see verse 38, and similarly in SP and LXX \fqa Sibmah\f* \rb Nebo,|וּנְב֖וֹ\rb* \rb and Beon,|וּבְעֹֽן׃\rb* \v 4 \rb |הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb conquered|הִכָּ֤ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the congregation|עֲדַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb are suitable|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb for livestock—|מִקְנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |הִ֑וא\rb*  \rb and your servants|וְלַֽעֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb have livestock.”|מִקְנֶֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb we have found|מָצָ֤אנוּ\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in your sight,”|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb they said,|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “let this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb be given|יֻתַּ֞ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to your servants|לַעֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb as a possession.|לַאֲחֻזָּ֑ה\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb make us cross|תַּעֲבִרֵ֖נוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan.”|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb But Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the Gadites|לִבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֖ד\rb* \rb and Reubenites,|וְלִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֑ן\rb* \rb “Shall your brothers|הַאַֽחֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb go|יָבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb while you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb sit|תֵּ֥שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb here?|פֹֽה׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Why|וְלָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb are you discouraging|תְנוּאוּן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לֵ֖ב\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb from crossing|מֵֽעֲבֹר֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb them?|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 8 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb did|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb when I sent|בְּשָׁלְחִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb them|מִקָּדֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb from Kadesh-barnea|בַּרְנֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb to inspect|לִרְא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
