\p \v 14 \rb Now behold,|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb you, a brood|תַּרְבּ֖וּת\rb* \rb of sinners,|חַטָּאִ֑ים\rb* \rb have risen up|קַמְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb in place|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to further|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb stoke|לִסְפּ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |עַ֛ל\rb* \rb the burning|חֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb anger|אַף־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 15 \rb For if|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you turn away|תְשׁוּבֻן֙\rb* \rb from following Him,|מֵֽאַחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb He will once again|וְיָסַ֣ף\rb*\rb |ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb leave|לְהַנִּיח֖וֹ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb in the wilderness,|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb and you will be the cause of their destruction.”|וְשִֽׁחַתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְכָל־\rb*
