\p \v 20 \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb “If|אִֽם־\rb* \rb you will do|תַּעֲשׂ֖וּן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb this—|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you will arm yourselves|תֵּחָֽלְצ֛וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb for battle,|לַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb* \v 21 \rb and if every one|כָּל־\rb* \rb of your armed men|חָל֛וּץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb crosses|וְעָבַ֨ר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb until|עַ֧ד\rb* \rb He has driven|הוֹרִישׁ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His enemies|אֹיְבָ֖יו\rb* \rb out before Him,|מִפָּנָֽיו׃\rb* \v 22 \rb then when the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb is subdued|וְנִכְבְּשָׁ֨ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb you may return|תָּשֻׁ֔בוּ\rb* \rb and be|וִהְיִיתֶ֧ם\rb* \rb free|נְקִיִּ֛ים\rb* \rb of obligation to the LORD|מֵיְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and to Israel.|וּמִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb And this|הַזֹּ֥את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb will belong|וְ֠הָיְתָה\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb as a possession|לַאֲחֻזָּ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 23 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשׂוּן֙\rb* \rb this,|כֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb you will certainly|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb sin|חֲטָאתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb against the LORD—|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*  \rb and be assured that|וּדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb your sin|חַטַּאתְכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb will find you out.|תִּמְצָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb Build|בְּנֽוּ־\rb* \rb cities|עָרִים֙\rb* \rb for your|לָכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb little ones|לְטַפְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and folds|וּגְדֵרֹ֖ת\rb* \rb for your flocks,|לְצֹנַאֲכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb but do|תַּעֲשֽׂוּ׃\rb* \rb what you have promised.”|וְהַיֹּצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |מִפִּיכֶ֖ם\rb*
