\p \v 28 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb gave orders|וַיְצַ֤ו\rb* \rb about them|לָהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb to Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb to Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun,|נ֑וּן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and to the family|אֲב֥וֹת\rb* \rb leaders|רָאשֵׁ֛י\rb* \rb of the tribes|הַמַּטּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 29 \rb And Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb the Gadites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֣ד\rb* \rb and Reubenites|וּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֣ן׀\rb* \rb cross|יַעַבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb with you,|אִ֠תְּכֶם\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb with every|כָּל־\rb* \rb man armed|חָל֤וּץ\rb* \rb for battle|לַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb is subdued|וְנִכְבְּשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb before you,|לִפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb then you are to give|וּנְתַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֖ד\rb* \rb as a possession.|לַאֲחֻזָּֽה׃\rb* \v 30 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb they do not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb arm themselves|חֲלוּצִ֖ים\rb* \rb and go across|יַֽעַבְר֛וּ\rb* \rb with you,|אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb then they must accept their possession|וְנֹֽאחֲז֥וּ\rb* \rb among you|בְתֹכְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan.”|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb The Gadites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֛ד\rb* \rb and Reubenites|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb replied,|וַיַּֽעֲנ֧וּ\rb* \rb “As|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your servants,|עֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb so|כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb we will do.|נַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \v 32 \rb We|נַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb will cross over|נַעֲבֹ֧ר\rb* \rb into the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb* \rb armed|חֲלוּצִ֛ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb that|וְאִתָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb we may have our inheritance|נַחֲלָתֵ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |אֲחֻזַּ֣ת\rb* \rb on this side|מֵעֵ֖בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan.”|לַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֡ה\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb to|לָהֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb the Gadites,|לִבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָד֩\rb* \rb to the Reubenites,|וְלִבְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵ֜ן\rb* \rb and to the half-tribe|וְלַחֲצִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣בֶט׀\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֗ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַמְלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb of Sihon|סִיחֹן֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָֽאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the kingdom|מַמְלֶ֔כֶת\rb* \rb of Og|ע֖וֹג\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Bashan—|הַבָּשָׁ֑ן\rb*  \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb including its cities|לְעָרֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and the territory|בִּגְבֻלֹ֔ת\rb* \rb surrounding|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb them.|עָרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb And the Gadites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |גָ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb built up|וַיִּבְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb Dibon,|דִּיבֹ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ataroth,|עֲטָרֹ֑ת\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb Aroer,|עֲרֹעֵֽר׃\rb* \v 35 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |עַטְרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb Atroth-shophan,|שׁוֹפָ֛ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Jazer,|יַעְזֵ֖ר\rb* \rb Jogbehah,|וְיָגְבֳּהָֽה׃\rb* \v 36 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Beth-nimrah,|נִמְרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and Beth-haran|הָרָ֑ן\rb* \rb as fortified|מִבְצָ֖ר\rb* \rb cities,|עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb and they built folds|וְגִדְרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb for their flocks.|צֹֽאן׃\rb*
\p \v 37 \rb The Reubenites|וּבְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵן֙\rb* \rb built up|בָּנ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Heshbon,|חֶשְׁבּ֖וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Elealeh,|אֶלְעָלֵ֑א\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb Kiriathaim,|קִרְיָתָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 38 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb as well as Nebo|נְב֞וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בַּ֧עַל\rb* \rb and Baal-meon|מְע֛וֹן\rb* \rb (whose names|שֵׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb were changed),|מֽוּסַבֹּ֥ת\rb* \rb and Sibmah.|שִׂבְמָ֑ה\rb* \rb And they renamed|וַיִּקְרְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |בְשֵׁמֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb the cities|הֶעָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they rebuilt.|בָּנֽוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb The descendants|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Machir|מָכִ֧יר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֨לְכ֜וּ\rb* \rb to Gilead,|גִּלְעָ֖דָה\rb* \rb captured it,|וַֽיִּלְכְּדֻ֑הָ\rb* \rb and drove out|וַיּ֖וֹרֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֥י\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb there.|בָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 40 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֔ד\rb* \rb to the clan of Machir|לְמָכִ֖יר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Manasseh,|מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb and they settled|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb there.|בָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 41 \rb Jair,|וְיָאִ֤יר\rb* \rb a descendant|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Manasseh,|מְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb went|הָלַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their villages|חַוֺּתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and called|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶתְהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb them|חַוֺּ֥ת\rb* \rb Havvoth-jair.|יָאִֽיר׃\rb*\f + \fr 32:41 \fqa Havvoth-jair \ft means \fqa the villages of Jair\ft .\f* \v 42 \rb And Nobah|וְנֹ֣בַח\rb* \rb went|הָלַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Kenath|קְנָ֖ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and its villages|בְּנֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb and called|וַיִּקְרָ֧א\rb* \rb it|לָ֦ה\rb* \rb Nobah,|נֹ֖בַח\rb* \rb after his own name.|בִּשְׁמֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\c 33
\s1 Forty-Two Journeys of the Israelites
\p \v 1 \rb These|אֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb are the journeys|מַסְעֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they came out|יָצְא֛וּ\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb by their divisions|לְצִבְאֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb under the leadership|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb and Aaron.|וְאַהֲרֹֽן׃\rb* \v 2 \rb At|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb command,|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb recorded|וַיִּכְתֹּ֨ב\rb* \rb the stages|מוֹצָאֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb of their journey.|לְמַסְעֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb These|וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb are the stages|מַסְעֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb listed by their starting points:|לְמוֹצָאֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\li1 \v 3 \rb On the fifteenth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֛ר\rb* \rb day|י֖וֹם\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the first|הָֽרִאשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb on|הָרִאשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb the day after|מִֽמָּחֳרַ֣ת\rb* \rb the Passover,|הַפֶּ֗סַח\rb* \rb the Israelites set out|וַיִּסְע֤וּ\rb* \rb from Rameses.|מֵֽרַעְמְסֵס֙\rb* \rb They|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb marched out|יָצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb defiantly|בְּיָ֣ד\rb*\f + \fr 33:3 \ft Or \fqa marched out boldly\ft ; literally \fqa marched out with an upraised hand\f* \rb |רָמָ֔ה\rb*\rb in full view|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Egyptians,|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 4 \rb who|וּמִצְרַ֣יִם\rb* \rb were burying|מְקַבְּרִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their firstborn,|בְּכ֑וֹר\rb* \rb whom the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had struck down|הִכָּ֧ה\rb* \rb among them;|בָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had executed|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb judgment|שְׁפָטִֽים׃\rb* \rb against their gods.|וּבֵאלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \v 5 \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb set out|וַיִּסְע֥וּ\rb* \rb from Rameses|מֵרַעְמְסֵ֑ס\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb at Succoth.|בְּסֻכֹּֽת׃\rb*
\li1 \v 6 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from Succoth|מִסֻּכֹּ֑ת\rb* \rb and camped|וַיַּחֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb at Etham,|בְאֵתָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on the edge|בִּקְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the wilderness.|הַמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*
\li1 \v 7 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb from Etham|מֵֽאֵתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and turned back|וַיָּ֙שָׁב֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb*\rb |פִּ֣י\rb* \rb Pi-hahiroth,|הַחִירֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb opposite|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb Baal-zephon,|צְפ֑וֹן\rb* \rb and they camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb near|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Migdol.|מִגְדֹּֽל׃\rb*
\li1 \v 8 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Pi-hahiroth|הַֽחִירֹ֔ת\rb*\f + \fr 33:8 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts, SP, and Vulgate; see verse 7; most MT manuscripts \fqa Hahiroth\f* \rb and crossed|וַיַּֽעַבְר֥וּ\rb* \rb through|בְתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the sea,|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb into the wilderness,|הַמִּדְבָּ֑רָה\rb* \rb and they journeyed three days|שְׁלֹ֤שֶׁת\rb*\rb |יָמִים֙\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֨לְכ֜וּ\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb into the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Etham|אֵתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb at Marah.|בְּמָרָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 9 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְעוּ֙\rb* \rb from Marah|מִמָּרָ֔ה\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Elim,|אֵילִ֑מָה\rb*\rb |וּ֠בְאֵילִם\rb* \rb where there were twelve|שְׁתֵּ֣ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֞ה\rb* \rb springs|עֵינֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |מַ֛יִם\rb* \rb and seventy|וְשִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb palm trees,|תְּמָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and they camped|וַיַּחֲנוּ־\rb* \rb there.|שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\li1 \v 10 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from Elim|מֵאֵילִ֑ם\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the Red|סֽוּף׃\rb* \rb Sea.|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 33:10 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\ft ; also in verse 11\f*
\li1 \v 11 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from the Red|ס֑וּף\rb* \rb Sea|מִיַּם־\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in the Desert|בְּמִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Sin.|סִֽין׃\rb*\f + \fr 33:11 \ft The geographical name \fqa Sin \ft is related to \fqa Sinai \ft and should not be mistaken for the English word \fqa sin\ft ; also in verse 12.\f*
\li1 \v 12 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from the Desert|מִמִּדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Sin|סִ֑ין\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb at Dophkah.|בְּדָפְקָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 13 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from Dophkah|מִדָּפְקָ֑ה\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb at Alush.|בְּאָלֽוּשׁ׃\rb*
\li1 \v 14 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from Alush|מֵאָל֑וּשׁ\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb at Rephidim,|בִּרְפִידִ֔ם\rb* \rb where|שָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb there was|הָ֨יָה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb water|מַ֛יִם\rb* \rb for the people|לָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb to drink.|לִשְׁתּֽוֹת׃\rb*
\li1 \v 15 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from Rephidim|מֵרְפִידִ֑ם\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of Sinai.|סִינָֽי׃\rb*
\li1 \v 16 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from the Wilderness|מִמִּדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Sinai|סִינָ֑י\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb*\rb |בְּקִבְרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb at Kibroth-hattaavah.|הַֽתַּאֲוָֽה׃\rb*
\li1 \v 17 \rb They set out|וַיִּסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִקִּבְרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb Kibroth-hattaavah|הַֽתַּאֲוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb at Hazeroth.|בַּחֲצֵרֹֽת׃\rb*
